290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Resource Type IDs
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// =================
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Note: We are using the String version of these IDs. These special strings
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>//       are interpreted as resource type integer id's in all Win32 functions
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>//       that accept a resource type ID as a parameter. Below is from Win32 API Help...
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// lpType specifies the integer identifier of the type of the given resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Otherwise, the parameter is a long pointer to a null-terminated string.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// If the first character of the String is a pound sign (#), the remaining
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// characters represent a Decimal Number that specifies the Integer identifier
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// of the resource's type. For example, the string "#1" represents the integer type 1
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_CURSOR       for '#1'     // Hardware-dependent cursor resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_BITMAP       for '#2'     // Bitmap resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_ICON         for '#3'     // Hardware-dependent icon resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_MENU         for '#4'     // Menu resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_DIALOG       for '#5'     // Dialog box.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_ACCELERATOR  for '#9'     // Accelerator table.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_STRING       for '#6'     // String-table entry.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_FONTDIR      for '#7'     // Font directory resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_FONT         for '#8'     // Font resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_RCDATA       for '#10'    // Application-defined resource (raw data).
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_MESSAGETABLE for '#11'    // Message-table entry.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_GROUP_CURSOR for '#12'    // Hardware-independent cursor resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_GROUP_ICON   for '#14'    // Hardware-independent icon resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_VERSION      for '#16'    // Version resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_DLGINCLUDE   for '#17'    // Allows a resource editing tool to associate a String with an .rc file. Typically, the String is the name of the header file that provides symbolic names. The resource compiler parses the String but otherwise ignores the value.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_PLUGPLAY     for '#19'    // Plug and Play resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_VXD          for '#20'    // VXD.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_ANICURSOR    for '#21'    // Animated cursor.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_ANIICON      for '#22'    // Animated icon.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_HTML         for '#23'    // HTML resource.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Define RT_MANIFEST     for '#24'    // Side-by-Side Assembly Manifest.
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
290>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>External_Function CopyMemory "RtlMoveMemory" Kernel32.dll ;    Pointer psDest Pointer psSource Longptr cChars Returns VOID_TYPE        // cChars is number of bytes
291>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
291>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// When called directly: lpFilename must be pointer of a WString.
291>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>External_Function DeleteFileW "DeleteFileW" Kernel32.Dll ;   Pointer lpFileName ;   Returns Integer
292>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
292>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Wrapper Function DeleteFile
292>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Function DeleteFile Global ;   Pointer lpFileName ;   Returns Integer
294>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
294>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Integer iResult
294>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    UWide   uwFileName
294>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    UWide   uwFileName
294>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
294>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Send StringToWide lpFileName (&uwFileName)
295>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    
295>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Move (DeleteFileW (uwFileName.lpUText)) to iResult
296>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>          
296>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function_Return iResult
297>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>End_Function
298>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
298>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Do not call directly, use the wrapper function instead
298>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>External_Function FormatMessageW "FormatMessageW" KERNEL32.DLL ;    DWord   dwFlags ;    Pointer lpSource ;    DWord   dwMessageId ;    DWord   dwLanguageId ;    Pointer lpwBuffer ;    DWord   nSize ;    Pointer Arguments ;    Returns DWord
299>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
299>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Compatibility Wrapper Function FormatMessage
299>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Function FormatMessage Global ;    DWord   dwFlags ;    Pointer lpSource ;    DWord   dwMessageId ;    DWord   dwLanguageId ;    Pointer lpBuffer ;    DWord   nSize ;    Pointer Arguments ;    Returns DWord
301>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
301>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    DWord dwResult
301>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    UWide uwBuffer
301>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    UWide uwBuffer
301>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
