446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file or directory is an archive file or directory.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// Applications use this attribute to mark files for backup or removal.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faArchive              for |CI$00000020
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file or directory is compressed.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// For a file, this means that all of the data in the file is compressed.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// For a directory, this means that compression is the default for newly created files and subdirectories.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faCompressed           for |CI$00000800
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The handle identifies a directory.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faDirectory            for |CI$00000010
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file or directory is encrypted.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// For a file, this means that all data in the file is encrypted.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// For a directory, this means that encryption is the default for newly created files and subdirectories.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faEncrypted            for |CI$00000040
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file or directory is hidden.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// It is not included in an ordinary directory listing.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faHidden               for |CI$00000002
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file or directory has no other attributes set.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// This attribute is valid only if used alone.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faNormal               for |CI$00000080
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file data is not immediately available.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// This attribute indicates that the file data has been physically moved to offline storage.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// This attribute is used by Remote Storage, the hierarchical storage management software in Windows 2000.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// Applications should not arbitrarily change this attribute.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faOffline              for |CI$00001000
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file or directory is read-only.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// Applications can read the file but cannot write to it or delete it.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// In the case of a directory, applications cannot delete it.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faReadOnly             for |CI$00000001
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file has an associated reparse point.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faReparsePoint         for |CI$00000400
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file is a sparse file.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faSparseFile          for |CI$00000200
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file or directory is part of the operating system,
446>>>>>>>>>>>// or is used exclusively by the operating system.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faSystem              for |CI$00000004
446>>>>>>>>>>>
446>>>>>>>>>>>// The file is being used for temporary storage.
446>>>>>>>>>>>// File systems attempt to keep all of the data in memory for quicker access, rather than flushing it back to mass storage. A temporary file should be deleted by the application as soon as it is no longer needed.
446>>>>>>>>>>>Define faTemporary           for |CI$00000100
