1117>>>>>>>>>// Returns True if the sPath is a directory.
1117>>>>>>>>>Function IsDirectory Global String sPath Returns Boolean
1119>>>>>>>>>    Integer iAttributes
1119>>>>>>>>>    Move (GetFileAttributes(sPath)) to iAttributes
1120>>>>>>>>>    If (iAttributes <> INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES) Begin
1122>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return  (IsFlagIn(FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DIRECTORY, iAttributes))
1123>>>>>>>>>    End
1123>>>>>>>>>>
1123>>>>>>>>>    Function_Return False // File is not a directory (or doesn't exist)
1124>>>>>>>>>End_Function
1125>>>>>>>>>
1125>>>>>>>>>//  Convert a short name or qualified name with relative references to a long name.
1125>>>>>>>>>//  Relative path is converted with respect to the current working directory. 
1125>>>>>>>>>//  (see Get_Current_Directory and SetCurrentDirectory).
1125>>>>>>>>>//
1125>>>>>>>>>//  This works even if the directories don't exist - this does more a syntatical check
1125>>>>>>>>>//  e.g.  c:\MyApp\..\MyApp\appsrc ----> c:\MyApp\appsrc
1125>>>>>>>>>//                   \MyApp\appsrc ----> c:\MyApp\appsrc  
1125>>>>>>>>>//
1125>>>>>>>>>Function FullPathName Global String sRelPathName Returns String
1127>>>>>>>>>    WString sFullPathName
1127>>>>>>>>>    Pointer lpsFilePart
1127>>>>>>>>>    Integer icChar // the number of characters returned
1127>>>>>>>>>    
1127>>>>>>>>>    Move (Repeat(character(0), 4096)) to sFullPathName
1128>>>>>>>>>    Move -1 to lpsFilePart
1129>>>>>>>>>    Move (GetFullPathNameW(sRelPathName, 4096, AddressOf(sFullPathName), AddressOf(lpsFilePart))) to icChar
1130>>>>>>>>>    
