1484>>>>>>>>>//   The Data_Set class is implemented as a subclass of Entry_Client, with
1484>>>>>>>>>//   a C language handler providing the majority of new behavior.  The
1484>>>>>>>>>//   Data_Set class is intended to be a grouping agent for data-entry objects
1484>>>>>>>>>//   and a container for subordinate Data_Sets.
1484>>>>>>>>>//
1484>>>>>>>>>Use BaseData_Set.pkg
1484>>>>>>>>>
1484>>>>>>>>>// Data_Set class definition, public class layer. (Extra class layer needed
1484>>>>>>>>>// to augment C-based (Constrain) procedure(s).)
1484>>>>>>>>>
1484>>>>>>>>>Class DataSet is a BaseData_Set
1485>>>>>>>>>    
1485>>>>>>>>>    
1485>>>>>>>>>    // maintain old name for the time being to maximize compatability
1485>>>>>>>>>    // between character mode and windows versions. Developers should be
1485>>>>>>>>>    // able to move DS classes back and forth without changes.
1485>>>>>>>>>    Replace_Class_Name Data_Set DataSet
1485>>>>>>>>>    
1485>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object //Integer Img#
1487>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object No_Image //Img#
1489>>>>>>>>>        
1489>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Constrain_File 0
1490>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Auto_Fill_State False
1491>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Change_Disabled_State  False
1492>>>>>>>>>        // RT sets this inside of Mark_components a part of old entry_client DSO behavior. Now it is never used
1492>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Component_State False
1493>>>>>>>>>        
1493>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
1494>>>>>>>>>    
1494>>>>>>>>>    
1494>>>>>>>>>    //
1494>>>>>>>>>    // This may be called by legacy DSO and DDO code
1494>>>>>>>>>    //
1494>>>>>>>>>    // IMPORTANT NOTE of change for 8.2:
1494>>>>>>>>>    //         DO NOT call or augment this anymore.
1494>>>>>>>>>    //
1494>>>>>>>>>    //         for sending: Find all cases of Field_main_index and change it to File_Field_Index
1494>>>>>>>>>    //
1494>>>>>>>>>    //         for augmenting: In DSOs - replace Field_main_index with File_field_index
1494>>>>>>>>>    //                         In DDOs - replace Field_main_Index with Field_Index and do not pass
1494>>>>>>>>>    //                                   the file parameter.
1494>>>>>>>>>    //                                   See DDOs Field_index and File_field_Index for more
1494>>>>>>>>>    //
1494>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Main_Index Integer file Integer Field Returns Integer
1496>>>>>>>>>        Integer dataType fldNdx retval ordr
1496>>>>>>>>>        Move -1 to retval      //field has no main index (default)
1497>>>>>>>>>        If (file <> 0) Begin
1499>>>>>>>>>//      FIELD_DEF file field to dataType fldNdx
1499>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_INDEX of file Field to fldNdx // main index field
1502>>>>>>>>>            If (fldNdx > 0 or Field = 0) ;                Move fldNdx to retval //field has main index
1505>>>>>>>>>        End
1505>>>>>>>>>>
1505>>>>>>>>>        If (file = main_file(Self)) Begin
1507>>>>>>>>>            Get ordering to ordr
1508>>>>>>>>>            If (ordr >= 0) ;                Move ordr to retval  //ordering takes precedence over main index
1511>>>>>>>>>        End
1511>>>>>>>>>>
1511>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return retval
1512>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
1513>>>>>>>>>    
1513>>>>>>>>>    // This allows packages that still use data-sets instead of DDOs to use this
1513>>>>>>>>>    // message syntax.
1513>>>>>>>>>    // Note that this will never get here if the DD class is used as
1513>>>>>>>>>    // it has its own handler for this. It only is called if DSOs are used in which
1513>>>>>>>>>    // case it calls the old message field_main_index above.
1513>>>>>>>>>    // DDO based objects will NEVER call this code
1513>>>>>>>>>    //
1513>>>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Index Integer iFile Integer iField Returns Integer
1515>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Field_main_Index(Self,iFile,iField))
1516>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
1517>>>>>>>>>    
1517>>>>>>>>>    
1517>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Item_Find Integer eFindMode ;            Integer iFile Integer iField ;            Integer bDoEntryUpdate Integer bShowFindErr Integer bDeferred
1519>>>>>>>>>        
1519>>>>>>>>>        RowID   riRow
1519>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
1519>>>>>>>>>        Handle  hoServer
1519>>>>>>>>>        Integer iSegments iSeg iSegFld iSegFldMainIndex
1519>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bChanged bDoCheck bOk
1519>>>>>>>>>        
1519>>>>>>>>>        //Get Field_Main_Index iFile iField to iIndex
1519>>>>>>>>>        Get File_Field_Index iFile iField to iIndex
1520>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex<>-1) Begin
1522>>>>>>>>>            // get prior rowId before it get cleared
1522>>>>>>>>>            Move (GetRowID(iFile)) to riRow
1523>>>>>>>>>            //  'hold' buffer to prepare for entry_update
1523>>>>>>>>>            Set_Attribute DF_FILE_STATUS of iFile to DF_FILE_INACTIVE
1526>>>>>>>>>            If bDoEntryUpdate Begin
1528>>>>>>>>>                Send Request_Entry_Update iFile 1  //entUpdt all DEOs as required
1529>>>>>>>>>                
1529>>>>>>>>>                // If the buffer is cleared (no record and no changed data) then we want
1529>>>>>>>>>                // to do a constrained_clear which will force the buffer to get cleared
1529>>>>>>>>>                // according to the rules of the current constraints.
1529>>>>>>>>>                //Get_field_value iFile 0 to iRec
1529>>>>>>>>>                //Move (GetRowID(iFile)) to riRow // 12.1 moved above the set file inactive
1529>>>>>>>>>                
1529>>>>>>>>>                // If there was an active record to begin with we consider this changed (not cleared)
1529>>>>>>>>>                If (not(IsNullRowId(riRow))) Begin
1531>>>>>>>>>                    Move True to bChanged
1532>>>>>>>>>                End
1532>>>>>>>>>>
1532>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
1533>>>>>>>>>                    // or, if the record was already changed or the entry_update created a change
1533>>>>>>>>>                    // we consider this changed
1533>>>>>>>>>                    Get_Attribute DF_FILE_CHANGED of iFile to bChanged
1536>>>>>>>>>                End
1536>>>>>>>>>>
1536>>>>>>>>>                
1536>>>>>>>>>                If not bChanged Begin
1538>>>>>>>>>                    // if buffer is unchanged, do a constrained clear. It is unchanged if there was not
1538>>>>>>>>>                    // active record, the record was unchanged, and the update didn't change anything.
1538>>>>>>>>>                    Constrained_Clear eFindMode iFile by iIndex
1541>>>>>>>>>                End
1541>>>>>>>>>>
1541>>>>>>>>>                Else If (eFindMode=GE or eFindMode=LE and iIndex>0) Begin
1544>>>>>>>>>                    
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // If mode is GE or LE we need to do some extra processing. We want to clear
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // all index segemnt fields that occur after this field in the index. This way
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // dbList searches and find ge searches (f9) will always find the first record
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // that matches the data in the field being searched. This was if an index like
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // customer.name x customer.number where you had 10 identical names "john" typing
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // john will find the first record, because customer.number will get cleared.
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // Note we can no do this with GT or LT or you'd get stuck in fields
1544>>>>>>>>>                    
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // check all fields for index. Once you find the iField field, clear all
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // fields that follow it. Only do this if the other fields do not use the
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // same index as its primary index (in which case we assume the data is intentional).
1544>>>>>>>>>                    // This should handle most cases.
1544>>>>>>>>>                    Get_Attribute DF_INDEX_NUMBER_SEGMENTS of iFile iIndex to iSegments
1547>>>>>>>>>                    For iSeg from 1 to iSegments
1553>>>>>>>>>>
1553>>>>>>>>>                        Get_Attribute DF_INDEX_SEGMENT_FIELD of iFile iIndex iSeg to iSegFld
1556>>>>>>>>>                        If not bDoCheck Begin
1558>>>>>>>>>                            If (iSegFld=iField) ;                                Move True to bDoCheck // marked after we find the find field in the index
1561>>>>>>>>>                        End
1561>>>>>>>>>>
1561>>>>>>>>>                        Else Begin // we get here after we've found the main field segment
1562>>>>>>>>>                            // if main index if this segment is same as our find index, do nothing
1562>>>>>>>>>                            Get File_Field_Index iFile iSegFld to iSegFldMainIndex
1563>>>>>>>>>                            If (iSegFldMainIndex<>iIndex) ;                                Set_Field_Value iFile iSegFld to ''
1568>>>>>>>>>                        End
1568>>>>>>>>>>
1568>>>>>>>>>                    Loop
1569>>>>>>>>>>
1569>>>>>>>>>                End
1569>>>>>>>>>>
1569>>>>>>>>>                
1569>>>>>>>>>                Get Which_Data_Set iFile to hoServer
1570>>>>>>>>>                If (hoServer and iFile=main_file(hoServer)) ;                    Send Attach_Main_File to hoServer
1573>>>>>>>>>                Else ;                    Attach iFile
1575>>>>>>>>>            End
1575>>>>>>>>>>
1575>>>>>>>>>            
1575>>>>>>>>>            Move False to Err
1576>>>>>>>>>            
1576>>>>>>>>>            If (Is_SuperFind_Required(Self,iFile)) ;                Send Request_SuperFind eFindMode iFile iField
1579>>>>>>>>>            Else If bDeferred ;                Send Request_Read eFindMode iFile iIndex
1583>>>>>>>>>            Else ;                Send Request_Find eFindMode iFile iIndex
1585>>>>>>>>>            
1585>>>>>>>>>            If (not(Found) and not(err)) Begin
1587>>>>>>>>>                // refind original record (or leave it cleared if not record)
1587>>>>>>>>>                Move (FindByRowId(iFile,riRow)) to bOk
1588>>>>>>>>>                
1588>>>>>>>>>                If bShowFindErr ;                    Error (If(eFindMode<2, DFERR_FIND_PRIOR_BEG_OF_FILE, DFERR_FIND_PAST_END_OF_FILE))
1591>>>>>>>>>                Move False to Found
1592>>>>>>>>>            End
1592>>>>>>>>>>
1592>>>>>>>>>        End
1592>>>>>>>>>>
1592>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            If bShowFindErr ;                Error DFERR_FIELD_NOT_INDEXED
1596>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
1597>>>>>>>>>    
1597>>>>>>>>>    
1597>>>>>>>>>    // We only care about should_saves of DEOs and not DSOs when
1597>>>>>>>>>    // exiting the app. Create a handler for data set class. We still
1597>>>>>>>>>    // broadcast in case we've got nested deos in the dso (hopefully not).
1597>>>>>>>>>    //
1597>>>>>>>>>    Function Exit_Application_Check Returns Integer
1599>>>>>>>>>        Integer rVal
1599>>>>>>>>>        Broadcast Get Exit_Application_Check to Rval // check w/ kids
1601>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return rVal
1602>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
