2089>>>>>>>>>// This is used by the DataDictionary class and provides a method for
2089>>>>>>>>>// windows DDs (for now) to support local buffers for text and binary buffers.
2089>>>>>>>>>// Field objects are created within the DD by sending the message:
2089>>>>>>>>>// The DD interface is:
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get  Field_Object iField to hExtFieldObject
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Send DefineExtendedField iField
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Send DefineAllExtendedFields
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Send ExtendedFieldsUpdate bSave
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Send ExtendedFieldsRefresh bCleared
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set  File_Field_Current_Pointer_Value iFile iField iLen to pValue
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_Current_Pointer_Value iField iLen to pValue
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set  File_Field_Pointer_Entry iFile iField iLen bShowErr to pValue
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_Pointer_Entry iField iOpts iLen bShowErr to pValue
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get  File_Field_Current_Pointer_Value iFile iField to pData
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get  Field_Current_Pointer_Value iField to pData
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>// Once object is identified, the following interface can be used
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldPointer of hExtFieldObject to iMemoryPointer
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldLength  of hExtFieldObject to iLen
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get File_Number  of hExtFieldObject to iFile
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get Field_Number of hExtFieldObject to iFile
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set Update_Save_State of hExtFieldObject to bState         // be careful!
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set Update_Find_State of hExtFieldObject to bState         // be careful
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set FieldRefresh_Save_State of hExtFieldObject to bState   // be careful
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>//  DD structure:
2089>>>>>>>>>//       DD Object           (property Field_objects points to child)
2089>>>>>>>>>//           FieldObjects    (array of field#s and field objs)
2089>>>>>>>>>//              FieldObject1 (heap alloc for each field)
2089>>>>>>>>>//              FieldObjectn
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>// This is used to create a single extended field object.
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>// Interface
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldPointer to iMemoryPointer
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldLength  to iLen
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get File_Number  to iFile
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Get Field_Number to iFile
2089>>>>>>>>>//      get/Set Update_Save_State to bState         // be careful!
2089>>>>>>>>>//      get/Set Update_Find_State to bState         // be careful
2089>>>>>>>>>//      get/Set FieldRefresh_Save_State to bState   // be careful
2089>>>>>>>>>//      get/set FieldChangedState
2089>>>>>>>>>//      send defineField  iFile iField
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Send FieldUpdate  bSave
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Send FieldRefresh bCleared bClearFieldChange
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_pEntry iOpts iLen to pValue
2089>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_pValue iLen to pValue
2089>>>>>>>>>//
2089>>>>>>>>>Use VDFBase.pkg
2089>>>>>>>>>
2089>>>>>>>>>Class FieldObject is a cObject
2090>>>>>>>>>    
2090>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
2092>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send construct_object
2094>>>>>>>>>        // these are all set by DefineField and should not be changed
2094>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer File_Number        0
2095>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Field_Number       0
2096>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer FieldLength        0
2097>>>>>>>>>        
2097>>>>>>>>>        // maintained by object
2097>>>>>>>>>        Property UChar[] pFieldArray
2098>>>>>>>>>        
2098>>>>>>>>>        // these can be changed, with care, by the developer
2098>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Update_Save_State  True
2099>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Update_Find_State  False // usually no point for finds
2100>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer FieldRefresh_State True
2101>>>>>>>>>        
2101>>>>>>>>>        // hopefully never used
2101>>>>>>>>>        Property Pointer pLegacyFieldPointer       0
2102>>>>>>>>>        
2102>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2103>>>>>>>>>    
2103>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set FieldChangedState Integer bState
2105>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField
2105>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
2106>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Field_Changed_state iField to bState
2108>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2109>>>>>>>>>    
2109>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldChangedState Returns Integer
2111>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField  bState
2111>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
2112>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Changed_state iField to bState
2114>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bState
2115>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2116>>>>>>>>>    
2116>>>>>>>>>    // return the field option specified
2116>>>>>>>>>    Function IsSaveNoPut Returns Boolean
2118>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField
2118>>>>>>>>>        Boolean  bState
2118>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
2119>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get FieldSaveNoPut iField to bState
2121>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bState
2122>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2123>>>>>>>>>    
2123>>>>>>>>>    // for object: define file, field, fieldlength and allocate heap memory
2123>>>>>>>>>    //             and set memory pointer
2123>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DefineField Integer iFile Integer iField
2125>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFldLen
2125>>>>>>>>>        Set File_Number  to iFile
2126>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_Number to iField
2127>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_LENGTH of iFile iField to iFldLen
2130>>>>>>>>>        Set FieldLength  to iFldLen
2131>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2132>>>>>>>>>    
2132>>>>>>>>>    // Move from the DD Buffer to the file buffer
2132>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FieldUpdate Integer bSave
2134>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iField iFieldLen
2134>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2135>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2135>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bNoPut
2135>>>>>>>>>        
2135>>>>>>>>>        // if bSave, part of save which means only update if changed
2135>>>>>>>>>        // if not bsave, part of find. You usually would not update this. You
2135>>>>>>>>>        // don't index on these types of fields
2135>>>>>>>>>        If ( (bSave and Update_Save_State(Self) and FieldChangedState(Self)) or ;            (not(bSave) and Update_Find_state(Self) ) ) Begin
2137>>>>>>>>>            // if save, we must respect DD_NoPut
2137>>>>>>>>>            If (bSave) Begin
2139>>>>>>>>>                // we are looking at the DD's field buffer itemoptions for, which
2139>>>>>>>>>                // should be set appropriately before a save. This setting has any
2139>>>>>>>>>                // changes made to support dd_commit
2139>>>>>>>>>                Get IsSaveNoPut to bNoPut
2140>>>>>>>>>                If bNoPut Begin
2142>>>>>>>>>                    Procedure_Return
2143>>>>>>>>>                End
2143>>>>>>>>>>
2143>>>>>>>>>            End
2143>>>>>>>>>>
2143>>>>>>>>>            Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
2144>>>>>>>>>            Get File_Number to iFile
2145>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Number to iField
2146>>>>>>>>>            If iFile Begin
2148>>>>>>>>>                Set_Field_Value iFile iField to FieldArray // LENGTH iFieldLen
2151>>>>>>>>>            End
2151>>>>>>>>>>
2151>>>>>>>>>        End
2151>>>>>>>>>>
2151>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2152>>>>>>>>>    
2152>>>>>>>>>    // Move from File buffer to local DD Buffer
2152>>>>>>>>>    // bCleared determines if this is a find or a clear.
2152>>>>>>>>>    // bClearFieldChange determines if we should clear the FieldChangedState.
2152>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FieldRefresh Boolean bCleared Boolean bClearFieldChange
2154>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iField
2154>>>>>>>>>        Integer bOk
2154>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2155>>>>>>>>>        If (FieldRefresh_state(Self)) Begin
2157>>>>>>>>>            //Get FieldPointer to pField
2157>>>>>>>>>            Get File_Number to iFile
2158>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Number to iField
2159>>>>>>>>>            // move from file buffer to memory pointed to by pField
2159>>>>>>>>>            If (iFile) Begin
2161>>>>>>>>>                If not bCleared Begin
2163>>>>>>>>>                    Get_Field_Value iFile iField to FieldArray
2166>>>>>>>>>                End
2166>>>>>>>>>>
2166>>>>>>>>>                Set Field_UCValue to FieldArray
2167>>>>>>>>>            End
2167>>>>>>>>>>
2167>>>>>>>>>        End
2167>>>>>>>>>>
2167>>>>>>>>>        If bClearFieldChange Begin
2169>>>>>>>>>            Set FieldChangedstate to False
2170>>>>>>>>>        End
2170>>>>>>>>>>
2170>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2171>>>>>>>>>    
2171>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_pEntry Integer iOpts Integer iLen Integer bShowErr Pointer pValue
2173>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iField iFldLen iMemLen
2173>>>>>>>>>        Integer bChanged
2173>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2174>>>>>>>>>        
2174>>>>>>>>>        // currently we do nothing with bShowErr because we don't checkfor errors!
2174>>>>>>>>>        
2174>>>>>>>>>        // if No-enter or Displayonly, this shouldn't be changed. For now we will
2174>>>>>>>>>        // let NoPut through, since a user might need it for finding.
2174>>>>>>>>>        If (iOpts iand DD_NOENTER) ;            Procedure_Return
2177>>>>>>>>>        
2177>>>>>>>>>        // maybe in the future
2177>>>>>>>>>        // Force a caplsock if required
2177>>>>>>>>>        //If (iOpts IAND DD_CAPSLOCK) Move (Uppercase(sValue)) to sValue
2177>>>>>>>>>        
2177>>>>>>>>>        Get File_Number  to iFile
2178>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
2179>>>>>>>>>        If (iFile) Begin
2181>>>>>>>>>            Get Is_pValueChanged iLen pValue to bChanged
2182>>>>>>>>>            If ( bChanged or (iOpts iand DD_FORCEPUT) ) Begin
2184>>>>>>>>>                Set Field_pValue iLen to pValue
2185>>>>>>>>>            End
2185>>>>>>>>>>
2185>>>>>>>>>            
2185>>>>>>>>>            
2185>>>>>>>>>            // Set changed state if changed and it is not No_put. This
2185>>>>>>>>>            // is an improvement on DEOs which would set changed-state for
2185>>>>>>>>>            // a no-put. This way, finds use the changed value but saves will
2185>>>>>>>>>            // not trigger a phony data loss
2185>>>>>>>>>            //If ( bChanged ) ;
2185>>>>>>>>>            If ( bChanged and not(iOpts iand DD_NOPUT) ) ;                Set FieldChangedState to True
2188>>>>>>>>>            
2188>>>>>>>>>            // The following is really highly unlikely!!!
2188>>>>>>>>>            // perform autofinds if needed. Note that required checking will occur as
2188>>>>>>>>>            // part of validation.
2188>>>>>>>>>            // We will only autofind if the field value is changed. This is consistent with
2188>>>>>>>>>            // DEOs which do not autofind on unchanged values. This provides optimizations
2188>>>>>>>>>            // when a parent record is already loaded.
2188>>>>>>>>>            If (bChanged or FieldChangedState(Self)) Begin
2190>>>>>>>>>                If (iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND) ;                    Delegate Send File_Field_AutoFind iFile iField EQ
2194>>>>>>>>>                Else If (iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND_GE) ;                    Delegate Send File_Field_AutoFind iFile iField GE
2199>>>>>>>>>            End
2199>>>>>>>>>>
2199>>>>>>>>>        End
2199>>>>>>>>>>
2199>>>>>>>>>        
2199>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2200>>>>>>>>>    
2200>>>>>>>>>    // convert pointer to UChar[]
2200>>>>>>>>>    Function PointerToUCharArray Pointer pValue Integer iLen Returns UChar[]
2202>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2203>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk
2203>>>>>>>>>        Move (ResizeArray(FieldArray,iLen)) to FieldArray
2204>>>>>>>>>        Move (MemCopy(AddressOf(FieldArray),pValue,iLen)) to bOK
2205>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return FieldArray
2206>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2207>>>>>>>>>    
2207>>>>>>>>>    // Raw update of pValue
2207>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_UCValue UChar[] FieldArray
2209>>>>>>>>>        Set pFieldArray to FieldArray
2210>>>>>>>>>        Send DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
2211>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2212>>>>>>>>>    
2212>>>>>>>>>    // Raw update of pValue
2212>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_pValue Integer iLen Pointer pValue
2214>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2215>>>>>>>>>        Get PointerToUCharArray pValue iLen to FieldArray
2216>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_UCValue to FieldArray
2217>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2218>>>>>>>>>    
2218>>>>>>>>>    Function Is_pValueChanged Integer iLen Pointer pValue Returns Boolean
2220>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bChanged
2220>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2221>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFldLen
2221>>>>>>>>>        Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
2222>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(FieldArray)) to iFldLen
2223>>>>>>>>>        If (iLen <> SizeOfArray(FieldArray)) Begin
2225>>>>>>>>>            Move True to bChanged
2226>>>>>>>>>        End
2226>>>>>>>>>>
2226>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iLen) Begin // check for empty pointer
2229>>>>>>>>>            Move (MemCompare(AddressOf(FieldArray),pValue,iLen)) to bChanged
2230>>>>>>>>>        End
2230>>>>>>>>>>
2230>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bChanged
2231>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2232>>>>>>>>>    
2232>>>>>>>>>    // returns data as UChar array - best way to access the data
2232>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldArray Returns UChar[]
2234>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2235>>>>>>>>>        Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
2236>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return FieldArray
2237>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2238>>>>>>>>>    
2238>>>>>>>>>    // legacy method. Hopefully this is never called.
2238>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldPointer Returns Pointer
2240>>>>>>>>>        Pointer pValue pOldValue
2240>>>>>>>>>        Integer iLen
2240>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
2241>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk
2241>>>>>>>>>        Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
2242>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(FieldArray)) to iLen
2243>>>>>>>>>        Move (Alloc(iLen)) to pValue
2244>>>>>>>>>        Move (MemCopy(pValue,AddressOf(FieldArray),iLen)) to bOk
2245>>>>>>>>>        Send DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
2246>>>>>>>>>        Set pLegacyFieldPointer to pValue
2247>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return pValue
2248>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2249>>>>>>>>>    
2249>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
2251>>>>>>>>>        Integer bOK
2251>>>>>>>>>        Pointer pField
2251>>>>>>>>>        Get pLegacyFieldPointer to pField
2252>>>>>>>>>        If (pField ) Begin
2254>>>>>>>>>            Move (Free(pField)) to bOk
2255>>>>>>>>>            Set pLegacyFieldPointer to 0
2256>>>>>>>>>        End
2256>>>>>>>>>>
2256>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2257>>>>>>>>>    
2257>>>>>>>>>    // augment to release heap allocation
2257>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy_Object
2259>>>>>>>>>        Send DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
2260>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy_object
2262>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2263>>>>>>>>>    
2263>>>>>>>>>End_Class
2264>>>>>>>>>
2264>>>>>>>>>// This contains all extended field objects.
2264>>>>>>>>>// The array contains a list of all objects where item=field#
2264>>>>>>>>>// and item+1=field object.
2264>>>>>>>>>//
2264>>>>>>>>>// Interface is:
2264>>>>>>>>>//     Get Field_object iField to hFldObj
2264>>>>>>>>>//     Send DefineFieldObject iField
2264>>>>>>>>>//     Send ExtendedFieldsUpdate bSave
2264>>>>>>>>>//     Send ExtendedFieldsRefresh bCleared
2264>>>>>>>>>//
2264>>>>>>>>>Class FieldObjects is an Array
2265>>>>>>>>>    
2265>>>>>>>>>    // return object Id for iField. 0 if none.
2265>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Object Integer iField Returns Integer
2267>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItm iCnt
2267>>>>>>>>>        Get Item_Count to iCnt
2268>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iItm
2269>>>>>>>>>        While iItm lt iCnt
2273>>>>>>>>>            If (Value(Self,iItm)=iField) ;                Function_Return (Value(Self,iItm+1))
2276>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
2277>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
2278>>>>>>>>>        Loop
2279>>>>>>>>>>
2279>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return 0
2280>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2281>>>>>>>>>    
2281>>>>>>>>>    // define an extended object for field
2281>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DefineFieldObject Integer iField
2283>>>>>>>>>        Integer hFld
2283>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCnt  iFile
2283>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bInUse
2283>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bHasRecord
2283>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
2285>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Object iField to hFld // this shouldn't exist yet
2286>>>>>>>>>        If not hFld Begin
2288>>>>>>>>>            Get Create U_FieldObject to hFld
2289>>>>>>>>>            Send DefineField to hFld iFile iField
2290>>>>>>>>>            Get Item_Count to iCnt          // add to array
2291>>>>>>>>>            Set Value  iCnt to iField   // Pos   = field#
2292>>>>>>>>>            Set Value  (iCnt+1) to hFld // Pos+1 = field object
2293>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Get In_Use_State to bInUse
2295>>>>>>>>>            If bInUse Begin
2297>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Send Refind_Records
2299>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Get HasRecord to bHasRecord
2301>>>>>>>>>                // updating the newly created field with the file buffer contents we don't
2301>>>>>>>>>                // want to change the field's changed state, which might have been set already.
2301>>>>>>>>>                Send FieldRefresh of hFld (not(bHasRecord)) False
2302>>>>>>>>>            End
2302>>>>>>>>>>
2302>>>>>>>>>        End
2302>>>>>>>>>>
2302>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2303>>>>>>>>>    
2303>>>>>>>>>    // update all extended fields. Field buffer <-- DD buffer
2303>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ExtendedFieldsUpdate Integer bSave
2305>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItm iCnt
2305>>>>>>>>>        Get Item_Count to iCnt
2306>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iItm
2307>>>>>>>>>        While iItm lt iCnt
2311>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
2312>>>>>>>>>            Send FieldUpdate to (Value(Self,iItm)) bSave
2313>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
2314>>>>>>>>>        Loop
2315>>>>>>>>>>
2315>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2316>>>>>>>>>    
2316>>>>>>>>>    // refresh all extended fields. Field buffer --> DD buffer
2316>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ExtendedFieldsRefresh Boolean bCleared
2318>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItm iCnt
2318>>>>>>>>>        Get Item_Count to iCnt
2319>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iItm
2320>>>>>>>>>        While iItm lt iCnt
2324>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
2325>>>>>>>>>            Send FieldRefresh to (Value(Self,iItm)) bCleared True
2326>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
2327>>>>>>>>>        Loop
2328>>>>>>>>>>
2328>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2329>>>>>>>>>    
2329>>>>>>>>>    //
2329>>>>>>>>>    // these are sent from the child field object. We need to direct them
2329>>>>>>>>>    // to the DDO (the parent).
2329>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Changed_State Integer iField Integer bState
2331>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Field_Changed_state iField to bState
2333>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2334>>>>>>>>>    
2334>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Changed_State Integer iField Returns Integer
2336>>>>>>>>>        Integer bState
2336>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Changed_state iField to bState
2338>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bState
2339>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2340>>>>>>>>>    
2340>>>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_AutoFind Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMode
2342>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Send File_field_AutoFind iFile iField iMode
2344>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2345>>>>>>>>>    
2345>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldSaveNoPut Integer iField Returns Boolean
2347>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bIsCommited bNoPut
2347>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get IsCommitted to bIsCommited
2349>>>>>>>>>        // we don't know if this is foreign or not (DDOs never do by themselves). We
2349>>>>>>>>>        // will test for regular. This should never be an issue as the DEO itself
2349>>>>>>>>>        // will be DisplayOnly as needed (we don't have indexed NoEnter=T/Noput=F issues)
2349>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get FieldNoPut iField bIsCommited False to bNoPut
2351>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bNoPut
2352>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
2353>>>>>>>>>    
2353>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy_Object
2355>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Field_Objects to 0
2357>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy_object
2359>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
