2583>>>>>>>// Every data_set will have a object based on this class. It will hold
2583>>>>>>>// the values for the fields, the entry_options and the messages IDs of the
2583>>>>>>>// iEntry, iExit and iValidate messages for each field.
2583>>>>>>>// It is assumed that an object of this class will always be used as a
2583>>>>>>>// child object of a Data_Set object.
2583>>>>>>>//
2583>>>>>>>// Currently the fieldtypes Overlap, Text and Binary are *not* supported.
2583>>>>>>>//
2583>>>>>>>// ITEM-PROPERTY   ASSIGNED-FUNCTION
2583>>>>>>>//
2583>>>>>>>// Value           The value of the field. Will be updated whenever the
2583>>>>>>>//                 value of a field changes due to data-entry or a found
2583>>>>>>>//                 record.
2583>>>>>>>// Data_File       Contains the filenumber. Is the same for every item.
2583>>>>>>>// Data_Field      Contains the fieldnumber for the item. Is equal to the
2583>>>>>>>//                 items' itemnumber.
2583>>>>>>>// Item_Options    Used to store the standard item-options of a field.
2583>>>>>>>// Aux_Value       Used to store the foreign-item-options of a field.
2583>>>>>>>Class cRecordBuffer is an cDDBuffer
2584>>>>>>>
2584>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called from the Data_Set when the Main_File is
2584>>>>>>>    // being set. It will create an item for each field of the file in this
2584>>>>>>>    // object. Fields of the types DF_OVERLAP, DF_TEXT and DF_BINARY are
2584>>>>>>>    // currently not added.
2584>>>>>>>    Procedure Create_Items Integer iFile
2586>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Count iField
2586>>>>>>>
2586>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_NUMBER_FIELDS of iFile to iField_Count
2589>>>>>>>        Set Main_File to iFile
2590>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Data
2591>>>>>>>        Set Item_Count to (iField_Count+1)
2592>>>>>>>        For iField from 0 to iField_Count
2598>>>>>>>>
2598>>>>>>>            // will skip recnum (field 0) if non-recnum table
2598>>>>>>>            // will set to skip if binary, text or overlap
2598>>>>>>>            Set Data_Field iField to iField
2599>>>>>>>        Loop
2600>>>>>>>>
2600>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2601>>>>>>>
2601>>>>>>>    // when an alias is created, we want to clear any values that will not be applied to
2601>>>>>>>    // this alias DD such as prompt and zoom objects (which would point to the superclass master)
2601>>>>>>>    Procedure ReDefineAliasItems Integer iFile
2603>>>>>>>        Integer i iItems
2603>>>>>>>
2603>>>>>>>        Set Main_File to iFile
2604>>>>>>>        Get item_count to iItems
2605>>>>>>>        For i from 0 to (iItems-1)
2611>>>>>>>>
2611>>>>>>>            Set Prompt_Object i to 0
2612>>>>>>>            Set Zoom_Object i to 0
2613>>>>>>>        Loop
2614>>>>>>>>
2614>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2615>>>>>>>
2615>>>>>>>
2615>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called from the parent Data_Set whenever the
2615>>>>>>>    // Data_Set changes its Current_Record property, or after a Save, Delete or Clear operation.
2615>>>>>>>    // We use this event to store the values of the fields in our local record buffer.
2615>>>>>>>    Procedure OnNewCurrentRecord RowID riOld RowID riNew
2617>>>>>>>        Integer iMain_File
2617>>>>>>>        Integer iOldState
2617>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
2617>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
2618>>>>>>>        Boolean bRetain bInReSync
2618>>>>>>>        Integer iFld iFlds iIndex
2618>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
2618>>>>>>>
2618>>>>>>>        Get Parent to hoDD
2619>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iMain_File
2621>>>>>>>
2621>>>>>>>        If not (IsNullRowId(riNew)) ;            Send Entry_Display
2624>>>>>>>        Else Begin
2625>>>>>>>            If (OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin
2627>>>>>>>                // This gets set by webapp during a resync. During resyncs, you don't want to rely
2627>>>>>>>                // on the values in the buffers (as they may not be yours), so you cannot do retain of rememberlast.
2627>>>>>>>                // Fortunately, you don't need to, as this information is not needed during a resync.
2627>>>>>>>                Get pbInResync of operation_origin to bInResync
2628>>>>>>>            End
2628>>>>>>>>
2628>>>>>>>
2628>>>>>>>            // If we have any 17.0 Remember last value items, we must add those items to our array.
2628>>>>>>>            // Only do this if this is the operation origin or a parent (i.e., skip if a child DDO).
2628>>>>>>>            // Also skip if a resync. See above
2628>>>>>>>            If ( not(bInReSync) and ;                ( (Operation_Origin=hoDD) or ;                ( OPERATION_ORIGIN and (Which_data_set(Operation_Origin,iMain_File)<>0) ) ) ) Begin
2630>>>>>>>                Delegate Get pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
2632>>>>>>>                Move (SizeOfArray(DefaultValues)) to iFlds
2633>>>>>>>                For iFld from 0 to (iFlds-1)
2639>>>>>>>>
2639>>>>>>>                    Move (DefaultValues[iFld].sDefault=DD_RememberLast) to bRetain // if this is a dynamically assigned remember-last
2640>>>>>>>                    If bRetain Begin
2642>>>>>>>                        Get Value DefaultValues[iFld].iField to DefaultValues[iFld].sLastValue
2643>>>>>>>                    End
2643>>>>>>>>
2643>>>>>>>                    Else Begin
2644>>>>>>>                        Move '' to DefaultValues[iFld].sLastValue
2645>>>>>>>                    End
2645>>>>>>>>
2645>>>>>>>                Loop
2646>>>>>>>>
2646>>>>>>>                Delegate Set pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
2648>>>>>>>            End
2648>>>>>>>>
2648>>>>>>>
2648>>>>>>>            // we must do this to make retains not set changed_state
2648>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Change_Disabled_State to iOldState
2650>>>>>>>            Delegate Set Change_Disabled_State to True
2652>>>>>>>            // If mode is anything other than clear, we do a clear all (clear keeps retains, clear all does not)
2652>>>>>>>            // Also do clear all if the DDO is foreign.
2652>>>>>>>
2652>>>>>>>            // If bInReSync, we never use retains, as the buffer is not ours yet.
2652>>>>>>>            // The Entry_Clear, Entry_Clear_All parameter is bIgnoreRetains.
2652>>>>>>>            // When True, retain and retain_all states are ignored and cleared.
2652>>>>>>>            If (Operation_Mode=MODE_CLEARING and ;                ( (Operation_Origin=parent(Self)) or ;                (Which_data_set(Operation_Origin,iMain_File)<>0) ) ) Begin
2654>>>>>>>                    Send Entry_Clear bInReSync
2655>>>>>>>            End
2655>>>>>>>>
2655>>>>>>>            Else Begin
2656>>>>>>>                Send Entry_Clear_all bInResync
2657>>>>>>>            End
2657>>>>>>>>
2657>>>>>>>            Delegate Set Change_Disabled_State to iOldState
2659>>>>>>>            Set Changed_State to False
2660>>>>>>>        End
2660>>>>>>>>
2660>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2661>>>>>>>
2661>>>>>>>    // Make sure to set the Changed_State of the Data_Set to TRUE when a
2661>>>>>>>    // field value changes and it's not during the Setting of the Defaults.
2661>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Changed_State Integer iState
2663>>>>>>>        Integer iNoChange
2663>>>>>>>        // Server.pkg in dso already knows this property
2663>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Change_disabled_State to iNoChange
2665>>>>>>>        If not iNoChange Begin
2667>>>>>>>            Forward Set Changed_State to iState
2669>>>>>>>            Delegate Set Changed_State to iState
2671>>>>>>>        End
2671>>>>>>>>
2671>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2672>>>>>>>
2672>>>>>>>End_Class
2673>>>>>>>
2673>>>>>>>
2673>>>>>>>// Objects of this class will be used to store all kinds of attributes
2673>>>>>>>// which belong to a field.
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>// FA_MIN_VALUE
2673>>>>>>>// Used to store the mininum value of field.
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>// FA_MAX_VALUE
2673>>>>>>>// Used to store the maximum value of a field.
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>// FA_CHECK_VALUE
2673>>>>>>>// Used to store a string which contains all possible values of a field.
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>// FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE
2673>>>>>>>// Used to store the TRUE value for a checkbox field
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>// FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE
2673>>>>>>>// Used to store the FALSE value of a checkbox field
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>// FA_TABLE_OBJECT
2673>>>>>>>// Stores object Id of a validation table.
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>// FA_ERROR_MESSAGE
2673>>>>>>>// Used to store a error text which will be shown to a user when a fields
2673>>>>>>>// value violates one of the rules defined for it.
2673>>>>>>>// This field may contain the special strings @MIN, @MAX and @CHECK. When
2673>>>>>>>// these are used, these will be replaced by the actual value of MIN_VALUE,
2673>>>>>>>// MAX_VALUE or CHECK_VALUE.
2673>>>>>>>//
2673>>>>>>>
2673>>>>>>>
2673>>>>>>>// Validation Types
2673>>>>>>>Enumeration_List
2673>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_NONE
2673>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE
2673>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK
2673>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX
2673>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE
2673>>>>>>>End_Enumeration_List
2673>>>>>>>
2673>>>>>>>
2673>>>>>>>Class Field_Attributes is a Array
2674>>>>>>>
2674>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
2676>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
2678>>>>>>>        // Private: This replaces the use of arrays to get at this value. This
2678>>>>>>>        // allows us to find specific validation types (like checkboxes) more
2678>>>>>>>        // quickly than scanning an array
2678>>>>>>>        Property String Private.Validation_Types     ''
2679>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2680>>>>>>>
2680>>>>>>>    // Returns the extended validation type for the passed field.
2680>>>>>>>    Function Field_Validation_Type Integer iField Returns Integer
2682>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2682>>>>>>>        If iField ;            Move (mid(Private.Validation_Types(Self),1,iField)) to iType
2685>>>>>>>        Else ;            Move FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_NONE to iType
2687>>>>>>>        Function_Return iType
2688>>>>>>>    End_Function
2689>>>>>>>
2689>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Validation_Type Integer iField String sType
2691>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2691>>>>>>>        String sTypes
2691>>>>>>>        If iField Begin
2693>>>>>>>            Get Private.Validation_Types to sTypes
2694>>>>>>>            Set Private.Validation_Types to (Overstrike(sType, sTypes, iField))
2695>>>>>>>        End
2695>>>>>>>>
2695>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2696>>>>>>>
2696>>>>>>>    // Set any defaults required by this class when the main file is created.
2696>>>>>>>    // Create a string which contains all validation types. Set all to
2696>>>>>>>    // No extended validation type.
2696>>>>>>>    Procedure Create_Items
2698>>>>>>>        String  sType
2698>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
2698>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Count to iCOunt
2700>>>>>>>        Move FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_NONE to sType
2701>>>>>>>        Set Private.Validation_Types to (Repeat(sType,iCount))
2702>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2703>>>>>>>
2703>>>>>>>    // Return field number of next field matching the passed validation type.
2703>>>>>>>    // Pass validation type and last position checked. Return 0 if no match
2703>>>>>>>    Function Next_Validation_Type String sType Integer iOffset Returns Integer
2705>>>>>>>        String sTypes
2705>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
2705>>>>>>>        Get Private.Validation_Types to sTypes
2706>>>>>>>        Move (Pos(sType, mid(sTypes,255,iOffset+1))) to iPos
2707>>>>>>>        If iPos ;            Add iOffset to iPos
2710>>>>>>>        Function_Return iPos
2711>>>>>>>    End_Function
2712>>>>>>>
2712>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called by the Extended_Data_Set to set the
2712>>>>>>>    // errornumber and message which will be triggered when it needs to.
2712>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Error Integer iField Integer iErr String sMsg
2714>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2714>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2715>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_ERROR_NUMBER) to iErr
2716>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_ERROR_MESSAGE) to sMsg
2717>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2718>>>>>>>
2718>>>>>>>    // Used to retreive the error number and message for a particular field
2718>>>>>>>    Function Field_Error_Number Integer iField Returns Integer
2720>>>>>>>        Integer iErr
2720>>>>>>>        Get Value (iField*FA_COUNT + FA_ERROR_NUMBER)  to iErr
2721>>>>>>>        Function_Return iErr
2722>>>>>>>    End_Function
2723>>>>>>>
2723>>>>>>>    Function Field_Error_Message Integer iField Returns String
2725>>>>>>>        String sValue
2725>>>>>>>        Get Value (iField*FA_COUNT + FA_ERROR_MESSAGE) to sValue
2726>>>>>>>        Function_Return sValue
2727>>>>>>>    End_Function
2728>>>>>>>
2728>>>>>>>
2728>>>>>>>    // This function manages the validation of a field against its extended
2728>>>>>>>    // validations.
2728>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field Integer iField Returns Integer
2730>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2730>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
2730>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
2731>>>>>>>        If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE) ;            Get Validate_Field_Range iField to iResult
2734>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK) ;            Get Validate_Field_Check iField to iResult
2738>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Get Validate_Field_Checkbox iField to iResult
2742>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE) ;            Get Validate_Field_Table iField to iResult
2746>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
2747>>>>>>>    End_Function
2748>>>>>>>
2748>>>>>>>    // All extended validations know how to send callback messages (iMsg) to
2748>>>>>>>    // the calling object (iObj). This allows external lists to get filled w/
2748>>>>>>>    // the contents of a range. Used by combo boxes, spinners, etc.
2748>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
2750>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2750>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
2750>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
2751>>>>>>>        If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Range iField iObj iMsg
2754>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Check iField iObj iMsg
2758>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Checkbox iField iObj iMsg
2762>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Table iField iObj iMsg
2766>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2767>>>>>>>
2767>>>>>>>    // Return the id of the validation table if one exists. Otherwise return
2767>>>>>>>    // a zero.
2767>>>>>>>    Function Field_Table_Object Integer iField Returns Integer
2769>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2769>>>>>>>        Integer iObj
2769>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2769>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2770>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
2771>>>>>>>        If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE) ;            Get Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iObj
2774>>>>>>>        Function_Return iObj
2775>>>>>>>    End_Function
2776>>>>>>>
2776>>>>>>>    // Procedure to set the range for a field. It will automatically set the
2776>>>>>>>    // validation type of the field as well.
2776>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Value_Range Integer iField String sMin String sMax
2778>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2778>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2779>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_MIN_VALUE) to sMin
2780>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_MAX_VALUE) to sMax
2781>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE
2782>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2783>>>>>>>
2783>>>>>>>    // Function to check a fields value agains a given check string.
2783>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Range Integer iField Returns Integer
2785>>>>>>>        String  sMin
2785>>>>>>>        String  sMax
2785>>>>>>>        String  sValue
2785>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Type
2785>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
2785>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
2785>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2785>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2786>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MIN_VALUE) to sMin
2787>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MAX_VALUE) to sMax
2788>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
2790>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
2792>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_TYPE of iFile iField to iField_Type
2795>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iResult
2796>>>>>>>        If (iField_Type=DF_ASCII) ;            Move (sValue < sMin or sValue > sMax) to iResult
2799>>>>>>>        Else If (iField_Type=DF_BCD) ;            Move (Number(sValue) < Number(sMin) or ;            Number(sValue) > Number(sMax)) to iResult
2803>>>>>>>        Else If (iField_Type=DF_DATE) ;            Move (Date(sValue) < Date(sMin) or Date(sValue) > Date(sMax)) to iResult
2807>>>>>>>        Else If (iField_Type=DF_DATETIME) ;            Move (Cast(sValue,DateTime) < Cast(sMin,DateTime) or Cast(sValue,DateTime) > Cast(sMax,DateTime)) to iResult
2811>>>>>>>        If iResult Begin
2813>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_RANGE sMin sMax
2815>>>>>>>            Function_Return 1
2816>>>>>>>        End
2816>>>>>>>>
2816>>>>>>>    End_Function
2817>>>>>>>
2817>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
2817>>>>>>>    // Just call back with the two range values
2817>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Range Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
2819>>>>>>>        String  sMin
2819>>>>>>>        String  sMax
2819>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2819>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2820>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MIN_VALUE) to sMin
2821>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MAX_VALUE) to sMax
2822>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 0 sMin '' 0 (NullrowId())
2823>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 1 sMax '' 0 (NullrowId())
2824>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2825>>>>>>>
2825>>>>>>>    // Procedure to set the check for a field. It will automatically set the
2825>>>>>>>    // validation type of the field as well.
2825>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Value_Check Integer iField String sCheck
2827>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2827>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2828>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_CHECK_VALUE) to sCheck
2829>>>>>>>        //Set Value iBase to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK
2829>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK
2830>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2831>>>>>>>
2831>>>>>>>    // Function to check a fields value agains a given check string.
2831>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Check Integer iField Returns Integer
2833>>>>>>>        String  sCheck
2833>>>>>>>        String  sValue
2833>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2833>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
2833>>>>>>>        Integer iLength
2833>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
2833>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
2833>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2834>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECK_VALUE) to sCheck
2835>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
2837>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
2839>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_LENGTH of iFile iField to iLength
2842>>>>>>>        Move (Pad( sValue,iLength)) to sValue
2843>>>>>>>        // Replace the seperation characters with two of them so the user
2843>>>>>>>        // can't bypass the check by entering a seperation character.
2843>>>>>>>        Move (Replaces("|", sValue, "||")) to sValue
2844>>>>>>>        // Report an error if rules are violated.
2844>>>>>>>        Move (Pos( sValue, sCheck)) to iPos
2845>>>>>>>        If not iPos Begin
2847>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_CHECK sCheck
2849>>>>>>>            Function_Return 1
2850>>>>>>>        End
2850>>>>>>>>
2850>>>>>>>    End_Function
2851>>>>>>>
2851>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
2851>>>>>>>    // Call back with all valid check values
2851>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Check Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
2853>>>>>>>        String  sCheck
2853>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2853>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
2853>>>>>>>        Integer iItem
2853>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2854>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECK_VALUE) to sCheck
2855>>>>>>>        Append sCheck "|"
2856>>>>>>>        Move (Pos( "|", sCheck)) to iPos
2857>>>>>>>        While iPos
2861>>>>>>>            If (iPos > 1) Begin
2863>>>>>>>                Send iMsg to iObj iItem (Left(sCheck,iPos-1)) '' 0 (NullrowId())
2864>>>>>>>                Increment iItem
2865>>>>>>>            End
2865>>>>>>>>
2865>>>>>>>            Move (Mid( sCheck, 255, iPos+1))  to sCheck
2866>>>>>>>            Move (Pos( "|", sCheck)) to iPos
2867>>>>>>>        Loop
2868>>>>>>>>
2868>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2869>>>>>>>
2869>>>>>>>    // Procedure to set up a checkbox field. We will store the TRUE and FALSE
2869>>>>>>>    // Values in the extended array.
2869>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_CheckBox_Values Integer iField String sTrue String sFalse
2871>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2871>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2872>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
2873>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE) to sFalse
2874>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX
2875>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2876>>>>>>>
2876>>>>>>>    // Return the Value associated with the field and its select-state.
2876>>>>>>>    Function Field_CheckBox_Value Integer iField Integer iState Returns String
2878>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2878>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2878>>>>>>>        String sValue
2878>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2879>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
2880>>>>>>>        If (iType <> FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Move iState to sValue
2883>>>>>>>        Else ;            Get Value (iBase + If(iState,FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE,FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE));            to sValue
2885>>>>>>>        Function_Return sValue
2886>>>>>>>    End_Function
2887>>>>>>>
2887>>>>>>>    // Return the select_state based on the passed value and field
2887>>>>>>>    Function Field_Value_Select_State Integer iField String sValue Returns Integer
2889>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2889>>>>>>>        Integer iType
2889>>>>>>>        String  sTrue
2889>>>>>>>        Integer iState
2889>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
2889>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Type
2889>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2890>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
2891>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
2892>>>>>>>        If (iType <> FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Move (not(sValue=0 or sValue='')) to iState
2895>>>>>>>        Else Begin
2896>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
2898>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_TYPE of iFile iField to iField_Type
2901>>>>>>>            If (iField_Type = DF_BCD) ;                Move (Number(sValue)=Number(sTrue)) to iState
2904>>>>>>>            Else ; // DF_ASCII                Move (sValue=sTrue) to iState
2906>>>>>>>        End
2906>>>>>>>>
2906>>>>>>>        Function_Return iState
2907>>>>>>>    End_Function
2908>>>>>>>
2908>>>>>>>
2908>>>>>>>    // Check that the buffer value is one of the two checkbox values.
2908>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Checkbox Integer iField Returns Integer
2910>>>>>>>        String  sTrue
2910>>>>>>>        String  sFalse
2910>>>>>>>        String  sValue
2910>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Type
2910>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
2910>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
2910>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2910>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2911>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
2912>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE) to sFalse
2913>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
2915>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
2917>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_TYPE of iFile iField to iField_Type
2920>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iResult
2921>>>>>>>        If (iField_Type = DF_BCD) ;            Move (Number(sValue)=Number(sTrue) or ;            Number(sValue)=Number(sFalse)) to iResult
2924>>>>>>>        Else ; // DF_ASCII            Move (sValue=sTrue or sValue=sFalse) to iResult
2926>>>>>>>        If not iResult Begin
2928>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_CHECKBOX sTrue sFalse
2930>>>>>>>            Function_Return 1
2931>>>>>>>        End
2931>>>>>>>>
2931>>>>>>>    End_Function
2932>>>>>>>
2932>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
2932>>>>>>>    // Just call back with the two true and false values
2932>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Checkbox Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
2934>>>>>>>        String  sTrue
2934>>>>>>>        String  sFalse
2934>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2934>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2935>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
2936>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE) to sFalse
2937>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 0 sTrue '' 0 (NullrowId())
2938>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 1 sFalse '' 0 (NullrowId())
2939>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2940>>>>>>>
2940>>>>>>>    // The object keeps track of a validation table object. This table object
2940>>>>>>>    // can be any type of object must at a minimum understand a small message
2940>>>>>>>    // protocol (see xvaltbl.pkg for info)
2940>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Value_Table Integer iField Integer iObj
2942>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2942>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2943>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iObj
2944>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE
2945>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2946>>>>>>>
2946>>>>>>>    // This valdates against a validation table if appropriate (if a table
2946>>>>>>>    // exists and the table's validate_State is T). It validates by passing
2946>>>>>>>    // the message validate_value to the validation table object
2946>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Table Integer iField Returns Integer
2948>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2948>>>>>>>        Integer iTableObj
2948>>>>>>>        String  sValue
2948>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
2948>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2949>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iTableObj
2950>>>>>>>        If (iTableObj and Validate_State(iTableObj) ) Begin
2952>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
2954>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Value of iTableOBj sValue to iResult
2955>>>>>>>            If iResult ;                Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_VALUE_TABLE
2959>>>>>>>        End
2959>>>>>>>>
2959>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
2960>>>>>>>    End_Function
2961>>>>>>>
2961>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
2961>>>>>>>    // Pass the request on to the validation table. This is the most common
2961>>>>>>>    // use of this.
2961>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Table Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
2963>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
2963>>>>>>>        Integer iTableObj
2963>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
2964>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iTableObj
2965>>>>>>>        If iTableObj ;            Send Request_Fill_From_List to iTableObj iObj iMsg
2968>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
2969>>>>>>>
2969>>>>>>>    // Often extended valditation types can provide automatic prompt
2969>>>>>>>    // objects. If the extended type supports a prompt object and there is
2969>>>>>>>    // a global validation_list object, we will use it
