3856>>>>>>>    // This procedure is being used by DEOs when they need to copy the item-
3856>>>>>>>    // options from the Data_Set. When the filenumber being passed is not
3856>>>>>>>    // equal to the Main_File of this Data_Set, then the Foreign_Field_Options
3856>>>>>>>    // will be applied.
3856>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Options Integer iFile Integer iField Returns Integer
3858>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
3858>>>>>>>        Integer iMain_File
3858>>>>>>>        Integer iOpts
3858>>>>>>>        Integer iRB
3858>>>>>>>        Integer iType
3858>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain_File
3859>>>>>>>        If (iFile <> iMain_File) ;            Get Data_Set iFile to iDSO
3862>>>>>>>        Else ;            Move Self to iDSO
3864>>>>>>>        If iDSO Begin
3866>>>>>>>            Get Field_Options of iDSO iField to iOpts
3867>>>>>>>            // we consider the item to be foreign if the DDO main file is different than the one
3867>>>>>>>            // passed and we do not allow foreign (parent) new records to be saved.
3867>>>>>>>            If (iFile<>iMain_File and Allow_Foreign_New_Save_State(iDSO)=0) ; // Add Foreign_Field_Options                Move (iOpts ior Foreign_Field_Options(iDSO, iField)) to iOpts
3870>>>>>>>            Function_Return iOpts
3871>>>>>>>        End
