4067>>>>>>>
4067>>>>>>>    // This function will be called from within DEOs when an item is being
4067>>>>>>>    // entered, exited or needs validation. The first argument holds the
4067>>>>>>>    // file number, the second argument holds the field and the third
4067>>>>>>>    // holds the id of the message  which can be send to retrieve the message
4067>>>>>>>    // which needs to be send for this File/Field/Event combination.
4067>>>>>>>    // The value of the second argument can be  GET_Field_Entry_MSG,
4067>>>>>>>    // GET_Field_Exit_MSG or GET_Field_Validate_MSG.
4067>>>>>>>    // This will redirect to the proper data-set object.
4067>>>>>>>    Function Exec_File_Field_Message Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMsg_ID Returns Integer
4069>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4069>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
4069>>>>>>>        Get Data_set iFile to iDSO
4070>>>>>>>        If iDSO ;            Get Exec_Field_Message of iDSO iField iMsg_ID to iResult
4073>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
4074>>>>>>>    End_Function
4075>>>>>>>
4075>>>>>>>    // Find the data-set whose main_file is the same as File#. The message
4075>>>>>>>    // Which_data_set includes updating parent files, we will throw those out.
4075>>>>>>>    // This has been augmented to search down the DDO tree if we do not find
4075>>>>>>>    // the DD with our quick C Which_Data_set search
4075>>>>>>>    Function Data_Set Integer iFile Returns Integer
4077>>>>>>>        Integer iTmp
4077>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4077>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iTmp
4078>>>>>>>        If (iTmp = iFile) ;            Function_Return Self
4081>>>>>>>        Get Which_Data_Set iFile to iDSO
4082>>>>>>>        If iDSO Begin
4084>>>>>>>            // check that DS's main-file is the File (and not a parent file)
4084>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of iDSO to iTmp
4085>>>>>>>            If (iTmp = iFile) ;                Function_Return iDSO
4088>>>>>>>        End
4088>>>>>>>>
4088>>>>>>>
4088>>>>>>>        // This really should have succeeded by now. If not we need to do a
4088>>>>>>>        // downward sweep looking for DD. This will be a slower process since it
4088>>>>>>>        // involves flex level DDO structure traversal. We should very rarely ever
4088>>>>>>>        // get to this point. If we do, it takes longer!
4088>>>>>>>
4088>>>>>>>        // Unlike other traversals we will mark and check in a single
4088>>>>>>>        // step.
4088>>>>>>>        // This Mark_Id creates a sequence Id for this clear. This way
4088>>>>>>>        // DSOs only get cleared one time during this process.
4088>>>>>>>        Send IncrementCurrentMarkId
4089>>>>>>>        Get Private.Data_set iFile to iDSO // this does the recursive downward search
4090>>>>>>>        Function_Return iDSO
4091>>>>>>>    End_Function
4092>>>>>>>
4092>>>>>>>    Function Private.Data_Set Integer iFile Returns Integer
4094>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
4094>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO hDD
4094>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
4094>>>>>>>
4094>>>>>>>        If (iFile=Main_file(Self)) ;            Function_Return Self
4097>>>>>>>
4097>>>>>>>        // We are only looking at sequence ID.
4097>>>>>>>        Set Last_Mark_Sequence_id to DD_Current_mark_id
4098>>>>>>>
4098>>>>>>>        // recurse Down first, since we already tried upward direction.
4098>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
4099>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4100>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4106>>>>>>>>
4106>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
4107>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
4107>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) Begin
4109>>>>>>>                Get Private.Data_Set of iDSO iFile to hDD
4110>>>>>>>                If hDD ;                    Function_Return hDD // when found...get out
4113>>>>>>>            End
4113>>>>>>>>
4113>>>>>>>        Loop
4114>>>>>>>>
4114>>>>>>>        // recurse up server list next. We do this 2nd because it is
4114>>>>>>>        // the less likely path for success.
4114>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4115>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4116>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4122>>>>>>>>
4122>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
4123>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
4123>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) Begin
4125>>>>>>>                Get Private.Data_Set of iDSO iFile to hDD
4126>>>>>>>                If hDD ;                    Function_Return hDD // when found...get out
4129>>>>>>>            End
4129>>>>>>>>
4129>>>>>>>        Loop
4130>>>>>>>>
4130>>>>>>>        Function_Return 0 // if here, our traversal has failed.
4131>>>>>>>    End_Function
4132>>>>>>>
4132>>>>>>>    // These methods can be used to set/get a field property in a flexible
4132>>>>>>>    // way. The first two argument are the file- and fieldnumber followed by
4132>>>>>>>    // the ID of the message that should be send. The last argument should
4132>>>>>>>    // be the value to set or the variable to store the value in.
4132>>>>>>>    Procedure Set File_Field_Property Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMsg String sValue
4134>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4134>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to iDSO
4135>>>>>>>        If iDSO Begin
4137>>>>>>>            Set iMsg of iDSO iField to sValue
4138>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return sValue
4139>>>>>>>        End
4139>>>>>>>>
4139>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4140>>>>>>>
4140>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Property Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMsg Returns Integer
4142>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4142>>>>>>>        String  sValue
4142>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to iDSO
4143>>>>>>>        If iDSO Begin
4145>>>>>>>            Get iMsg of iDSO iField to sValue
4146>>>>>>>            Function_Return sValue
4147>>>>>>>        End
4147>>>>>>>>
4147>>>>>>>    End_Function
4148>>>>>>>
4148>>>>>>>    // This procedure will return the number of fields in the object
4148>>>>>>>    Function Field_Count Returns Integer
4150>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Item_Count(Record_Buffer(Self)) - 1)
4151>>>>>>>    End_Function
4152>>>>>>>
4152>>>>>>>    // This procedure will clear all flags in the visited_fields string so
4152>>>>>>>    // that all field will be validated on the next requests.
4152>>>>>>>    Procedure Clear_Visited_Fields
4154>>>>>>>        // this clears field visitation marks
4154>>>>>>>        Set Visited_Fields to (Repeat(" ", Field_Count(Self)))
4155>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4156>>>>>>>
4156>>>>>>>    // Private.Initialize_Visited
4156>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called when validations (and perhaps other
4156>>>>>>>    // events) is requested. It clears the visited marks and then proceeds
4156>>>>>>>    // to clear the marks up the server tree.
4156>>>>>>>    // This is passed two parameters: Up_and_down, If true upward and downward
4156>>>>>>>    // initialize. If Clear_Fields also clear the field string
4156>>>>>>>    Procedure Private.Initialize_Visited Integer Up_and_Down Integer Clear_Fields
4158>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
4158>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4158>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
4158>>>>>>>
4158>>>>>>>        // recurse up server list first. Only recurse up
4158>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4159>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4160>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4166>>>>>>>>
4166>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
4167>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
4167>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                Send Private.Initialize_Visited to iDSO False Clear_Fields
4170>>>>>>>        Loop
4171>>>>>>>>
4171>>>>>>>
4171>>>>>>>        If Clear_Fields ;            Send Clear_Visited_Fields // clear all markers in this object
4174>>>>>>>        // this clears the visited mark for the entire object
4174>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to False
4175>>>>>>>        Set DownDelete_State to False
4176>>>>>>>        Set Last_Mark_Sequence_id to DD_Current_mark_id
4177>>>>>>>
4177>>>>>>>        // If Up_and_Down recurse Down server list
4177>>>>>>>        If Up_and_Down Begin
4179>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
4180>>>>>>>            Decrement iMax // **EK** This line was missing
4181>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to iMax
4187>>>>>>>>
4187>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
4188>>>>>>>                // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
4188>>>>>>>                If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                    Send Private.Initialize_Visited to iDSO True Clear_Fields
4191>>>>>>>            Loop
4192>>>>>>>>
4192>>>>>>>        End
4192>>>>>>>>
4192>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4193>>>>>>>
4193>>>>>>>
4193>>>>>>>    // Clears Visited marks and (maybe) field visited marks in all required
4193>>>>>>>    // DSOs. If Up_and_Down is TRUE DSOs are marked up and Down (delete style)
4193>>>>>>>    // propagation. If False, DSOs are marked up (save style). This does not
4193>>>>>>>    // have a mode to mark ALL DSOs in a structure. (Not needed so far).
4193>>>>>>>    // If Clear_Fields is T the field string marker is also cleared.
4193>>>>>>>    // The method of using the global integer DD_Current_Mark_ID is an opt-
4193>>>>>>>    // imizer. This is private - do not tamper with it!
4193>>>>>>>    // Note that Intialize_Visited does not always Clear all DDOs in the structure. When
4193>>>>>>>    // Up_and_Down is true, it is marking all DDOs that will participate in a cascade delete
4193>>>>>>>    // which may not be all DDOs in the structure. If you want to initialize all DDOs use InitializeAllVisited
4193>>>>>>>    Procedure Initialize_Visited Integer Up_and_Down Integer Clear_Fields
4195>>>>>>>        Send IncrementCurrentMarkId
4196>>>>>>>        Send Private.Initialize_Visited Up_and_Down Clear_Fields
4197>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4198>>>>>>>
4198>>>>>>>    Procedure InitializeAllVisited2
4200>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount
4200>>>>>>>        Handle hoDSO
4200>>>>>>>
4200>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to False
4201>>>>>>>        Set Last_Mark_Sequence_id to DD_Current_mark_id // marks this as visited
4202>>>>>>>
4202>>>>>>>        // recurse up server list.
4202>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4203>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
4209>>>>>>>>
4209>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoDSO
4210>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
4210>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(hoDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                Send InitializeAllVisited2 of hoDSO
4213>>>>>>>        Loop
4214>>>>>>>>
4214>>>>>>>
4214>>>>>>>        // recurse down client list.
4214>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
4215>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
4221>>>>>>>>
4221>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoDSO
4222>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
4222>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(hoDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                Send InitializeAllVisited2 to hoDSO
4225>>>>>>>        Loop
4226>>>>>>>>
4226>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4227>>>>>>>
4227>>>>>>>    // clears visited flag for *all* ddos in the structure.
4227>>>>>>>    Procedure InitializeAllVisited
4229>>>>>>>        Send IncrementCurrentMarkId
4230>>>>>>>        Send InitializeAllVisited2
4231>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4232>>>>>>>
4232>>>>>>>
4232>>>>>>>    // Internal recursive message to check file connections. Called from
4232>>>>>>>    // Valid_connections only. Private message
4232>>>>>>>    Function Private.Valid_Structure Integer Up_And_Down Returns Integer
4234>>>>>>>        Integer iRval iCount iMax
4234>>>>>>>        Handle iDSO iPDSO
4234>>>>>>>        Integer iPMax iPCount iPMain
4234>>>>>>>        Boolean bUpDown bNull bCascadeNull bDown
4234>>>>>>>
4234>>>>>>>        // Check Current Connections
4234>>>>>>>        Get Valid_Servers to iRval           // always check servers
4235>>>>>>>        If (iRval=0 and Up_and_Down) ;       // check Clients if required            Get Valid_Clients to iRval
4238>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
4239>>>>>>>
4239>>>>>>>        // Ask Server data-sets to check their server connections
4239>>>>>>>        If not iRval Begin // check up
4241>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4242>>>>>>>            Decrement iMax
4243>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to iMax
4249>>>>>>>>
4249>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
4250>>>>>>>                If not (Visited_state(iDSO)) ;                    Get Private.Valid_Structure of iDSO False to iRVal
4253>>>>>>>            Until iRval
4255>>>>>>>        End
4255>>>>>>>>
4255>>>>>>>
4255>>>>>>>        // If required, Ask Clients to check their server and client connections
4255>>>>>>>        //
4255>>>>>>>        If (iRval=0 and Up_and_Down) Begin // check down
4257>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
4258>>>>>>>            Decrement iMax
4259>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to iMax
4265>>>>>>>>
4265>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
4266>>>>>>>                If not (Visited_state(iDSO)) Begin
4268>>>>>>>                    Get Data_Set_Server_Count of iDSO to iPMax
4269>>>>>>>                    // test if all deletable parents for a non parent null allowed/cascade delete null
4269>>>>>>>                    For iPCount from 0 to (iPMax-1)
4275>>>>>>>>
4275>>>>>>>                        Get Data_Set_Server of iDSO iPCount to iPDSO
4276>>>>>>>                        Get DownDelete_State of iPDSO to bDown
4277>>>>>>>                        If (bDown) Begin
4279>>>>>>>                            Get Main_File of iPDSO to iPMain
4280>>>>>>>                            Get IsNullParentAllowed of iDSO iPMain to bNull
4281>>>>>>>                            Get IsCascadeDeleteNull of iDSO iPMain to bCascadeNull
4282>>>>>>>                            Move (not(bNull) or not(bCascadeNull)) to bUpDown
4283>>>>>>>                        End
4283>>>>>>>>
4283>>>>>>>                    Until bUpDown
4285>>>>>>>                    Get Private.Valid_Structure of iDSO bUpDown to iRVal
4286>>>>>>>                End
4286>>>>>>>>
4286>>>>>>>            Until iRval
4288>>>>>>>        End
4288>>>>>>>>
4288>>>>>>>
4288>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
4289>>>>>>>
4289>>>>>>>    End_Function
4290>>>>>>>
4290>>>>>>>    // Validate data-set updating connections against required connections
4290>>>>>>>    // Pass: Up_and_down=T if we should check Server and Client connections
4290>>>>>>>    //                  =F is we only check servers
4290>>>>>>>    // Ret: 0 if ok, Missing File# if not ok.
4290>>>>>>>    // Up_And_Down should be true when testing for cascade delete structures and
4290>>>>>>>    // false when testing for save / delete-no-cascade structures
4290>>>>>>>    Function Valid_Structure Integer Up_And_Down Returns Integer
4292>>>>>>>        Send Initialize_Visited Up_and_Down False // False=don't clear field marks
4293>>>>>>>        If (Up_And_Down) Begin
4295>>>>>>>            Send MarkDDOsForCascadeDelete
4296>>>>>>>        End
4296>>>>>>>>
4296>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Private.Valid_Structure(Self,Up_and_Down))
4297>>>>>>>    End_Function
4298>>>>>>>
4298>>>>>>>    // mark all DDOs which are part of this deletes cascade delete tree
4298>>>>>>>    // mark this and all clients as Downward deletable. This includes
4298>>>>>>>    // cacscade delete and cascade set to null (not for cascade_delete_state=F)
4298>>>>>>>    Procedure MarkDDOsForCascadeDelete
4300>>>>>>>        Integer iMax  iCount
4300>>>>>>>        Boolean bDown
4300>>>>>>>        Handle hoDDO
4300>>>>>>>        Set DownDelete_State to True
4301>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
4302>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
4308>>>>>>>>
4308>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoDDO
4309>>>>>>>            Get DownDelete_State of hoDDO to bDown
4310>>>>>>>            If not bDown Begin // circular DDO test - never do this
4312>>>>>>>                Send MarkDDOsForCascadeDelete of hoDDO
4313>>>>>>>            End
4313>>>>>>>>
4313>>>>>>>        Loop
4314>>>>>>>>
4314>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4315>>>>>>>
4315>>>>>>>
4315>>>>>>>    // This function will execute the validation message for each field within
4315>>>>>>>    // this object. If DoAllFG is true all items are validated. If false
4315>>>>>>>    // only unvisited items are checked.
4315>>>>>>>    // Added bNoStop, If true, all items are validated. It is up to you to
4315>>>>>>>    // do something with the possible cascade of errors
4315>>>>>>>    // if the err returns DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID we will not continue
4315>>>>>>>    // the validation (the other fields will be bad). This works best if the
4315>>>>>>>    // findreq appears as one of the first fields in the file (which is almost
4315>>>>>>>    // always the case
4315>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Fields Integer DoAllFg Integer bNoStop Returns Integer
4317>>>>>>>        Integer iRetval
4317>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
4317>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
4317>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
4317>>>>>>>        Integer iErr
4317>>>>>>>        String  sVS
4317>>>>>>>        Get Visited_Fields to sVS
4318>>>>>>>        Get Field_Count to iMax
4319>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iFile
4320>>>>>>>        For iCount from 1 to iMax
4326>>>>>>>>
4326>>>>>>>            If (DoAllFG or Mid(sVS, 1, iCount)=" ") Begin
4328>>>>>>>                Get Validate_Field iCount to iErr
4329>>>>>>>                If iErr Begin
4331>>>>>>>                    Move iErr to iRetVal
4332>>>>>>>                    // error occurred. If not no-stop or the error is
4332>>>>>>>                    // a findreq error - we are done.
4332>>>>>>>                    If (not(bNoStop) or iRetVal=DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID) ;                        Function_Return iRetVal
4335>>>>>>>                End
4335>>>>>>>>
4335>>>>>>>            End
4335>>>>>>>>
4335>>>>>>>        Loop
4336>>>>>>>>
4336>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
4337>>>>>>>    End_Function
4338>>>>>>>
4338>>>>>>>    // 17.0 - added support for null-parents. If null parents allowed, req lets it through
4338>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Required Integer iField Returns Integer
4340>>>>>>>        Boolean bNull bErr
4340>>>>>>>
4340>>>>>>>        Move (trim(Field_Current_Value(Self,iField))='') to bErr
4341>>>>>>>        If bErr ;            Send Data_set_Error iField DFERR_ENTRY_REQUIRED ""
4344>>>>>>>        Function_Return bErr
4345>>>>>>>    End_Function
4346>>>>>>>
4346>>>>>>>    // return true if we should skip validation for this field. This can happen with Null allowed parents.
4346>>>>>>>    // if this is foreign, new and has no changes and is null allowed we will skip.
4346>>>>>>>    Function SkipValidate Integer iField Returns Boolean
4348>>>>>>>        Boolean bSkip bFieldChanged bEmpty
4348>>>>>>>        String sValue
4348>>>>>>>
4348>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN<>Self and not(HasRecord(Self)) and not(changed_state(Self))) Begin
4350>>>>>>>            // We must also check field_changed_state and only skip if this is not changed.
4350>>>>>>>            Get Field_Changed_State iField to bFieldChanged
4351>>>>>>>            // Retain and remember may set field_changed_state to true even when empty. If this field is changed
4351>>>>>>>            // but its value is empty we assume it is a candidate for Null checking, so we will set field-changed to false
4351>>>>>>>            If bFieldChanged Begin
4353>>>>>>>                Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
4354>>>>>>>                Get IsEmptyField iField sValue to bEmpty
4355>>>>>>>                If bEmpty Begin
4357>>>>>>>                    Move False to bFieldChanged
4358>>>>>>>                End
4358>>>>>>>>
4358>>>>>>>            End
4358>>>>>>>>
4358>>>>>>>            If (not(bFieldChanged)) Begin
4360>>>>>>>                // we must find the child that points to this DD, starting with operation_origin. If a child
4360>>>>>>>                // is found, it will be in array position 1 (0 is self, 1 is child)
4360>>>>>>>                Get IsNullParentOrAncestor to bSkip
4361>>>>>>>            End
4361>>>>>>>>
4361>>>>>>>        End
4361>>>>>>>>
4361>>>>>>>        Function_Return bSkip
4362>>>>>>>    End_Function
4363>>>>>>>
4363>>>>>>>
4363>>>>>>>    // This will tell us if this DD can be treated as either a null parent
4363>>>>>>>    // or an ancestor of a null parent. This should only be called for a DD
4363>>>>>>>    // that is a candidate for this meaning that it does not have a change.
4363>>>>>>>    // We will test if its child allows this parent to be null or if this
4363>>>>>>>    // is in the path of an allowed null parent. We assume that parents of
4363>>>>>>>    // null parents will also be null. This is used to test if validations are
4363>>>>>>>    // needed.
4363>>>>>>>    Function IsNullParentOrAncestor Returns Boolean
4365>>>>>>>        Handle[] hoDDs
4366>>>>>>>        Integer i iSize iMain
4366>>>>>>>        Boolean bNullAllowed
4366>>>>>>>        // gets an array where 0 is self, 1 is parent, 2 is grandparent, and the
4366>>>>>>>        // last item is the operation_origin.
4366>>>>>>>        Send DDOServerPath of operation_origin Self (&hoDDs)
4367>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(hoDDs)) to iSize
4368>>>>>>>        If (iSize) Begin
4370>>>>>>>            // see if the immediate child allows this to be null.
4370>>>>>>>            Get Main_File to iMain
4371>>>>>>>            Get IsNullParentAllowed of hoDDs[1] iMain to bNullAllowed
4372>>>>>>>
4372>>>>>>>            // if null not allowed, see if this is an ancestor to a null allowed
4372>>>>>>>            // parent where all DDs in this path are unchanged. For example:
4372>>>>>>>            // G.DD <- P.DD <- C.DD where we C.DD allows P.DD to be null and we
4372>>>>>>>            // want to test if G.DD needs validation
4372>>>>>>>            Move 1 to i
4373>>>>>>>            While (not(bNullAllowed) and (i+1<iSize) and not(changed_state(hoDDs[i])) )
4377>>>>>>>                Get Main_File of hoDDs[i] to iMain
4378>>>>>>>                Get IsNullParentAllowed of hoDDs[i+1] iMain to bNullAllowed
4379>>>>>>>                Increment i
4380>>>>>>>            Loop
4381>>>>>>>>
4381>>>>>>>
4381>>>>>>>        End
4381>>>>>>>>
4381>>>>>>>        Function_Return bNullAllowed
4382>>>>>>>    End_Function
4383>>>>>>>
4383>>>>>>>
4383>>>>>>>    Function Validate_FindReq Integer iField Returns Integer
4385>>>>>>>        Integer bErr iOpts
4385>>>>>>>        // if no current record, we have not found the required record.
4385>>>>>>>        Move (not(HasRecord(Self))) to bErr
4386>>>>>>>        // We also need to check if the field is changed. If the field is changed and this
4386>>>>>>>        // is an autofind field, this indicates that an autofind was attempted and failed. We
4386>>>>>>>        // can't jut rely on current_record because a failed autofind restores the old current
4386>>>>>>>        // record. For this to work, DEOs must set the DD field's changed_state to true on
4386>>>>>>>        // no-put fields (dd_deomx.pkg was changed to do this).
4386>>>>>>>        If (not(bErr) and field_changed_state(Self,iField)) Begin
4388>>>>>>>            Get Field_Options iField to iOpts
4389>>>>>>>            Move ( ((iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND)=DD_AUTOFIND) or ;                ((iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND_GE)=DD_AUTOFIND_GE) ) ;                to bErr
4390>>>>>>>        End
4390>>>>>>>>
4390>>>>>>>        If bErr ;            Send Data_set_Error iField DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID ""
4393>>>>>>>        Function_Return bErr
4394>>>>>>>    End_Function
4395>>>>>>>
4395>>>>>>>    // This function will be called to validate a field.
4395>>>>>>>    // mark field currently being validated
4395>>>>>>>    // Altered to Check DD options (required, findreq)
4395>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field Integer iField Returns Integer
4397>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
4397>>>>>>>        Integer iMsg
4397>>>>>>>        Integer iObj
4397>>>>>>>        String  sValue
4397>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
4397>>>>>>>        Integer iOpts iMain
4397>>>>>>>        Boolean bSkipValidate
4397>>>>>>>        Handle[] hoDDs
4398>>>>>>>
4398>>>>>>>        Set Current_Validate_Field to iField
4399>>>>>>>
4399>>>>>>>        // test if we should skip validation on this field
4399>>>>>>>        Get SkipValidate iField to bSkipValidate
4400>>>>>>>
4400>>>>>>>        If (not(bSkipValidate)) Begin
4402>>>>>>>
4402>>>>>>>            Move (Record_Buffer(Self)) to iObj
4403>>>>>>>            Get Main_File to iFile
4404>>>>>>>
4404>>>>>>>            // Check for DD option failures: required, find_required
4404>>>>>>>            // "File_field" gets regular and foreign fields as needed
4404>>>>>>>            //Get File_Field_Options iFile iField to iOpts
4404>>>>>>>            Get Field_Options iField to iOpts  // get reg options
4405>>>>>>>            // if this is not the DDO that started the validation, we will assume that
4405>>>>>>>            // this is foreign. Operation_origin is set in Request_Validate
4405>>>>>>>            // If foreign (as defined above) and we do not allow new saves when
4405>>>>>>>            // foreign, we will consider this to be foreign and add foreign options
4405>>>>>>>            If (Operation_Origin<>Self and ;                Allow_Foreign_New_Save_State(Self)=0)  ;                Move (iOpts ior Foreign_Field_Options(Self, iField)) to iOpts
4408>>>>>>>
4408>>>>>>>
4408>>>>>>>            // Check for FindReq first. If it fails, set iResult to DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID so
4408>>>>>>>            // the calling function knows that a findreq failed. Always do this validation first
4408>>>>>>>            If (iOpts iand DD_FINDREQ) ;                Get Validate_FindReq  iField to iResult
4411>>>>>>>            If iResult Begin
4413>>>>>>>                Send AddDDHasFindReqError
4414>>>>>>>                Move DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID to iResult
4415>>>>>>>            End
4415>>>>>>>>
4415>>>>>>>            Else Begin
4416>>>>>>>
4416>>>>>>>                If (iOpts iand DD_REQUIRED) ;                    Get Validate_Required iField to iResult
4419>>>>>>>
4419>>>>>>>                If (iResult=0) Begin
4421>>>>>>>                    // First execute the user defined validation message
4421>>>>>>>                    Get Item_Validate_MSG of iObj iField to iMsg
4422>>>>>>>                    If iMsg Begin
4424>>>>>>>                        Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
4425>>>>>>>                        Get iMsg iField sValue to iResult
4426>>>>>>>                    End
4426>>>>>>>>
4426>>>>>>>                End
4426>>>>>>>>
4426>>>>>>>
4426>>>>>>>                // Check for keys
4426>>>>>>>                If (iResult=0 and Key_Field_State(Self, iField)) ;                    Get Validate_Key_Field iField to iResult
4429>>>>>>>
4429>>>>>>>                // Do extended validations
4429>>>>>>>                If (iResult=0) ;                    Get Validate_Field of (Field_Attributes(Self)) iField to iResult
4432>>>>>>>            End
4432>>>>>>>>
4432>>>>>>>        End
4432>>>>>>>>
4432>>>>>>>
4432>>>>>>>        Set Current_Validate_Field to 0
4433>>>>>>>        // Mark this field being validated
4433>>>>>>>        Get Visited_Fields to sValue
4434>>>>>>>        Set Visited_Fields to (Overstrike("X", sValue, iField))
4435>>>>>>>
4435>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
4436>>>>>>>
4436>>>>>>>    End_Function
4437>>>>>>>
4437>>>>>>>
4437>>>>>>>    // This function will be called to validate a field.
4437>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Validate_Field Integer iFile Integer iField Returns Integer
4439>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4439>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
4439>>>>>>>        Integer hOldOrigin
4439>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to iDSO
4440>>>>>>>        If not iDSO ;            Function_Return 0
4443>>>>>>>
4443>>>>>>>        // This function is only called by the DEOs.
4443>>>>>>>        // It is possible for validate_item when called as part of
4443>>>>>>>        // request_validate to get called more than once
4443>>>>>>>        // when a field is foreign (it is attached to both its DDO and the
4443>>>>>>>        // child-main ddo). This makes sure the validation is only called once.
4443>>>>>>>        // (vdf7 change: previously we set OpMode to Mode_Saving and checked that, now we have
4443>>>>>>>        // a mode just for request_validate).
4443>>>>>>>        If (Operation_Mode=MODE_VALIDATING and ;         // if from request_validate            Mid(Visited_Fields(iDSO), 1, iField)="X" ) ; // and already marked            Function_Return 0                         // skip it
4446>>>>>>>
4446>>>>>>>        Move Operation_origin to hOldOrigin
4447>>>>>>>
4447>>>>>>>        // if from request_validate operation_origin will be set and should not
4447>>>>>>>        // be reset here.
4447>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN=0) Begin
4449>>>>>>>            Move Self to Operation_Origin
4450>>>>>>>        End
4450>>>>>>>>
4450>>>>>>>
4450>>>>>>>        Get Validate_Field of iDSO iField to iResult
4451>>>>>>>        Move hOldOrigin to Operation_Origin
4452>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
4453>>>>>>>    End_Function
4454>>>>>>>
4454>>>>>>>    // This function will be called to check if a key has been changed.
4454>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Key_Field Integer iField Returns Integer
4456>>>>>>>        String  sOld_Value
4456>>>>>>>        String  sNew_Value
4456>>>>>>>        String  sKeys
4456>>>>>>>        Integer iState
4456>>>>>>>        Boolean bMultiKeys
4456>>>>>>>        Get Protect_Key_State to iState
4457>>>>>>>        If iState Begin
4459>>>>>>>            Get Key_Value to sNew_Value
4460>>>>>>>            // Only check existing records.
4460>>>>>>>            If (HasRecord(Self)) Begin
4462>>>>>>>                Get Existing_Key_Value to sOld_Value
4463>>>>>>>                If (sNew_Value <> sOld_Value) Begin
4465>>>>>>>                    // we have an error. If there is only one key field we know
4465>>>>>>>                    // where the field is and we can report that field. If we have
4465>>>>>>>                    // multiple key fields, we don't really know where the offending key change
4465>>>>>>>                    // is, so we will not report a field.
4465>>>>>>>                    Get Key_Fields to sKeys
4466>>>>>>>                    Move (Pos("X",sKeys)<>RightPos("X",sKeys)) to bMultiKeys
4467>>>>>>>                    Send Data_set_Error (If(bMultiKeys, -1, iField)) 0 DD_TEXT_NO_KEY_CHANGE_ALLOWED
4468>>>>>>>                    Function_Return 1
4469>>>>>>>                End
4469>>>>>>>>
4469>>>>>>>            End
4469>>>>>>>>
4469>>>>>>>        End
4469>>>>>>>>
4469>>>>>>>    End_Function
4470>>>>>>>
4470>>>>>>>
4470>>>>>>>    // During request_validate process tell us if this DD has had a find_request error. This
4470>>>>>>>    // is handled by the DD that originated the request_validate. Very private
4470>>>>>>>    Function DDHasFindReqError Returns Boolean
4472>>>>>>>        Handle[] DDsWithFindReqErrors
4473>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
4473>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin
4475>>>>>>>            Get pDDsWithFindReqErrors of OPERATION_ORIGIN to DDsWithFindReqErrors
4476>>>>>>>            Move (SearchArray(Self,DDsWithFindReqErrors)) to iIndex
4477>>>>>>>            Function_Return (iIndex<>-1)
4478>>>>>>>        End
4478>>>>>>>>
4478>>>>>>>    End_Function
4479>>>>>>>
4479>>>>>>>    // During a request_validate a find_request error has occurred. Add this DD
4479>>>>>>>    // to list of DDs that have this error. This is handled by the DD that
4479>>>>>>>    // originated the request_validate.  Very private
4479>>>>>>>    Procedure AddDDHasFindReqError
4481>>>>>>>        Handle[] DDsWithFindReqErrors
4482>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin
4484>>>>>>>            Get pDDsWithFindReqErrors of OPERATION_ORIGIN to DDsWithFindReqErrors
4485>>>>>>>            Move Self to DDsWithFindReqErrors[SizeOfArray(DDsWithFindReqErrors)]
4486>>>>>>>            Set pDDsWithFindReqErrors of OPERATION_ORIGIN to DDsWithFindReqErrors
4487>>>>>>>        End
4487>>>>>>>>
4487>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4488>>>>>>>
4488>>>>>>>    // This function will execute the validation message for each field of the
4488>>>>>>>    // data set and all of its parents in parent first order.
4488>>>>>>>    // Pass: DoALLFg bNoStop
4488>>>>>>>    // Added bNoStop, If true, all items are validated. It is up to you to
4488>>>>>>>    // do something with the possible cascade of errors
4488>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Data_Sets Integer DoAllFg Integer bNoStop Returns Integer
4490>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4490>>>>>>>        Integer iRetval
4490>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
4490>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
4490>>>>>>>        Integer bErr
4490>>>>>>>        Boolean bDDHasFindReqError
4490>>>>>>>        // ShowLn "Validate_Data_Sets in Data_Set in " (Name(self))
4490>>>>>>>        // Validate if not foreign, or foreign new saves allowed, or
4490>>>>>>>        // foreign validation is supported (it normally is)
4490>>>>>>>        If (Operation_Origin=Self or ;            Allow_Foreign_New_Save_State(Self) or ;            Validate_Foreign_File_State(Self)) Begin
4492>>>>>>>
4492>>>>>>>            If (bNoStop) Begin
4494>>>>>>>                // if do all, it is possible that this DD as a find-req error. If so there is no
4494>>>>>>>                // need to look for more errors in this DD or its parents. This makes the do all checking
4494>>>>>>>                // a little more intelligent and doesn't return a bunch of errors when it is not needed
4494>>>>>>>                Get DDHasFindReqError to bDDHasFindReqError
4495>>>>>>>            End
4495>>>>>>>>
4495>>>>>>>
4495>>>>>>>            If (not(bDDHasFindReqError)) Begin
4497>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4498>>>>>>>                Decrement iMax
4499>>>>>>>                For iCount from 0 to iMax
4505>>>>>>>>
4505>>>>>>>                    Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
4506>>>>>>>                    If not (Visited_state(iDSO)) Begin
4508>>>>>>>                        Get Validate_Data_Sets of iDSO DoAllFg bNoStop to bErr
4509>>>>>>>                        If bErr Begin
4511>>>>>>>                            Move bErr to iRetVal
4512>>>>>>>                            If bNoStop ;                                Move 0 to bErr
4515>>>>>>>                        End
4515>>>>>>>>
4515>>>>>>>                    End
4515>>>>>>>>
4515>>>>>>>                Until bErr
4517>>>>>>>                If not bErr Begin
4519>>>>>>>                    Get Validate_Fields DoAllFg bNoStop to bErr
4520>>>>>>>                    If bErr ;                        Move bErr to iRetVal
4523>>>>>>>                End
4523>>>>>>>>
4523>>>>>>>            End
4523>>>>>>>>
4523>>>>>>>        End
4523>>>>>>>>
4523>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
4524>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
4525>>>>>>>    End_Function
4526>>>>>>>
4526>>>>>>>    // This tests the DDO and all "up" DDOs to see if a switched parent / commit test even needs to be
4526>>>>>>>    // tested. This is called by the top ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents to see if a switch parent test
4526>>>>>>>    // even needs to be applied before it has to refinds records.
4526>>>>>>>    // Return true is there is nothing to test (i.e., the shortcut worked).
4526>>>>>>>    Function IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed Returns Boolean
4528>>>>>>>        Boolean bAllowed bCommitted bVisited bHasRecord
4528>>>>>>>        Integer iServers iSrvr iParent
4528>>>>>>>        Handle hoSrvr
4528>>>>>>>
4528>>>>>>>
4528>>>>>>>        // optimization. We only test committed parents if one parent does not allow changing committed records.
4528>>>>>>>        // This avoids extra finds and relates when not needed
4528>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
4529>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iServers
4530>>>>>>>        Get IsCommitted to bCommitted
4531>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iSrvr
4532>>>>>>>        Move True to bAllowed
4533>>>>>>>        While (iSrvr<iServers and bAllowed)
4537>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iSrvr to hoSrvr
4538>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoSrvr to iParent
4539>>>>>>>            // if committed and parent change not allowed, we are done
4539>>>>>>>            If (bCommitted) Begin
4541>>>>>>>                Get IsCommittedParentChangeAllowed iParent to bAllowed
4542>>>>>>>            End
4542>>>>>>>>
4542>>>>>>>            // if still allowed, check all parents
4542>>>>>>>            If (bAllowed) Begin
4544>>>>>>>                Get Visited_State of hoSrvr to bVisited
4545>>>>>>>                If not bVisited Begin
4547>>>>>>>                    Get IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed of hoSrvr to bAllowed
4548>>>>>>>                End
4548>>>>>>>>
4548>>>>>>>            End
4548>>>>>>>>
4548>>>>>>>            Increment iSrvr
4549>>>>>>>        Loop
4550>>>>>>>>
4550>>>>>>>        Function_Return bAllowed
4551>>>>>>>    End_Function
4552>>>>>>>
4552>>>>>>>
4552>>>>>>>    // special validate-save check for changed committed parent. If the record is committed
4552>>>>>>>    // and it has a switched parent and this is not allowed, we have an error. This should rarely happen because the
4552>>>>>>>    // DEOs should guard aginst this. This is a recursive routine that requires special attention the first time through.
4552>>>>>>>    // When called from the we must refind the original record and all original parents. This way we can compare these parent
4552>>>>>>>    // rowids to the DD row id (if different, they've changed). At the end we must restore the DD records. Because this takes time
4552>>>>>>>    // we only even do this if this is committed and there is a chance that there are changed parents
4552>>>>>>>
4552>>>>>>>    Function ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents Boolean bTop Returns Boolean
4554>>>>>>>        Integer iServers iSrvr iMain iParent iPMain
4554>>>>>>>        Handle hoSrvr
4554>>>>>>>        RowID riCrnt riParent riPCrnt
4554>>>>>>>        Boolean bChanged bCommitted bAllowed bErr bParentChanged bVisited
4554>>>>>>>        Boolean bHasRecord bPHasRecord bFound
4554>>>>>>>
4554>>>>>>>
4554>>>>>>>        // Shortcut optimization. This tests for any committed DDO with a parent that doesn't allow a switch
4554>>>>>>>        // return true if there is any reason to actually test any DDO up the tree for a parent change
4554>>>>>>>        If bTop Begin
4556>>>>>>>            // init visited nodes, these will be tested and set in IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed
4556>>>>>>>            Send Initialize_Visited False False //false=up only, true=clear fields
4557>>>>>>>            Get IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed to bAllowed
4558>>>>>>>            If bAllowed Begin
4560>>>>>>>                Function_Return False // if all are allowed, we have nothing to test - its ok
4561>>>>>>>            End
4561>>>>>>>>
4561>>>>>>>        End
4561>>>>>>>>
4561>>>>>>>
4561>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
4562>>>>>>>        Get CurrentRowId to riCrnt
4563>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iServers
4564>>>>>>>        Get HasRecord to bHasRecord
4565>>>>>>>
4565>>>>>>>        If (bHasRecord and (bTop or not(IsSameRowID(GetRowID(iMain),riCrnt))) ) Begin
4567>>>>>>>            // this refinds the main record and, most importantly, relates all original parents on up
4567>>>>>>>            // We now have the original parents which we can test to see if they are changed.
4567>>>>>>>            Get ReadByRowIdEx iMain riCrnt to bFound
4568>>>>>>>            If not bFound Begin
4570>>>>>>>                Error DFERR_CANT_REFIND_RECORD
4571>>>>>>>>
4571>>>>>>>                Function_Return True
4572>>>>>>>            End
4572>>>>>>>>
4572>>>>>>>        End
4572>>>>>>>>
4572>>>>>>>
4572>>>>>>>        If (bTop) Begin
4574>>>>>>>            // If at start, init visited nodes, these will be tested and set during recursive calls to this function
4574>>>>>>>            Send Initialize_Visited False False // false=up only, true=clear fields
4575>>>>>>>        End
4575>>>>>>>>
4575>>>>>>>
4575>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
4576>>>>>>>        Get IsCommitted to bCommitted
4577>>>>>>>        If bCommitted Begin
4579>>>>>>>            // Parent_Changed_State tells us a parent is changed but not which one. Look at each child to see if it is changed.
4579>>>>>>>            // First see any any of the parents are changed.
4579>>>>>>>            Get Parent_Changed_State to bChanged
4580>>>>>>>            If bChanged Begin
4582>>>>>>>                // Parent_Changed_State tells us a parent is changed but not which one. Look at each child to see if it is changed.
4582>>>>>>>                Move 0 to iSrvr
4583>>>>>>>                While (iSrvr<iServers and not(bErr))
4587>>>>>>>                    Get Data_Set_Server iSrvr to hoSrvr
4588>>>>>>>                    Get Main_File of hoSrvr to iParent
4589>>>>>>>                    Get CurrentRowId of hoSrvr to riParent
4590>>>>>>>                    Move (not(IsSameRowID(GetRowID(iParent),riParent))) to bParentChanged // is parent changed?
4591>>>>>>>                    If bParentChanged Begin
4593>>>>>>>                        Get IsCommittedParentChangeAllowed iParent to bAllowed // is changing committed parent allowed?
4594>>>>>>>                        If not bAllowed Begin
4596>>>>>>>                            Move True to bErr
4597>>>>>>>                            If bErr Begin
4599>>>>>>>                                Send Data_Set_Error of hoSrvr -1 0 DD_CANNOT_SWITCH_PARENT
4600>>>>>>>                            End
4600>>>>>>>>
4600>>>>>>>                        End
4600>>>>>>>>
4600>>>>>>>                    End
4600>>>>>>>>
4600>>>>>>>                    Increment iSrvr
4601>>>>>>>                Loop
4602>>>>>>>>
4602>>>>>>>            End
4602>>>>>>>>
4602>>>>>>>        End
4602>>>>>>>>
4602>>>>>>>
4602>>>>>>>        // no error in immediate we must continue this check up the parent tree.
4602>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iSrvr
4603>>>>>>>        While (iSrvr<iServers and not(bErr))
4607>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iSrvr to hoSrvr
4608>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoSrvr to bVisited
4609>>>>>>>            If (not(bVisited)) Begin
4611>>>>>>>
4611>>>>>>>                // if new record, we need to refind parent records from here since you cannot
4611>>>>>>>                // have done a find/relate on a new record.
4611>>>>>>>                If (not(bHasRecord)) Begin
4613>>>>>>>                    Get HasRecord of hoSrvr to bPHasRecord
4614>>>>>>>                    If (bPHasRecord) Begin
4616>>>>>>>                        Get Main_File of hoSrvr to iPMain
4617>>>>>>>                        Get CurrentRowId of hoSrvr to riPCrnt
4618>>>>>>>                        If (not(IsNullRowID(riPCrnt))) Begin
4620>>>>>>>                            Get ReadByRowIdEx of hoSrvr iPMain riPCrnt to bFound
4621>>>>>>>                            If not bFound Begin
4623>>>>>>>                                Error DFERR_CANT_REFIND_RECORD
4624>>>>>>>>
4624>>>>>>>                                Function_Return True
4625>>>>>>>                            End
4625>>>>>>>>
4625>>>>>>>                        End
4625>>>>>>>>
4625>>>>>>>                    End
4625>>>>>>>>
4625>>>>>>>                End
4625>>>>>>>>
4625>>>>>>>
4625>>>>>>>                Get ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents of hoSrvr False to bErr // call recursively up the parent tree
4626>>>>>>>            End
4626>>>>>>>>
4626>>>>>>>            Increment iSrvr
4627>>>>>>>        Loop
4628>>>>>>>>
4628>>>>>>>
4628>>>>>>>        If bTop Begin // if back to the top, make sure our buffers are correct.
4630>>>>>>>            Send Refind_Records
4631>>>>>>>        End
4631>>>>>>>>
4631>>>>>>>
4631>>>>>>>        Function_Return bErr
4632>>>>>>>    End_Function
4633>>>>>>>
4633>>>>>>>    Procedure Entry_Update_Data_Sets Integer iFile Integer iAll
4635>>>>>>>
4635>>>>>>>        Handle hoBuff hoDSO
4635>>>>>>>        Boolean bCommit bIsFind bVisited bIsForeign
4635>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount iItems iOpts iChanges
4635>>>>>>>
4635>>>>>>>
4635>>>>>>>        Move record_buffer to hoBuff
4636>>>>>>>        Move (OPERATION_MODE<>MODE_SAVING) to bIsFind
4637>>>>>>>
4637>>>>>>>        // first recurse to all parent ddos
4637>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4638>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4639>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4645>>>>>>>>
4645>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoDSO
4646>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoDSO to bVisited
4647>>>>>>>            If not (bVisited) Begin
4649>>>>>>>                Send Entry_Update_Data_Sets to hoDSO iFile iAll
4650>>>>>>>            End
4650>>>>>>>>
4650>>>>>>>        Loop
4651>>>>>>>>
4651>>>>>>>
4651>>>>>>>        // if find, we only do this if the main file is the same as the find file
4651>>>>>>>        If (not(bIsFind) or iFile=Main_File(Self)) Begin
4653>>>>>>>            If (not(bIsFind)) Begin
4655>>>>>>>                // if a save, we care if it is committed.
4655>>>>>>>                Get IsCommitted to bCommit
4656>>>>>>>            End
4656>>>>>>>>
4656>>>>>>>
4656>>>>>>>            // pass if Find (True) or save (False). We only care about commit on saves
4656>>>>>>>            // The setting of bIsForeign is an approximation. Foreign is really a DEO and and not
4656>>>>>>>            // a DD concept - in fact, at this point we don't really know. For example, a save in a header/dtl
4656>>>>>>>            // detail DEO (ordrdtl grid)has header DEOs that are not really foreign. This test errs on the side
4656>>>>>>>            // of assuming it's foreign. This would cause problems with incorrect parent NoPuts except we also
4656>>>>>>>            // set a flag, Field_NoPutValueChangedByDeo, when a field is changed via a NoPut DEO. The DD will still update
4656>>>>>>>            // foreign NoPuts unless this field flag is set.
4656>>>>>>>            Move (OPERATION_ORIGIN<>Self and Allow_Foreign_New_Save_State(Self)=0) to bIsForeign
4657>>>>>>>            Send Entry_Update of hoBuff bIsFind (If(bCommit,1,0) + If(bIsForeign,2,0))
4658>>>>>>>
4658>>>>>>>            // also move data from extended dd fields to buffer
4658>>>>>>>            Send ExtendedFieldsUpdate (not(bIsFind))
4659>>>>>>>        End
4659>>>>>>>>
4659>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
4660>>>>>>>
4660>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4661>>>>>>>
4661>>>>>>>    // is this field NoPut based passed Commit and Foreign flags.
4661>>>>>>>    Function FieldNoPut Integer iField Boolean bIsCommited Boolean bIsForeign Returns Boolean
4663>>>>>>>        Boolean bNoPut
4663>>>>>>>        // this uses runtime logic - the same use for moving DD Buffer to Field Buffer
4663>>>>>>>        Get IsFieldDDNoPut of Record_Buffer iField (If(bIsCommited,1,0) + If(bIsForeign,2,0)) to bNoPut
4664>>>>>>>        Function_Return bNoPut
4665>>>>>>>    End_Function
4666>>>>>>>
4666>>>>>>>
4666>>>>>>>    // Check that Server data-sets exist for all required server file numbers
4666>>>>>>>    Function Valid_Servers Returns Integer
4668>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
4668>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
4668>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
4668>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4668>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
4668>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
4668>>>>>>>        String  sFiles
4668>>>>>>>
4668>>>>>>>        // First assemble a string of all server file#s in ','##',' format
4668>>>>>>>        Move ',' to sFiles
4669>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4670>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4671>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4677>>>>>>>>
4677>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
4678>>>>>>>            Move ( sFiles + String(Main_file(iDSO)) + ",") to sFiles
4679>>>>>>>        Loop
4680>>>>>>>>
4680>>>>>>>
4680>>>>>>>        // Make sure each required File exists
4680>>>>>>>        Get Server_File_Count to iMax
4681>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4682>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4688>>>>>>>>
4688>>>>>>>            Get Server_File iCount to iFile
4689>>>>>>>            Move (Pos ( ','+String(iFile)+',' , sFiles)) to iPos
4690>>>>>>>            If (iPos = 0) ;                Move iFile to iRVal
4693>>>>>>>        Until iRval
4695>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
4696>>>>>>>    End_Function
4697>>>>>>>
4697>>>>>>>
4697>>>>>>>    // Check that Client data-sets exist for all required Client file numbers
4697>>>>>>>    Function Valid_Clients Returns Integer
4699>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
4699>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
4699>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
4699>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
4699>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
4699>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
4699>>>>>>>        String  sFiles
4699>>>>>>>
4699>>>>>>>        // First assemble a string of all Client file#s in ','##',' format
4699>>>>>>>        Move ',' to sFiles
4700>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
4701>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4702>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4708>>>>>>>>
4708>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
4709>>>>>>>            Move ( sFiles + String(Main_file(iDSO))+",") to sFiles
4710>>>>>>>        Loop
4711>>>>>>>>
4711>>>>>>>
4711>>>>>>>        // Make sure each required File exists
4711>>>>>>>        Get Client_File_Count to iMax
4712>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4713>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4719>>>>>>>>
4719>>>>>>>            Get Client_File iCount to iFile
4720>>>>>>>            Move (Pos( ','+String(iFile)+',', sFiles)) to iPos
4721>>>>>>>            If (iPos = 0) ;                Move iFile to iRVal
4724>>>>>>>        Until iRval
4726>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
4727>>>>>>>    End_Function
4728>>>>>>>
4728>>>>>>>
4728>>>>>>>    // Validates save updating connections. If error returns file# that is
4728>>>>>>>    // expected and missing. If no error Set Validated_Save_connectio_State
4728>>>>>>>    // indicating that the connection validation has occurred and is ok
4728>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Save_Structure Integer ForceFg Returns Integer
4730>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
4730>>>>>>>        Integer iMode
4730>>>>>>>        If not ForceFg Begin
4732>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Save_Structure_Mode to iMode
4733>>>>>>>            Move ( iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ALWAYS or ;                (iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ONCE and ;                Save_Structure_Validated_state(Self)=0 ) ) ;                to ForceFg
4734>>>>>>>        End
4734>>>>>>>>
4734>>>>>>>        If ForceFg Begin
4736>>>>>>>            Get Valid_Structure False to iRval
4737>>>>>>>            If (iRVal = 0) ;                Set Save_Structure_Validated_State to True
4740>>>>>>>        End
4740>>>>>>>>
4740>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
4741>>>>>>>    End_Function
4742>>>>>>>
4742>>>>>>>    // Validates Delete Structure. If cascade_state is true this must check
4742>>>>>>>    // up and down the tree. If no cascade_state just check up the tree.  If
4742>>>>>>>    // Ok, set Validated_Delete_no_Cascade_Connection_State and and or
4742>>>>>>>    // Validated_Delete_Cascade_Connection_State
4742>>>>>>>    // Pass: ForceFg - if TRUE force the validation.
4742>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Delete_Structure Integer ForceFg Returns Integer
4744>>>>>>>        Integer iCascade
4744>>>>>>>        Integer iMode
4744>>>>>>>        Integer iSt
4744>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
4744>>>>>>>        Get Cascade_delete_State to iCascade
4745>>>>>>>        If not ForceFg Begin
4747>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Delete_Structure_Mode to iMode
4748>>>>>>>            If (iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ONCE and iCascade );                Get Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_state to iSt
4751>>>>>>>            Else ;                Get No_Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_state to iSt
4753>>>>>>>            Move ( iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ALWAYS or ;                (iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ONCE and iSt=0) ) to ForceFg
4754>>>>>>>        End
4754>>>>>>>>
4754>>>>>>>
4754>>>>>>>        If ForceFg Begin
4756>>>>>>>            Get Valid_Structure iCascade to iRval
4757>>>>>>>            If (iRval = 0) Begin
4759>>>>>>>                Set No_Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_State to True
4760>>>>>>>                If iCascade ;                    Set Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_State to True
4763>>>>>>>            End
4763>>>>>>>>
4763>>>>>>>        End
4763>>>>>>>>
4763>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRval
4764>>>>>>>    End_Function
4765>>>>>>>
4765>>>>>>>
4765>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called whenever the Data_Set wants its DEOs to
4765>>>>>>>    // write their values to the record buffer. The value of OPERATION_MODE
4765>>>>>>>    // determines if this is for finding an record or before saving a record.
4765>>>>>>>    // We use this event to tell our Record_Buffer to update the
4765>>>>>>>    // global record buffer.
4765>>>>>>>    // Modified to visit all server DSOs
4765>>>>>>>    // Note that this is only sent to the DSO starting the operation.
4765>>>>>>>    // We must manually send this to all server data-sets ourselves
4765>>>>>>>    // Note that during a DSO save this will get passed iFile=0 and iAll=3
4765>>>>>>>    // Changed to Support EntryUpdateLocalState (private)
4765>>>>>>>    // as of 17.0, EntryUpdateLocalState is True which means that entry_updates
4765>>>>>>>    // for finds now through the DD Buffer (saves always did).
4765>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Entry_Update Integer iFile Integer iAll
4767>>>>>>>        If ((Operation_Mode=MODE_SAVING and iAll=3) or (EntryUpdateLocalState(Self)) ) Begin //3=dso save
4769>>>>>>>            If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
4771>>>>>>>                // we will only not be in an operation if we are doing a find with EntryUpdateLocalState
4771>>>>>>>                // set to true. In such a case make this a finding. I am not this is actually needed
4771>>>>>>>                Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_FINDING
4772>>>>>>>            End
4772>>>>>>>>
4772>>>>>>>            Else Begin
4773>>>>>>>                // if here we already have an operation_mode so there is no need to do anything special
4773>>>>>>>                Send Update_Focus_Field // Make sure buffer has latest focus item changes
4774>>>>>>>            End
4774>>>>>>>>
4774>>>>>>>            Send Initialize_Visited False False // Clear up, do not clear fields
4775>>>>>>>            Send Entry_Update_Data_Sets iFile iAll
4776>>>>>>>        End
4776>>>>>>>>
4776>>>>>>>        Forward Send Request_Entry_Update iFile iAll
4778>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4779>>>>>>>
4779>>>>>>>
4779>>>>>>>
4779>>>>>>>    // Forces the focus field to get update its value with the data-set.
4779>>>>>>>    // This insures that the DSO and DEO contain the same values.
4779>>>>>>>    Procedure Update_Focus_Field
4781>>>>>>>        Integer iFocObj
4781>>>>>>>        Get Focus of desktop to iFocObj
4782>>>>>>>        If (Extended_DEO_State(iFocObj)) ;            Send Update_Focus_Field to iFocObj
4785>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4786>>>>>>>
4786>>>>>>>    // very internal. Used to set Operation_mode and Operation_origin before the
4786>>>>>>>    // update. A developer can use this in the DEO to know what state the update is in.
4786>>>>>>>    // This was created because a DEO value change will trigger an OnChange event and you
4786>>>>>>>    // can look at this and know that this is part of a DD operation.
4786>>>>>>>    // This is *only* called by the DD operations in this class and the change is made for as
4786>>>>>>>    // small of a period as possible.
4786>>>>>>>    Procedure Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation Integer iOperationMode
4788>>>>>>>        Integer iOldMode iOldOrigin
4788>>>>>>>
4788>>>>>>>        Move OPERATION_MODE to iOldMode
4789>>>>>>>        Move OPERATION_ORIGIN to iOldOrigin
4790>>>>>>>        Move iOperationMode to OPERATION_MODE
4791>>>>>>>        Move Self to OPERATION_ORIGIN
4792>>>>>>>        Send Update_Focus_Field
4793>>>>>>>        Move iOldMode to OPERATION_MODE
4794>>>>>>>        Move iOldOrigin to OPERATION_ORIGIN
4795>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4796>>>>>>>
4796>>>>>>>
4796>>>>>>>    // Augment to validate all field values that do not get
4796>>>>>>>    // validated as part of the item validation process. The advantage
4796>>>>>>>    // of item validation (over only field validation) is that an error
4796>>>>>>>    // returns you to the offending item.
4796>>>>>>>    Function Request_Validate Returns Integer
4798>>>>>>>        Integer iRetval iOldOrigin iOldMode iRetVal2
4798>>>>>>>        Handle[] DDsWithFindReqErrors
4799>>>>>>>
4799>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
4801>>>>>>>            Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_VALIDATING // added 12.1/15.1
4802>>>>>>>        End
4802>>>>>>>>
4802>>>>>>>        Move Operation_Origin to iOldOrigin
4803>>>>>>>        Move Self to Operation_Origin
4804>>>>>>>        Move Operation_Mode to iOldMode
4805>>>>>>>        // clear all find req DD markers at the origin of the validate request. When request validates occur
4805>>>>>>>        // they will get added to this array and can be tested to see of such an error has occurred.
4805>>>>>>>        Set pDDsWithFindReqErrors to DDsWithFindReqErrors
4806>>>>>>>        // Prior to VDF7, we set this to Mode_Saving. We now have a special mode just for request_validate.
4806>>>>>>>        // We do this because:
4806>>>>>>>        //   1) because it is useful (more detail never hurts) and
4806>>>>>>>        //   2) we will allow set_field_current_value to update when mode_validation is set
4806>>>>>>>        Move MODE_VALIDATING to Operation_Mode
4807>>>>>>>        Send Initialize_Visited False True //false=up only, true=clear fields
4808>>>>>>>        Forward Get Request_Validate to iRetval // normal deo validate
4810>>>>>>>        // If DEO validation failed, do not validate other fields unless Validate_All_Fields is set
4810>>>>>>>        If ( (iRetval=0 or (Validate_All_Fields_State(Self))) and Validate_DEOs_Only_State(Self)=0) Begin
4812>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Data_Sets False (Validate_All_Fields_State(Self)) to iRetval2
4813>>>>>>>            Move (iRetval or iRetVal2) to iRetval
4814>>>>>>>        End
4814>>>>>>>>
4814>>>>>>>
4814>>>>>>>        If (iRetval=0) Begin
4816>>>>>>>            Get ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents True to iRetval
4817>>>>>>>        End
4817>>>>>>>>
4817>>>>>>>
4817>>>>>>>        Move iOldMode   to Operation_Mode
4818>>>>>>>        Move iOldOrigin to Operation_Origin
4819>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
4820>>>>>>>    End_Function
4821>>>>>>>
4821>>>>>>>    Function Request_Validate_All Returns Integer
4823>>>>>>>        Integer bOld iRetVal
4823>>>>>>>        Get Validate_All_Fields_State to bOld
4824>>>>>>>        Set Validate_All_Fields_State to True
4825>>>>>>>        Get request_validate to iretVal
4826>>>>>>>        Set Validate_All_Fields_State to bOld
4827>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
4828>>>>>>>    End_Function
4829>>>>>>>
4829>>>>>>>
4829>>>>>>>
4829>>>>>>>    // Like Item_find except entry-update is forced through the DD, not DEO
4829>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_Find Integer iFindMode Integer iFile Integer iField ;            Integer bEntUpdt  Integer bShowErr Integer bDfrd
4831>>>>>>>        Integer bOld
4831>>>>>>>        Get EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
4832>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to True
4833>>>>>>>        Send Item_Find iFindMode iFile iField bEntUpdt bShowErr bDfrd
4834>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
4835>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4836>>>>>>>
4836>>>>>>>    // Autofind for requestd file, field and mode.
4836>>>>>>>    //    If mode not passed, EQ is assummed
4836>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_AutoFind Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iFindMode
4838>>>>>>>        Integer eMode
4838>>>>>>>        If iFile  Begin
4840>>>>>>>            // if no 3rd argument, default to autofind
4840>>>>>>>            Move (If(Num_Arguments<3,EQ,iFindMode)) to eMode
4841>>>>>>>            Send File_Field_Find eMode iFile iField True False False
4842>>>>>>>        End
4842>>>>>>>>
4842>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4843>>>>>>>
4843>>>>>>>    // Autofind in default mode (does not set changed states). Can be used
4843>>>>>>>    // within Clear and Clear_all to autofind parents. Parent values can be
4843>>>>>>>    // maintained using retainAll option
4843>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_Default_AutoFind Integer iFile Integer iField
4845>>>>>>>        Integer iOldState
4845>>>>>>>        Handle  hoDD
4845>>>>>>>        Get Data_set iFile to hoDD
4846>>>>>>>        If hoDD Begin
4848>>>>>>>            Get Change_disabled_State of hoDD to iOldState
4849>>>>>>>            Set Change_disabled_State of hoDD to True
4850>>>>>>>            Send File_Field_AutoFind  of hoDD iFile iField EQ
4851>>>>>>>            Set Change_disabled_State of hoDD to iOldState
4852>>>>>>>            Set changed_state to False
4853>>>>>>>        End
4853>>>>>>>>
4853>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4854>>>>>>>
4854>>>>>>>    // File_Index_find
4854>>>>>>>    // Like item_find except you pass the index you want to find with and
4854>>>>>>>    // ent-update occurs through DDO buffers not deo buffers.
4854>>>>>>>    // This is currently private and is only used by web-applications
4854>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Index_Find Integer iFindMode Integer iFile Integer iIndex ;            Integer bEntUpdt  Integer bShowErr Integer bDfrd
4856>>>>>>>        Integer bOld
4856>>>>>>>        RowID riRec
4856>>>>>>>        Integer wasChanged hDD iOldStat
4856>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk
4856>>>>>>>
4856>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to hDD
4857>>>>>>>        If (hDD=0) Begin
4859>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM C_$CannotFindDD
4860>>>>>>>>
4860>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
4861>>>>>>>        End
4861>>>>>>>>
4861>>>>>>>
4861>>>>>>>        Get EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
4862>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to True
4863>>>>>>>
4863>>>>>>>        //  'hold' buffer to prepare for entry_update
4863>>>>>>>        Move (getRowId(iFile)) to riRec
4864>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_STATUS of iFile to iOldStat
4867>>>>>>>        Set_Attribute DF_FILE_STATUS of iFile to DF_FILE_INACTIVE
4870>>>>>>>
4870>>>>>>>        If bEntUpdt Begin
4872>>>>>>>            Send Request_Entry_Update to hDD iFile 1  //entUpdt all DEOs as required
4873>>>>>>>
4873>>>>>>>            //
4873>>>>>>>            // we really only need to know if any segment of the index changed
4873>>>>>>>            // but since we don't have field-changed flags, we look at the
4873>>>>>>>            // whole recbuf - this is consistent with 2.3b and 3.0 non-dataset
4873>>>>>>>            // behavior.
4873>>>>>>>            //
4873>>>>>>>            Move (iOldStat<>DF_FILE_INACTIVE) to wasChanged
4874>>>>>>>            If not wasChanged ;                Get_Attribute DF_FILE_CHANGED of iFile to wasChanged
4879>>>>>>>            If not wasChanged ;                Constrained_Clear iFindMode iFile by iIndex
4884>>>>>>>
4884>>>>>>>        End
4884>>>>>>>>
4884>>>>>>>        Move False to Err
4885>>>>>>>        If bDfrd ;            Send Request_Read iFindMode iFile iIndex
4888>>>>>>>        Else ;            Send Request_Find iFindMode iFile iIndex
4890>>>>>>>        If (not(Found) and  not(err)) Begin
4892>>>>>>>            // refind original record (or leave it cleared if not record)
4892>>>>>>>            Move (FindByRowId(iFile,riRec)) to bOk
4893>>>>>>>
4893>>>>>>>            If bShowErr ;                Error (If(iFindMode<2, DFERR_FIND_PRIOR_BEG_OF_FILE, DFERR_FIND_PAST_END_OF_FILE))
4896>>>>>>>            Move False to Err
4897>>>>>>>        End
4897>>>>>>>>
4897>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
4898>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4899>>>>>>>
4899>>>>>>>    // This does a refind of all records based on the contents of the
4899>>>>>>>    // refine_record_id property.
4899>>>>>>>    // This would be used after clearing the DDs and loading the local rencum
4899>>>>>>>    // buffer with recnums. This can be used by remote DEOs (BPOs).
4899>>>>>>>    //
4899>>>>>>>    // Find all existing records. This must be done in bottom-up, breadth
4899>>>>>>>    // first order. i.e., Start with the passed DD, find it and then find for
4899>>>>>>>    // parents. Only find if the record is non-zero and it is different than
4899>>>>>>>    // the current_record.
4899>>>>>>>    // This order will allow us to support changed parents.
4899>>>>>>>    // Don't use this if you do not understand what it does.
4899>>>>>>>    // Private.Find_Records is a helper. We will keep this private because
4899>>>>>>>    // it is rather specialized and only used by WebApp.
4899>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Records
4901>>>>>>>        Send Initialize_Visited False False // Clear up, do not clear fields
4902>>>>>>>        Send Private.Find_Records           // refind all records in upward sweep
4903>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4904>>>>>>>
4904>>>>>>>
4904>>>>>>>    Procedure Private.Find_Records
4906>>>>>>>        Integer hPrnt
4906>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
4906>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
4906>>>>>>>        RowID riRec
4906>>>>>>>        Integer iRec iMain
4906>>>>>>>        // works with both recId and rowId. Only one should ever be set.
4906>>>>>>>        // find(clear) record, if needed
4906>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
4907>>>>>>>        // assume that either prFindRowId or Find_record_id has a value - never both
4907>>>>>>>        // also assume Find_record_id only has values when you are using a recnum table
4907>>>>>>>        Get prFindRowId to riRec
4908>>>>>>>        If not (IsNullRowId(riRec)) Begin
4910>>>>>>>            If not (IsSameRowId(riRec, CurrentRowId(Self) ) ) Begin
4912>>>>>>>                Send FindByRowId iMain riRec // find an Relate all parents
4913>>>>>>>            End
4913>>>>>>>>
4913>>>>>>>            Set prFindRowId to (NullRowId())  // reset refind rec back to zero.
4914>>>>>>>        End
4914>>>>>>>>
4914>>>>>>>        Else Begin
4915>>>>>>>            // if this has a recnum, it better be a recnum table or an error will occur.
4915>>>>>>>            // This is not being tested for a recnum table on purpose. If someone is setting Find_record_id
4915>>>>>>>            // on a non-recnum table, they doing something wrong. An Error will be a good thing.
4915>>>>>>>            Get Find_Record_Id to iRec
4916>>>>>>>            If iRec Begin
4918>>>>>>>                If (iRec<>Current_record(Self)) Begin
4920>>>>>>>                    Send Find_By_Recnum iMain iRec // find an Relate all parents
4921>>>>>>>                End
4921>>>>>>>>
4921>>>>>>>                Set Find_record_id to 0 // reset refind rec back to zero.
4922>>>>>>>            End
4922>>>>>>>>
4922>>>>>>>        End
4922>>>>>>>>
4922>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
4923>>>>>>>
4923>>>>>>>        // recurse and do the same to all parent files
4923>>>>>>>        // in almost all cases, there will be no new finding here since the relate has
4923>>>>>>>        // found the records. If the record is different than the relate, we have
4923>>>>>>>        // a switched parent state (should_save will be set appropriately).
4923>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4924>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
4925>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
4931>>>>>>>>
4931>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hPrnt
4932>>>>>>>            If not (Visited_state(hPrnt)) ;                Send Private.Find_Records to hPrnt
4935>>>>>>>        Loop
4936>>>>>>>>
4936>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4937>>>>>>>
4937>>>>>>>    // This Mark_Id creates a sequence Id for this clear. This way
4937>>>>>>>    // DDOs only get cleared one time during this process.
4937>>>>>>>    Procedure IncrementCurrentMarkId
4939>>>>>>>        If (DD_Current_Mark_ID>65536) Begin
4941>>>>>>>            Move 0 to DD_Current_Mark_id
4942>>>>>>>        End
4942>>>>>>>>
4942>>>>>>>        Increment DD_Current_Mark_id
4943>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
4944>>>>>>>
4944>>>>>>>
4944>>>>>>>    // private use by new webapp framework as of 18.2.
4944>>>>>>>    // pass bStart as True if this is the start of the resynch.
4944>>>>>>>    Function ReSyncRecords Boolean bStart Returns Handle
4946>>>>>>>        RowID riRowId riCrnt
4946>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk bOldReSync bVisited
4946>>>>>>>        Handle hoOtherDDO hoBadDDO hoBadPrntDDO
4946>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount iMain
4946>>>>>>>
4946>>>>>>>        If bStart Begin
4948>>>>>>>            Send InitializeAllVisited
4949>>>>>>>        End
4949>>>>>>>>
4949>>>>>>>
4949>>>>>>>        // we want depth first traversal. Make sure children are handled before parents
4949>>>>>>>        // Recursively traverse Children, Find by RowId, Recursively traverse Parents
4949>>>>>>>        // Use visited_state logic to avoid multiple visits caused by diamond DDO strutures
4949>>>>>>>
4949>>>>>>>        //mark first so we don't visit this coming back up.
4949>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
4950>>>>>>>
4950>>>>>>>        // traverse downward first
4950>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
4951>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
4957>>>>>>>>
4957>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoOtherDDO
4958>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
4959>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
4961>>>>>>>                Get ReSyncRecords of hoOtherDDO False to hoBadPrntDDO
4962>>>>>>>                If (hoBadPrntDDO and not(hoBadDDO)) Begin
4964>>>>>>>                    Move hoBadPrntDDO to hoBadDDO
4965>>>>>>>                End
4965>>>>>>>>
4965>>>>>>>            End
4965>>>>>>>>
4965>>>>>>>        Loop
4966>>>>>>>>
4966>>>>>>>
4966>>>>>>>        // Find record for DD. It might already be correct if child has already
4966>>>>>>>        // related it in. If not correct after a relate, this has been switched by this
4966>>>>>>>        // user or switched by another user, in which case it will be swtitched back
4966>>>>>>>        // (DDOs have always worked this way).
4966>>>>>>>        Get prFindRowId to riRowId
4967>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
4968>>>>>>>        Get CurrentRowId to riCrnt
4969>>>>>>>        If ( not(IsSameRowId(riRowID, riCrnt)) ) Begin
4971>>>>>>>            Get pbInReSync to bOldReSync
4972>>>>>>>            Set pbInReSync to True
4973>>>>>>>
4973>>>>>>>            If (IsNullRowId(riRowID)) Begin
4975>>>>>>>                Send Clear
4976>>>>>>>            End
4976>>>>>>>>
4976>>>>>>>            Else Begin
4977>>>>>>>                Get FindByRowIdExNoAutoFill iMain riRowId to bOk
4978>>>>>>>                If not bOk Begin
4980>>>>>>>                    Move Self to hoBadDDO
4981>>>>>>>                End
4981>>>>>>>>
4981>>>>>>>            End
4981>>>>>>>>
4981>>>>>>>            Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
4982>>>>>>>        End
4982>>>>>>>>
4982>>>>>>>
4982>>>>>>>        // finally traverse to parents
4982>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
4983>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
4989>>>>>>>>
4989>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoOtherDDO
4990>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
4991>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
4993>>>>>>>                Get ReSyncRecords of hoOtherDDO False to hoBadPrntDDO
4994>>>>>>>                If (hoBadPrntDDO and not(hoBadDDO)) Begin
4996>>>>>>>                    Move hoBadPrntDDO to hoBadDDO
4997>>>>>>>                End
4997>>>>>>>>
4997>>>>>>>            End
4997>>>>>>>>
4997>>>>>>>        Loop
4998>>>>>>>>
4998>>>>>>>
4998>>>>>>>        If bStart Begin
5000>>>>>>>            Send InitializeAllVisited
5001>>>>>>>            Send ResetChangedStates
5002>>>>>>>        End
5002>>>>>>>>
5002>>>>>>>
5002>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoBadDDO
5003>>>>>>>    End_Function
5004>>>>>>>
5004>>>>>>>
5004>>>>>>>    Procedure ResetChangedStates
5006>>>>>>>        Boolean bVisited
5006>>>>>>>        Handle hoOtherDDO
5006>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount
5006>>>>>>>        tDDChangedInfo DDChangedInfo
5006>>>>>>>        tDDChangedInfo DDChangedInfo
5006>>>>>>>
5006>>>>>>>        // we want depth first traversal.
5006>>>>>>>        //mark first so we don't visit this coming back up.
5006>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
5007>>>>>>>
5007>>>>>>>        // traverse downward first
5007>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
5008>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
5014>>>>>>>>
5014>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoOtherDDO
5015>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
5016>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
5018>>>>>>>                Send ResetChangedStates of hoOtherDDO
5019>>>>>>>            End
5019>>>>>>>>
5019>>>>>>>        Loop
5020>>>>>>>>
5020>>>>>>>
5020>>>>>>>        // Set changed states for this DDO
5020>>>>>>>        Get pDDChangedInfo to DDChangedInfo
5021>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False // clears changed_state and parent_changed_states
5022>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to DDChangedInfo.bChanged
5023>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (SizeOfArray(DDChangedInfo.ParentChanged)-1)
5029>>>>>>>>
5029>>>>>>>            Send SetParentDDOSwitched DDChangedInfo.ParentChanged[iCount].iTable DDChangedInfo.ParentChanged[iCount].bSwitched
5030>>>>>>>        Loop
5031>>>>>>>>
5031>>>>>>>
5031>>>>>>>        // finally traverse to parents
5031>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
5032>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
5038>>>>>>>>
5038>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoOtherDDO
5039>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
5040>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
5042>>>>>>>                Send ResetChangedStates of hoOtherDDO
5043>>>>>>>            End
5043>>>>>>>>
5043>>>>>>>        Loop
5044>>>>>>>>
5044>>>>>>>
5044>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
5045>>>>>>>
5045>>>>>>>    // private use by new webapp framework (pre 18.2)
5045>>>>>>>    Function ReSyncRecord Returns Boolean
5047>>>>>>>        RowID riRowId
5047>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk bOldReSync
5047>>>>>>>        Handle hPrnt
5047>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount iMain
5047>>>>>>>
5047>>>>>>>        Get pbInReSync to bOldReSync
5048>>>>>>>
5048>>>>>>>        Get prFindRowId to riRowId
5049>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
5050>>>>>>>        If not (IsSameRowId(riRowID, CurrentRowId(Self) ) ) Begin
5052>>>>>>>            If (IsNullRowId(riRowID)) Begin
5054>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to True
5055>>>>>>>                Send Clear
5056>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
5057>>>>>>>            End
5057>>>>>>>>
5057>>>>>>>            Else Begin
5058>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to True
5059>>>>>>>                Get FindByRowIdExNoAutoFill iMain riRowId to bOk
5060>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
5061>>>>>>>                If not bOk Begin
5063>>>>>>>                    Function_Return False
5064>>>>>>>                End
5064>>>>>>>>
5064>>>>>>>            End
5064>>>>>>>>
5064>>>>>>>
5064>>>>>>>            // check that the relate found all the parent records we expect.
5064>>>>>>>            // This should be correct unless a parent has been switched. Constrained
5064>>>>>>>            // parents, by definition, should already be correct. See **Note** below
5064>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
5065>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
5071>>>>>>>>
5071>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hPrnt
5072>>>>>>>                If (Constrain_File(Self)<>Main_File(hPrnt) and ;                    not (IsSameRowID(prFindRowId(hPrnt),CurrentRowId(hPrnt)))) Begin
5074>>>>>>>                    // the parent is either wrong or not processed yet. Either way
5074>>>>>>>                    // make it right.
5074>>>>>>>                    Get ReSyncRecord of hPrnt to bOk
5075>>>>>>>                    If not bOk Begin
5077>>>>>>>                        Function_Return False
5078>>>>>>>                    End
5078>>>>>>>>
5078>>>>>>>                End
5078>>>>>>>>
5078>>>>>>>            Loop
5079>>>>>>>>
5079>>>>>>>        End
5079>>>>>>>>
5079>>>>>>>
5079>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
5080>>>>>>>    End_Function
5081>>>>>>>
5081>>>>>>>    // **Note** - dealing with changed parents and diamonds during a resync.
5081>>>>>>>    // If there is not a relates-to contraint between DD and child it is possible
5081>>>>>>>    // that the child find's relate will change the just found parent DD.
5081>>>>>>>    // Assuming this is not a structure bug, it means the parent is changed parent and that
5081>>>>>>>    // change must occur after the child record has been found and related. Therefore we add
5081>>>>>>>    // check after each child find to see if an parent is incorrect. If it is, either it is a
5081>>>>>>>    // switched parent or we haven't processed it yet. If the record is fine it
5081>>>>>>>    // just does nothing. For example (where *=relates-to):
5081>>>>>>>    //     W
5081>>>>>>>    //   */  \*
5081>>>>>>>    //   X    Y
5081>>>>>>>    //    \  /*
5081>>>>>>>    //     Z
5081>>>>>>>    // Assume you found a Z and changed its parent X.
5081>>>>>>>    // The refind order can be: WXZY or WYZX
5081>>>>>>>    // If WXZY the refound parent will be lost because Z will relate after the X
5081>>>>>>>    // find and replace it with the original parent. To control this we add this check
5081>>>>>>>    // after child Z has done its work. We only need to do this when child DDOs exist
5081>>>>>>>    // that are not constrained. This can change the order that DDOs are resynced but it
5081>>>>>>>    // should not matter.
5081>>>>>>>
5081>>>>>>>
5081>>>>>>>
5081>>>>>>>    // Private use by new webapp framework
5081>>>>>>>    Procedure ReSyncClearAll
5083>>>>>>>        Boolean bOldReSync
5083>>>>>>>        Get pbInReSync to bOldReSync
5084>>>>>>>        // we need this to stop RememberLast and retains. We don't want those during a resyc clear
5084>>>>>>>        Set pbInReSync to True
5085>>>>>>>        Send Clear_All
5086>>>>>>>        Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
5087>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
