5750>>>>>>>
5750>>>>>>>
5750>>>>>>>    //   Set, clear or toggle a field option
5750>>>>>>>    //   Multiple options can be passed as an expression
5750>>>>>>>    //   (e.g. Set Field_option 2 (dd_Retain IOR dd_NoEnter).
5750>>>>>>>    //   Unlike set Field_options this notifies DEOs of changes
5750>>>>>>>    // supports setting and clearing. e.g.:
5750>>>>>>>    //    Set Field_Option Field Customer.Name DD_NoEnter to True
5750>>>>>>>    // This new syntax is now the recommended syntax but the older syntax without
5750>>>>>>>    // the last parameter is supported (where true is the default). The old syntax is
5750>>>>>>>    // only supported for compatibility. This means that Field_Option_Clear should
5750>>>>>>>    // also be replaced with Field_Option
5750>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Option Integer iField Integer iOption Boolean bSet
5752>>>>>>>        Boolean bSetTrue
5752>>>>>>>        Move (If(num_arguments>2, bSet, True)) to bSetTrue // support for old deprecated syntax
5753>>>>>>>        If bSetTrue Begin
5755>>>>>>>            Set Field_options iField to iOption
5756>>>>>>>        End
5756>>>>>>>>
5756>>>>>>>        Else Begin
5757>>>>>>>            Set Field_options iField to DD_CLEAR_FIELD_OPTIONS iOption
5758>>>>>>>        End
5758>>>>>>>>
5758>>>>>>>        If (Data_Set_User_Interface_Count(Self)) Begin
5760>>>>>>>            Send Field_Option_Changed iField iOption (not(bSetTrue))
5761>>>>>>>        End
5761>>>>>>>>
5761>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
