6594>>>>>>>    // returns active constraints in atConstraintDef array.
6594>>>>>>>    // Should be called after constraints are built
6594>>>>>>>    // typically right after Rebuild_Constraints
6594>>>>>>>
6594>>>>>>>    Function DDOConstraints Returns tConstraintDef[]
6596>>>>>>>        tConstraintDef[] Constraints
6596>>>>>>>        tConstraintDef[] Constraints
6597>>>>>>>        Integer i iCount i1
6597>>>>>>>        Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_COUNT to iCount
6598>>>>>>>        For i from 0 to (iCount-1)
6604>>>>>>>>
6604>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO i 0 to i1 // type / mode
6605>>>>>>>            Move (Hi(i1)) to  Constraints[i].eType
6606>>>>>>>            Move (Low(i1)) to  Constraints[i].eMode
6607>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO i 1 to i1 // file / field
6608>>>>>>>            Move (Hi(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iFile
6609>>>>>>>            Move (Low(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iField
6610>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO i 2 to i1 // other file /field
6611>>>>>>>            Move (Hi(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iOtherFile
6612>>>>>>>            Move (Low(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iOtherField
6613>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO_Value i  to Constraints[i].sValue
6614>>>>>>>        Loop
6615>>>>>>>>
6615>>>>>>>        Function_Return Constraints
6616>>>>>>>    End_Function
6617>>>>>>>
6617>>>>>>>    // returns constraint finding information about the current find. This tells us what kinds
6617>>>>>>>    // of constraint find "expressions" are used. This will actually do a cosntrained find
6617>>>>>>>    // initialization much like Establish_Find_Direction, which means it can change the values in
6617>>>>>>>    // the file buffer to assist with a jump-in.
6617>>>>>>>    Function DDOConstraintFindMeta Integer eMode Integer iOrder Returns tDDOConstraintFindMeta
6619>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
6619>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
6619>>>>>>>        Integer i
6619>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Constraint_Exps eMode iOrder to i
6620>>>>>>>        Move (Hi(i)) to FindMeta.iJumpInSegments
6621>>>>>>>        Move (i iand CONST_EXP_JUMPOUT) to FindMeta.bJumpOut
6622>>>>>>>        Move (i iand CONST_EXP_PRE_RELATE) to FindMeta.bPreRelate
6623>>>>>>>        Move (i iand CONST_EXP_POST_RELATE) to FindMeta.bPostRelate
6624>>>>>>>        Function_Return FindMeta
6625>>>>>>>    End_Function
6626>>>>>>>
6626>>>>>>>    // this tells you if the current find or read requires a relate to evaluate the DF constraint.
6626>>>>>>>    // If false you could use this to set no_relate_state to false for the find/read process and then
6626>>>>>>>    // restore it when complete. Be careful using this.
6626>>>>>>>    Function DDOConstraintNeedsRelate Integer iOrder Returns Boolean
6628>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
6628>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
6628>>>>>>>        Get DDOConstraintFindMeta (GE) iOrder to FindMeta
6629>>>>>>>        Function_Return FindMeta.bPostRelate
6630>>>>>>>    End_Function
