11536>>>>>>>    // this does a low level login, which basically wraps the login command with some error handling
11536>>>>>>>    // and the ability to make a login silent.
11536>>>>>>>    // This is essentially a Login command surrounded by error checking and trapping
11536>>>>>>>    Function BasicLogin String sDriver String sServer String sName String sPassword Returns Integer
11538>>>>>>>        Integer iError iIndex
11538>>>>>>>        Handle hoConnect
11538>>>>>>>
11538>>>>>>>        Get DriverIndex sDriver to iIndex
11539>>>>>>>        If (iIndex>0) Begin
11541>>>>>>>            Send CheckTokenConnection sDriver sServer                       
11542>>>>>>>            Send TrapErrors               
11543>>>>>>>            Login sServer sName sPassword sDriver
11545>>>>>>>            Send UnTrapErrors
11546>>>>>>>            Get piErrorNumber to iError
11547>>>>>>>        End
11547>>>>>>>>
11547>>>>>>>        Else Begin
11548>>>>>>>            Move DFERR_PROGRAM to iError
11549>>>>>>>            Error iError (SFormat(C_$DriverNotFound,  sDriver))
11550>>>>>>>>
11550>>>>>>>        End
11550>>>>>>>>
11550>>>>>>>        Function_Return iError
11551>>>>>>>    End_Function   
