14144>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Initialize_Files
14146>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
14146>>>>>>>>>        String sname
14146>>>>>>>>>        Send Clear_File_Data
14147>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iFile
14148>>>>>>>>>        Repeat
14148>>>>>>>>>>
14148>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute Df_File_Next_Used of iFile to iFile
14151>>>>>>>>>            If (iFile = 0) ;                Break
14154>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute Df_File_Logical_Name of iFile to sName
14157>>>>>>>>>            Send Set_File_Data sName iFile
14158>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14159>>>>>>>>>>
14159>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14160>>>>>>>>>    
14160>>>>>>>>>    // Search_Field_Name provides a way of getting the
14160>>>>>>>>>    // field Name without generating an error. We will use an error
14160>>>>>>>>>    // handle in this object to "swallow" the error.
14160>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Error_Report Integer iErrNum Integer iErrLine String sErrMsg
14162>>>>>>>>>        Move True to Err
14163>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14164>>>>>>>>>    
14164>>>>>>>>>    Function Search_Field_Name Integer iFile String sFieldName Returns Integer
14166>>>>>>>>>        Handle hOldErr
14166>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField
14166>>>>>>>>>        If (iFile = 0) ;            Function_Return 0
14169>>>>>>>>>        Move Error_Object_id to hOldErr           // push error handler
14170>>>>>>>>>        Move Self to Error_Object_Id    // redirect here, it is silent!
14171>>>>>>>>>        Move False to Err
14172>>>>>>>>>        Field_Map iFile sFieldName to iField      // this could gen an error, we will trap it here
14174>>>>>>>>>        Move hOldErr to Error_object_id           // pop old error handler
14175>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (If( (Err), -1, iField))
14176>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14177>>>>>>>>>    
14177>>>>>>>>>End_Class
