18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// This provides DEO to DDO server support for Web DEOs.
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Notes:
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Add_Focus_msg   - not supported.
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Deferred_State  - not supported.
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Default_static_server_state - not supported.
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Refresh_Dirty_State         - not supported
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Static_Server_State         - not supported.
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Function Find_Server - not supported.
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>Class cWebBaseDEOServer is a cWebBaseUIObject
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Server is the object id of the database agent for this object.
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Watched_Servers is a set of object ids for database agents whose state
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   must also be monitored by this object (but which never receive requests
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   directly from this object, unlike the Server).
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Servers_Scanned determines if the items of this object have been
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   scanned to see if this object should be connected to other database
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   agents as 'just watching' (see Watched_Servers, above).
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
18632>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
18634>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18634>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean Auto_Fill_State False       // Used to tell DDO's whether first record should be found automatically after a clear.
18635>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbAutoFillOnInit False      // Used to tell DDO's that we want autofill on initialization when DEO is attaching
18636>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18636>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer private_Server 0
18637>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Watched_Servers 0          // Handle to Broadcaster object broacasting tos server DDO's
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // used to send Set Changed_State to "foreign" servers, while Watched_Servers
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // is used for sending messages from the DDO to DEOs (there are more of them)
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer ChangedStateWatched_Servers     0
18639>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer private_pbServersScanned 0
18640>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18640>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // added to support DEO request-delegation. This is set true if the
18640>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // server is explicitly set in this DEO (normally via a USING parameter).
18640>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Explicit_Server_State False
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Since this package's SET changed_state is using change_disabled_state
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // we might as well Define it here. This gets changed by Clear_mx to support
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // setting of defaults without changing the objects changed_state.
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // This stops changed_state from getting changed. It allows item_changed_state
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // to change without the object's changed_state getting changed. This Should
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // be considered protected (i.e., likely to change). The new messages Entry_Defaults
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // and Set Default_Value are both public and Use this. Try to use these messages
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // instead of this Property.
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Change_Disabled_State False
18642>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18642>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean Extended_DEO_State False    // Defines DEO behavior according to Extended_DEO_State of the server DDO
18643>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18643>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean Active_State False          // True when the DEO has been attached to the DDO
18644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Handle Verify_Save_msg (RefProc(SaveConfirmation))
18645>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Handle Verify_Data_Loss_msg (RefProc(DataLossConfirmation))
18646>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Handle Verify_Delete_msg (RefProc(DeleteConfirmation))
18647>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18647>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // pbClearAfterSave: When true forces a DDO Request_Clear after performing a Request_Save. This property is reached
18647>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // via delegation from the DEO that processes the Request_Save operation. Thus this property will control the
18647>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // behavior for all DEOs belonging to this view.
18647>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbClearAfterSave True
18648>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18648>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Determines if the Delete callback is allowed, is set to true when the verification dialog is shown. Additional security check.
18648>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbDeleteCallbackActive False
18651>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Determines if the Save callback is allowed, is set to true when the verification dialog is shown. Additional security check.
18651>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbSaveCallbackActive False
18654>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18654>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestClearCallback
18655>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestDeleteCallback
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestSaveCallBack
18657>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestClearAllCallback
18658>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure adds the specified object id (hoServer) to this object's
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and establishes a
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // connection between the database agent and this object.
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_Watched_Server Integer hoServer
18661>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
18661>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
18661>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18661>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18662>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoWatchedServers = 0) Begin
18664>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to hoWatchedServers // modern syntax
18665>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18666>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18666>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18666>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18666>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to False
18667>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Find_Element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
18668>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18668>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex < 0) Begin
18670>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_Element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
18671>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18671>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18671>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18671>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to True
18672>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18672>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex < 0 and Active_State(Self)) Begin
18674>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_User_Interface to hoServer Self True // TRUE for watchers
18675>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18675>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18675>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18676>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18676>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_ChangedStateWatched_Server Integer hoServer
18678>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
18678>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
18678>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18678>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18679>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoWatchedServers = 0) Begin
18681>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to hoWatchedServers // modern syntax
18682>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18683>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18683>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18683>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18683>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to False
18684>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Find_Element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
18685>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18685>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex < 0) Begin
18687>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_Element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
18688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18688>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to True
18689>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18690>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18690>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18690>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Expects the class to understand the Active_State property. Relies on the pbDataBindable interface.
18690>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Attach_Deo_To_Server
18692>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
18692>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bServerScan bDataBindable
18692>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18692>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18693>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
18694>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18694>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
18696>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_User_Interface to hoServer Self
18697>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // Extended_DEO_State is used to determine whether the object receives the data binding related
18697>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // message interface from the server DDO...
18697>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Extended_DEO_State to (Extended_DSO_State(hoServer) and bDataBindable)
18698>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18698>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18698>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_pbServersScanned to bServerScan
18699>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bServerScan)) Begin
18701>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Scan_Servers
18702>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18702>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18702>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18702>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18703>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // True for watchers
18706>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18706>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18706>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18706>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Active_State to True
18707>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed so that this respects Change_disabled_state. I don't
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // like this here but its the best I can think of. Therefore, all
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // objects using server.pkg must understand Change_disabled_state.
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed to not remove from server if static.
18708>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Changed_State Integer newVal
18710>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
18710>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18710>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (Change_Disabled_State(Self)) Begin
18712>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get server to hoServer
18713>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
18713>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newVal and hoServer) Begin
18715>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Changed_State of hoServer to True
18716>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // We also set changed_state of all "foreign" servers. These
18716>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // are the ones whose Data_File is a parent File
18716>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18717>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If hoWatchedServers ;                    Set Changed_State of hoWatchedServers to True
18720>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18720>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18720>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18720>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18720>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18721>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18721>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns the table's status for the refresh event. A table can either be
18721>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // cleared, found or not touched by the operation. This can only be called while
18721>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // within Refresh. This was created to hide the private is_file_included command
18721>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DDRefreshTableStatus Integer iTable Returns Integer
18723>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bIncluded
18723>>>>>>>>>>>>>        is_file_included iTable 1 to bIncluded // see if main file is in find done array
18725>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bIncluded Begin
18727>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return ddrtsFound
18728>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18728>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18728>>>>>>>>>>>>>        is_file_included iTable 0 to bIncluded // see if main file is in clear done array
18730>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bIncluded Begin
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return ddrtsCleared
18733>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
18733>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18733>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18733>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ddrtsNone
18734>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure empties the Watched_Servers broadcaster, after
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   detaching this object from all of the broadcaster's elements.
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked by Find_Servers_to_Watch, in preparation
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   for a scan.
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Delete_Watched_Servers
18737>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoWatchedServers
18737>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18737>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18738>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18740>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // detach from all, TRUE for watchers
18741>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
18742>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Delete_Data to hoWatchedServers                     // empty it
18743>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
18744>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18744>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18744>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18745>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18747>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
18748>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Delete_Data to hoWatchedServers                     // empty it
18749>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
18750>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18750>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18750>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18751>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18751>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface. Indicates if this DEO is a data bindable control or a container.
18751>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // For cWebControls, this is just another way of querying pbDataBindable, used by DD's
18751>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DEO_Control_Object Returns Boolean
18753>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataBindable
18753>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
18754>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bDataBindable
18755>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface. Indicates that this DEO understands the DEO Request_Find protocol
18756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DEO_Find_Object Returns Boolean
18758>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return False
18759>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18760>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18760>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Used to determine if the object understands the DEO interface.
18760>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Probably not used in Ajax WebApps.
18760>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DEO_Object Returns Boolean
18762>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
18763>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This only gets called when the developer is killing this object. During application
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // shut-down, only destroy_object is called. This augmentation destroys the watched broadcaster
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (which is sitting on the desktop). During program shut down we don't care if this is called
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // because it is getting destroyed anyway. We are making the assumption that a developer controlled
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // destroy will always be called with the watcher still existing.
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy
18766>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatched
18766>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False //   is this really needed anymore???
18767>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The watched server, must still exist.
18767>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatched
18768>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
18770>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
18771>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
18772>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18772>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The bound watched server, must still exist.
18772>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatched
18773>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
18775>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
18776>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy
18779>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // sent by DD before a find and save. We only care about DD finds which
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // means DoAll is 1
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Entry_Update Integer iFile Integer iDoAll
18782>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // STUB: Not used with Ajax WebApp
18782>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure scans the fields of this object's items to determine
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   what other database agents (data_sets) other than this object's Server
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   should be 'watched' (for data changes).
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   iTableFlag is a boolean determining whether this object relies on a
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   prototype row (TRUE) or an item list (FALSE).
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   [JVH] VDF 17.0 - Ignored in this class.
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This object must understand pbDataBindable, and have a private
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   boolean property named Private_pbServersScanned to note the event.
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Notes
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked once per object, the first time the object
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   is activated.  If the data_file, data_field, and/or main_file of this
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   object are changed (don't change them while this object is active!),
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set Private_pbServersScanned to FALSE to force this object to scan
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   again (when it is next activated).
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 17.0: The logic has been retooled to add more watched servers to the DDOs. This is done so
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // DD operations will send Refresh to these additional watched-servers. There are two changes:
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 1. Containers are now made watched servers for the Server and all parent servers
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 2. Non-file.field DEOs (e.g., expressions) are made watched servers for the server (which it
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    already did and for all parent servers. Without this, parent entry_item expressions were not
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    getting updated
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Here is how watched-servers works.
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Each DEO attaches and detaches from its Server by sending Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to the server DD. Once attached, the DD knows about this DEO and sends messages to it as needed (Refresh,
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Entry_Update, etc.). In addition, a DEO may need to attach a parent DDO so that changes in that parent DD
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // results in those messages being sent. This is needed if the binding table in entry_item refers to a parent
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // table. So we need to send Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface to that parent server as well. If a DEO
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // has multiple, there could be multiple parent servers. As of 17.0, we are also attaching to parent servers if
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // we are unsure about how the DEO is being used. If an expression is used, it might need to be updated when
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // a parent (or any ancestor) changes. Each DEO keeps track of servers that it attaches to and this is referred
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to as the watched_server list. This list is maintained so the DEO knows which DDOs to attach and detach to.
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // [JVH] VDF 17.1 cWebAppDEOServer_mixin Notes:
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to support only 1 item per control. Get Item_Count interface not supported.
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to not support the Prototype_Object interface (old windows Table class).
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Servers_To_Watch Integer iTableFlag
18785>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFileNum iServerFile
18785>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoDataSet
18785>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataBindable
18785>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18785>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
18786>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Private_pbServersScanned to True
18787>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18788>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18788>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer = 0) Begin
18790>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
18791>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18791>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18791>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18791>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Watched_Servers  // empty Watched_Servers broadcaster first
18792>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoServer to iServerFile  // data-set's main-file
18793>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18793>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bDataBindable)) Begin
18795>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // containers should get added to all parent DDOs
18795>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
18796>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
18797>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18797>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18797>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18797>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_File to iFileNum
18798>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // we need watched server if file exists, it is not the main file
18798>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // and is not an updating file (as opposed to updating data-set).
18798>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFileNum > 0 and iFileNum <> iServerFile) Begin
18800>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Which_Data_Set of hoServer iFileNum to hoDataSet
18801>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (hoDataSet <> 0 and hoDataSet <> hoServer) Begin
18803>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_Watched_Server hoDataSet
18804>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_ChangedStateWatched_Server hoDataSet
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iFileNum = 0) Begin
18808>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no file (e.g., expression) we don't know when it changes so we tell all servers
18808>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // that this is a watcher
18808>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
18809>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18809>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18809>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18810>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18810>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function returns the object id of the database agent of this object,
18810>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // or 0.
18810>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Locate_Server Returns Integer
18812>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
18812>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18813>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServer
18814>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
18817>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18818>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18818>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure discontinues the connection between this object and its
18818>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   database agent(s) (Server and Watched_Servers).
18818>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_DEO_From_Server
18820>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
18820>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18820>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18821>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18821>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
18823>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self
18824>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18824>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18824>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18824>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only send if watched-server exists
18824>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18825>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18825>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18827>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // TRUE for watchers
18828>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18828>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18828>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18828>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // when removed the deo is no longer up to date.
18828>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Refresh_Dirty_State to True
18829>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure removes the specified object id (hoServer) from this object's
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and destroys the
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_Watched_Server Integer hoServer
18832>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
18832>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
18832>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18832>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18833>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only if w server exists
18833>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18835>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
18836>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get find_element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
18837>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0) Begin
18839>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send remove_element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
18840>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18840>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18840>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
18841>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0 and Active_State(Self)) Begin
18843>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self True // TRUE for watchers
18844>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18844>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18844>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18844>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18844>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function returns the object id of the database agent of this object, or 0.
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // If this object's Server is 0, this object's parent's Server is returned, if any.
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function is used to allow nested data-entry objects to use the
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // database agent defined by their parent object.
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Server Returns Integer
18847>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer
18847>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_Server to hoServer
18848>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer = 0) Begin
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return (Locate_Server(parent(Self)))
18851>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18851>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18851>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServer
18852>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure sets the value of the Server property of this object,
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // notifying child-objects of the change, and destroying and creating
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // connections with database agents, as required.
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // If the Server of this object is changed while this object is inactive,
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // no notification of child-objects is required or performed.
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Server Integer newVal
18855>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldVal
18855>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18855>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Explicit_Server_State to (newVal <> 0)
18856>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to oldVal
18857>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18857>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (newVal <> 0) Begin
18859>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set private_Server to (object_id(newVal))
18860>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18860>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18860>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
18861>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set private_Server to newVal
18862>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18862>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18862>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18862>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Active_State(Self)) Begin
18864>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Broadcast Send server_changed oldVal newVal
18866>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) Begin
18868>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Remove_DEO_From_Server  // detach from current server
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newval <> 0) Begin
18871>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Attach_Deo_To_Server    // attach to new server
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure servers as notification of a change in the connection
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   of this object's parent to its database agent.  If this object uses
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   its parent's database agent by default (see the Server and Find_Server
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   functions, above), it must disconnect from the old agent and connect
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   with the new agent.
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Server_Changed Integer oldVal Integer newVal
18875>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldSrvr
18875>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18875>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_Server to oldSrvr
18876>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (oldSrvr = 0) Begin  //assumes Server(self) = oldVal by deleg
18878>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) ;                Send remove_user_interface to oldVal Self
18881>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newVal <> 0) ;                Send add_user_interface to newVal Self
18884>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18884>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18884>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18885>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18885>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18885>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // return the DEO that sets the server
18885>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function ServerDEO Returns Handle
18887>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoServerDeo
18887>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bExplicitServer
18887>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18888>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer) Begin
18890>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Explicit_Server_State to bExplicitServer
18891>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bExplicitServer) Begin
18893>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Move Self to hoServerDeo
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
18895>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Get ServerDEO to hoServerDeo
18897>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18897>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18897>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18897>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18897>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServerDeo
18898>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18899>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18899>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure causes the scanning of this object's items' fields,
18899>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   and the production of a set of database agents who should be 'watched'.
18899>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Scan_Servers
18901>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Find_Servers_To_Watch False
18902>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18903>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18903>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18903>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Not used for cWebControls
18903>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Update_Dependent_Items
18905>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Stub
18905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18906>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18906>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18906>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // required DD/DEO interface
18906>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Items Boolean bNotFindReq Returns Integer
18908>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // This is handled by the DDO
18908>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18909>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18909>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18909>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface (maybe). We don't use the setter in cWebControls
18909>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Value Integer iItem String sValue
18911>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18912>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18912>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Value Integer iItem Returns String
18914>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ""
18915>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18916>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18916>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This adds every parent DDO for the passed DDO to the DEO's list of DDOs to watch.
18916>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // It adds the parents and then does this recursively up the DDO tree.
18916>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This means that this DEO will respond to any DD change for any server. This does not
18916>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure WatchAllParentServers Handle hoDDO
18918>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSrvr
18918>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iServer iServers
18918>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count of hoDDO to iServers
18919>>>>>>>>>>>>>        For iServer from 0 to (iServers-1)
18925>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18925>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server of hoDDO iServer to hoSrvr
18926>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_Watched_Server hoSrvr
18927>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoSrvr
18928>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
18929>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18929>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18930>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18930>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // standard helper used for all verify save, delete, clear confirmation
18930>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure VerifyRequest Handle hmCallBack Handle hmVerifyMsg
18932>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hmVerifyRequest
18932>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get hmVerifyMsg to hmVerifyRequest // this is the verify message for this operation
18933>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hmVerifyRequest Begin
18935>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if a verify message exists call it passing the callback message
18935>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send hmVerifyRequest hmCallBack
18936>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18936>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18936>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
18937>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no verify message, just execute the callback with a yes
18937>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send hmCallBack cmYes
18938>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18938>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18938>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18939>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18939>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // return true if this message can be delegated to an explicit server
18939>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DelegateDeoRequest Returns Boolean
18941>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoServerDEO
18941>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ServerDEO to hoServerDEO
18942>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (hoServerDEO<>0 and hoServerDEO<>Self)
18943>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18944>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18944>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18944>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // default save confirmation message
18944>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SaveConfirmation Handle hmCallBack
18946>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ShowYesNo (Self) hmCallBack C_$SaveThisRecord  C_$Confirm
18947>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18948>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18948>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // default Data_Loss Y/Nconfirmation message
18948>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DataLossConfirmation Handle hmCallBack
18950>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ShowYesNo (Self) hmCallBack C_$AbandonChanges  C_$Confirm
18951>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18952>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18952>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // default Data_Loss Save/Close/Cancel confirmation message
18952>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SaveClearCancelConfirmation Handle hmCallBack
18954>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ShowYesNoCancel (Self) hmCallBack C_$Save_Changes_Before_Closing  C_$Confirm
18955>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18956>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18956>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18956>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // default Delete confirmation message
18956>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DeleteConfirmation Handle hmCallBack
18958>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ShowYesNo (Self) hmCallBack C_$DeleteThisRecord  C_$Confirm
18959>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18960>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18960>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestClearCallBack Integer eConfirmMode
18962>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (eConfirmMode=cmYes) Begin
18964>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestClearExec
18965>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18965>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18965>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18966>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18966>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Clear
18968>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
18968>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDelegate
18968>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18968>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DelegateDeoRequest to bDelegate
18969>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bDelegate Begin
18971>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Request_Clear
18973>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
18974>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18974>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18974>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18974>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18975>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
18977>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Should_Save(hoServer)) Begin
18979>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send VerifyRequest (RefProc(RequestClearCallBack)) (RefFunc(Verify_Data_Loss_Msg))
18980>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18980>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18980>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
18981>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send RequestClearExec
18982>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18982>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18982>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18983>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18983>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestClearExec
18985>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
18985>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18986>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Clear to hoServer
18987>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18987>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send FocusFirst
18988>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send OnViewCleared hoServer
18989>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18990>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18990>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18990>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestClearAllCallBack Integer eConfirmMode
18992>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (eConfirmMode=cmYes) Begin
18994>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestClearAllExec
18995>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18995>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18995>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18996>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18996>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Clear_All
18998>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
18998>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDelegate
18998>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18998>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DelegateDeoRequest to bDelegate
18999>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bDelegate Begin
19001>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Request_Clear_All
19003>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
19004>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19004>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19004>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19004>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
19005>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
19007>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Should_Save(hoServer)) Begin
19009>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send VerifyRequest (RefProc(RequestClearAllCallBack)) (RefFunc(Verify_Data_Loss_Msg))
19010>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19010>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
19011>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send RequestClearAllExec
19012>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19012>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19012>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19012>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19012>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19013>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19013>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestClearAllExec
19015>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
19015>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
19016>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Clear_All to hoServer
19017>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19017>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send FocusFirst
19018>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19019>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19019>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestDeleteCallBack Integer eConfirmMode
19021>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bActive
19021>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19021>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //  Security check
19021>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebGet pbDeleteCallbackActive to bActive
19022>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bActive)) Begin
19024>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_WEBAPP_ACCESS_DENIED
19025>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19025>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
19026>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19026>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19026>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebSet pbDeleteCallbackActive to False
19027>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19027>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (eConfirmMode=cmYes) Begin
19029>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestDeleteExec
19030>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19030>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19031>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19031>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Delete
19033>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Request delete message for DDO delete.
19033>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
19033>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDelegate
19033>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19033>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DelegateDeoRequest to bDelegate
19034>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bDelegate Begin
19036>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Request_Delete
19038>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
19039>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19039>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19039>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19039>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
19040>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19040>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0 and can_delete(hoServer) <> 0) Begin
19042>>>>>>>>>>>>>            WebSet pbDeleteCallbackActive to True
19043>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send VerifyRequest (RefProc(RequestDeleteCallBack)) (RefFunc(Verify_Delete_Msg))
19044>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19044>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19044>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19045>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19045>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestDeleteExec
19047>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
19047>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
19048>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move False to Err
19049>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Delete to hoServer
19050>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Always clear deleted record
19050>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(err)) Begin
19052>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestClearExec
19053>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send OnViewDeleted hoServer
19054>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19054>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19054>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19055>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19055>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestSaveCallBack Integer eConfirmMode
19057>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bActive
19057>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19057>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //  Security check
19057>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebGet pbSaveCallbackActive to bActive
19058>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bActive)) Begin
19060>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_WEBAPP_ACCESS_DENIED
19061>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19061>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
19062>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19062>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19062>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebSet pbSaveCallbackActive to False
19063>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19063>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // called as a callback started by Request_Save
19063>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (eConfirmMode=cmYes) Begin
19065>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestSaveExec
19066>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19066>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19066>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19067>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19067>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // What to do with a new unchanged record. The normal framework behavior has always been
19067>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to do nothing. With drilldown, it might make the most sense to attempt a save. Currently
19067>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // when drilldown, we will return True, else false
19067>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function AlwaysSaveNew Returns Boolean
19069>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer eViewStyle
19069>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bSave
19069>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get WebViewStyle to eViewStyle
19070>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (eViewStyle=wvsDrillDown) Begin
19072>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get AlwaysSaveWhenNewDrillDown to bSave
19073>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19073>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19073>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bSave
19074>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
19075>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19075>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Save
19077>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
19077>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRetVal
19077>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDelegate bRequestValidateAll bShouldSave bHasRec
19077>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19077>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DelegateDeoRequest to bDelegate
19078>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bDelegate Begin
19080>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Request_Save
19082>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
19083>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19083>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19083>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19083>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
19084>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19084>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If ((hoServer <> 0) and not(Read_Only_State(hoServer))) Begin
19086>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Should_Save of hoServer to bShouldSave
19087>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no changes but a new record, we may want to attempt a save anyway (for drilldown style)
19087>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (not(bShouldSave)) Begin
19089>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get HasRecord of hoServer to bHasRec
19090>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bHasRec Begin
19092>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get AlwaysSaveNew to bShouldSave
19093>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19093>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19093>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19093>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19093>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If bShouldSave Begin
19095>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // Handle save validation....
19095>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get pbRequesteValidateAll to bRequestValidateAll
19096>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If bRequestValidateAll Begin
19098>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Request_Validate_All of hoServer to iRetVal
19099>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19099>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19099>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
19100>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Request_Validate of hoServer to iRetVal
19101>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19101>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19101>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iRetVal=0) Begin
19103>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    WebSet pbSaveCallbackActive to True
19104>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send VerifyRequest (RefProc(RequestSaveCallBack)) (RefFunc(Verify_Save_Msg))
19105>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19105>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19105>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19105>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19105>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
19106>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (pbClearAfterSave(Self)) Begin
19108>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send RequestClearExec
19109>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19109>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19109>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send OnViewSaved hoServer False
19110>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19110>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19110>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19110>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19110>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19111>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19111>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19111>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestSaveExec
19113>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
19113>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRetVal
19113>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bRequestValidateAll bErr
19113>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
19114>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // this may be a 2nd request_validate, that's ok.
19114>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbRequesteValidateAll to bRequestValidateAll
19115>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bRequestValidateAll Begin
19117>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Request_Validate_All of hoServer to iRetVal
19118>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19118>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19118>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
19119>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Request_Validate of hoServer to iRetVal
19120>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19120>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19120>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iRetVal=0) Begin
19122>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move False to Err
19123>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Request_Save to hoServer
19124>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move Err to bErr
19125>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (not(bErr)) Begin
19127>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // clear saved record
19127>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (pbClearAfterSave(Self)) Begin
19129>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send RequestClearExec
19130>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19130>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19130>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send OnViewSaved hoServer True
19131>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19131>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19131>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19131>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19131>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
