19304>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19304>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_GE
19306>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Find GE True
19307>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19308>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19308>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Next
19310>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Find GT True
19311>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19312>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19312>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Previous
19314>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Find LT True
19315>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 3/22/2002: Added find_first and Find_last. Previously this
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // was accomplished by sending beginning_of_data and end_of_data. The
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // problem with that message is that it had multiple meaning. In a edit
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // or grid, it means go to top/bottom of file. In forms, it means first
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // last record. Since we can not change this without breaking existing
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // programs we will create a message that *always* does a find first/last
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // record. This can be used in tool bars (or anywhere) to consistently provide
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // the same behavior.
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_First
19318>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Find FIRST_RECORD False // param is false because entry-update is not needed
19319>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19320>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19320>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Last
19322>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Find LAST_RECORD False
19323>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19324>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19324>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SuperFind
19326>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_SuperFind GE
19327>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19328>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19328>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SuperFind_Next
19330>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_SuperFind GT
19331>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19332>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19332>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SuperFind_Previous
19334>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_SuperFind LT
19335>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
