21743>>>>>>>>>
21743>>>>>>>>>    // Sent when a refind record fails during one of the refind records operation 
21743>>>>>>>>>    // By default it does nothing, but it can raise an error and allows for careful customization
21743>>>>>>>>>    //
21743>>>>>>>>>    // hoDDO is the DDO that had the refind failure.
21743>>>>>>>>>    // This failed because RowId record cannot be refound or the RowId record is not 
21743>>>>>>>>>    // constraint valid.
21743>>>>>>>>>    //
21743>>>>>>>>>    // eOperation tells you what operation caused this:
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 0 - reoUndefined: should not get called with this
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 1 - reoSyncDDOs: During a request resync 
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 2 - reoNavigateForward: After resync during a NavigateForward
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 3 - reoNavigateBack: After resync during a NavigateBack 
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 4 - reoRefreshRecord: during RefreshRecord.
21743>>>>>>>>>    //
21743>>>>>>>>>    // eReason tells you the type of record find failure. 
21743>>>>>>>>>    // These only apply to NavigateForward|Back
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 0 - retUndefined
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 1 - retCannotRereadMain: Failed rereading the main file
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 2 - retCannotRereadConstrainingParent: Failed rereading a constraining parent
21743>>>>>>>>>    // 
21743>>>>>>>>>    // If you place a breakpoint here, you've got a place where all refind errors
21743>>>>>>>>>    // are redirected - very useful for debugging.
21743>>>>>>>>>
21743>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnRefindRecordError Handle hoDD Integer eOperation Integer eReason
21745>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bShowAllRefindErrors
21745>>>>>>>>>        
21745>>>>>>>>>        // pbShowAllRefindErrors is cWebApp property, set it true when debugging to see all
21745>>>>>>>>>        // errors. This assumes that a refind error during debugging is probably a programming bug.
21745>>>>>>>>>        
21745>>>>>>>>>        Get pbShowAllRefindErrors to bShowAllRefindErrors
21746>>>>>>>>>        If bShowAllRefindErrors Begin
21748>>>>>>>>>             Send CannotRefindRecordUnhandledError hoDD
21749>>>>>>>>>        End
21749>>>>>>>>>>
21749>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
21750>>>>>>>>>
21750>>>>>>>>>    // Sent when RefreshRecord fails. 
21750>>>>>>>>>    // By default call standard OnRefindRecordError. This allows for customization
21750>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnRefreshRecordError Handle hoDD
21752>>>>>>>>>        Send OnRefindRecordError hoDD reoRefreshRecord retUndefined
21753>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
