26879>>>>>>>>>
26879>>>>>>>>>    // RegisterColumn:
26879>>>>>>>>>    
26879>>>>>>>>>    // Registers a column object in the columns collection.
26879>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RegisterColumn Handle hoColumn
26881>>>>>>>>>        Integer iSize
26881>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] hoColumnObjects
26882>>>>>>>>>        Get phoColumnObjects to hoColumnObjects
26883>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(hoColumnObjects)) to iSize
26884>>>>>>>>>        Move hoColumn to hoColumnObjects[iSize]
26885>>>>>>>>>        Set piColumnId of hoColumn to iSize
26886>>>>>>>>>        Set phoColumnObjects to hoColumnObjects
26887>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26888>>>>>>>>>    
26888>>>>>>>>>    
26888>>>>>>>>>    // Sent by DDO when there is a clear/find/save/delete.
26888>>>>>>>>>    //
26888>>>>>>>>>    // eMode - Determines the type of DDO operation which generated this refresh message. 
26888>>>>>>>>>    //         It may be one of the following:
26888>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear:             Used only for DEOs attached to the DDO that was the
26888>>>>>>>>>    //                                 "origin" of a Clear operation, (i.e., the DDO received
26888>>>>>>>>>    //                                 the original Clear message). All other DDOs Send their 
26888>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DEOs the refresh message passing mode_find_or_clear_set.  
26888>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set: Used for DEOs attached to DDOs which have Found and/or cleared records.  
26888>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear_All:         Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that participated in a clear_all operation.  
26888>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Delete:            Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that performed a successful deletion. 
26888>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DDOs that were merely updated as the result of a deletion Use Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set.  
26888>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Save:              Used for DEOs attached to any DDO involved in a successful Save operation. 
26888>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
26890>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMainFile
26890>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDDStatus
26890>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDDO
26890>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bActive bAppSynching bMainFound
26890>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bRowDisplay bInClearGrid bDataAware 
26890>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDBGridType
26890>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26890>>>>>>>>>        RowID riCurrentRowID riID
26890>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCurrentRowIndex
26890>>>>>>>>>        
26890>>>>>>>>>        Get Active_State to bActive
26891>>>>>>>>>        Get AppSynching to bAppSynching
26892>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26893>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDBGridType
26894>>>>>>>>>
26894>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware and bActive and not(bAppSynching)) Begin
26896>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadingServer to hoDDO                  // hoDDO cannot be 0 otherwise we would never receive Refresh!
26897>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDDO to iMainFile
26898>>>>>>>>>        
26898>>>>>>>>>            Get DDRefreshTableStatus iMainFile to eDDStatus
26899>>>>>>>>>            Move (eDDStatus <> ddrtsNone) to bMainFound     // True = a main dd find or constrained child dd find has occurred
26900>>>>>>>>>            Get pbNotifyingExternalDD to bRowDisplay                 // True = we are simply responding to a change of the current row ID on the client
26901>>>>>>>>>            
26901>>>>>>>>>            // Get the current row's row id
26901>>>>>>>>>            WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26902>>>>>>>>>            Move (DeserializeRowID(sCurrentRowID)) to riCurrentRowID
26903>>>>>>>>>            WebGet piCurrentRowIndex to iCurrentRowIndex
26904>>>>>>>>>        
26904>>>>>>>>>            // Handle the case where there is no selected row and we've done a save or delete on the main file.
26904>>>>>>>>>            // We don't know what to do in this case so we will refresh the grid. This could happen if the save
26904>>>>>>>>>            // is occuring from an external source (e.g., create a new record directly in the DD)
26904>>>>>>>>>            If (iCurrentRowIndex=-1 and (eMode = MODE_SAVE or eMode = MODE_DELETE) and bMainFound and (not(bRowDisplay))) Begin
26906>>>>>>>>>                Move MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET to eMode
26907>>>>>>>>>            End
26907>>>>>>>>>>
26907>>>>>>>>>
26907>>>>>>>>>            // If this is a clear on the grid's main file and it is not grid insert/append row, all we can do is clear and refresh the grid
26907>>>>>>>>>            Get pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
26908>>>>>>>>>            If (bInClearGrid) Begin
26910>>>>>>>>>                Move MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET to eMode
26911>>>>>>>>>            End
26911>>>>>>>>>>
26911>>>>>>>>>
26911>>>>>>>>>            If (eMode = MODE_CLEAR and bMainFound and sCurrentRowID <> "") Begin
26913>>>>>>>>>                //  HW: Added check for empty current row id which prevents recursive clearing with two grids on a single DD.
26913>>>>>>>>>                // special case with clear. If this comes from some other DEO (which is unusual)
26913>>>>>>>>>                // and the curent row has a record, then we need to insert a row for the
26913>>>>>>>>>                // cleared row.
26913>>>>>>>>>                If (not(bRowDisplay)) Begin
26915>>>>>>>>>                    Send AppendNewRow
26916>>>>>>>>>                End
26916>>>>>>>>>>
26916>>>>>>>>>                
26916>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26917>>>>>>>>>            End
26917>>>>>>>>>>
26917>>>>>>>>>            
26917>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_DELETE or eMode = MODE_SAVE or bRowDisplay or not(bMainFound)) Begin
26920>>>>>>>>>                // Perform necessary actions for Save or Delete of a Grid Row
26920>>>>>>>>>                If (hoDDO = OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin    // OPERATION_ORIGIN is the DDO that is the origin of the Save, Delete, find or clear
26922>>>>>>>>>                    // if a save notification and the save's DD is the same as the grid's
26922>>>>>>>>>                    // we are saving the main record and it may now be out of order
26922>>>>>>>>>                    If (eMode = MODE_SAVE) Begin
26924>>>>>>>>>                        WebSet pbUnOrdered to True
26925>>>>>>>>>                    End
26925>>>>>>>>>>
26925>>>>>>>>>                End
26925>>>>>>>>>>
26925>>>>>>>>>
26925>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26926>>>>>>>>>            End
26926>>>>>>>>>>
26926>>>>>>>>>            
26926>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_CLEAR_ALL) Begin
26929>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26930>>>>>>>>>                If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26932>>>>>>>>>                    Send ClearFilter
26933>>>>>>>>>                    Send EmptyGridRefresh
26934>>>>>>>>>                End
26934>>>>>>>>>>
26934>>>>>>>>>            End
26934>>>>>>>>>>
26934>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET) Begin
26937>>>>>>>>>                // If we got here then refresh the entire grid
26937>>>>>>>>>                Move (GetRowID(iMainFile)) to riID
26938>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26939>>>>>>>>>                If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26941>>>>>>>>>                    Send GridRefresh
26942>>>>>>>>>                End
26942>>>>>>>>>>
26942>>>>>>>>>                Send ReadByRowId of hoDDO iMainFile riID
26943>>>>>>>>>            End
26943>>>>>>>>>>
26943>>>>>>>>>        End
26943>>>>>>>>>>
26943>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26944>>>>>>>>>    
26944>>>>>>>>>    /*    Refresh event during intialization of FlexTron controls. Latches onto the current record buffer     which may not have been recently found.    */
26944>>>>>>>>>    Procedure InitialRefresh
26946>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bActive bAppSynching bDataAware
26946>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDBGridType iMainFile
26946>>>>>>>>>        Handle  hoDDO
26946>>>>>>>>>        RowID riID
26946>>>>>>>>>        
26946>>>>>>>>>        Get Active_State to bActive
26947>>>>>>>>>        Get AppSynching to bAppSynching
26948>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26949>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDBGridType
26950>>>>>>>>>
26950>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware and bActive and not(bAppSynching)) Begin
26952>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadingServer to hoDDO                  // hoDDO cannot be 0 otherwise we would never receive Refresh!
26953>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDDO to iMainFile
26954>>>>>>>>>            
26954>>>>>>>>>            // If we got here then refresh the entire grid
26954>>>>>>>>>            Move (GetRowID(iMainFile)) to riID
26955>>>>>>>>>            Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26956>>>>>>>>>            If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26958>>>>>>>>>                Send GridRefresh
26959>>>>>>>>>            End
26959>>>>>>>>>>
26959>>>>>>>>>            Send ReadByRowId of hoDDO iMainFile riID
26960>>>>>>>>>        End
26960>>>>>>>>>>
26960>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26961>>>>>>>>>    
26961>>>>>>>>>    
26961>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. See ClearSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
26961>>>>>>>>>    // returns True.
26961>>>>>>>>>    Function ClearSelectedRow Returns Boolean
26963>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
26964>>>>>>>>>    End_Function  
26965>>>>>>>>>    
26965>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. cWebList is read only. See SaveSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
26965>>>>>>>>>    Function SaveSelectedRow Returns Integer
26967>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sroSucceed
26968>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26969>>>>>>>>>    
26969>>>>>>>>>    // Delete Logic to delete the current row pointed to by psCurrentRowId.
26969>>>>>>>>>    // returns True if the delete was successful.
26969>>>>>>>>>    Function DeleteSelectedRow Returns Integer
26971>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
26971>>>>>>>>>        Handle hmVerify
26971>>>>>>>>>        RowID riCurrentRowID riTestRowID
26971>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26971>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iMainFile
26971>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering
26971>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataAware
26971>>>>>>>>>        Integer iReturn
26971>>>>>>>>>
26971>>>>>>>>>        WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26972>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26973>>>>>>>>>        
26973>>>>>>>>>        // db-aware handling
26973>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
26975>>>>>>>>>            Get Server to hoDD
26976>>>>>>>>>            If (hoDD <> 0) Begin
26978>>>>>>>>>                Move (DeserializeRowID(sCurrentRowID)) to riCurrentRowID
26979>>>>>>>>>                Get CurrentRowId of hoDD to riTestRowID
26980>>>>>>>>>                
26980>>>>>>>>>                If (not(IsSameRowID(riCurrentRowID, riTestRowID))) Begin
26982>>>>>>>>>                    Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Assert: Server DDO's current record does not match psCurrentRowId"
26983>>>>>>>>>>
26983>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return sroFail
26984>>>>>>>>>                End
26984>>>>>>>>>>
26984>>>>>>>>>                
26984>>>>>>>>>                // Verify that we are allowed to delete
26984>>>>>>>>>                If (Read_Only_State(hoDD) or not(pbAllowDeleteRow(Self)) or not(Can_Delete(hoDD))) Begin
26986>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return sroFail         // the view should not allow this to happen
26987>>>>>>>>>                End
26987>>>>>>>>>>
26987>>>>>>>>>            End
26987>>>>>>>>>>
26987>>>>>>>>>        End
26987>>>>>>>>>>
26987>>>>>>>>>        
26987>>>>>>>>>        Get Verify_Delete_msg to hmVerify
26988>>>>>>>>>        If (hmVerify) Begin
26990>>>>>>>>>            WebSet pbDeleteCallbackActive to True
26991>>>>>>>>>            Send VerifyRequest (RefProc(RequestDeleteCallBack)) (RefFunc(Verify_Delete_Msg))
26992>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return sroPending
26993>>>>>>>>>        End
26993>>>>>>>>>>
26993>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
26994>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestDeleteExec
26995>>>>>>>>>            // we actually don't know if this will work or not, since this finds another row. For now, we say success
26995>>>>>>>>>        End
26995>>>>>>>>>>
26995>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sroSucceed
26996>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26997>>>>>>>>>    
26997>>>>>>>>>    // This event is triggered by Request_Delete. It is intended to be implemented on grids having 
26997>>>>>>>>>    // pbDataAware set to false to process the delete. If the delete cannot be performed return 
26997>>>>>>>>>    // false to cancel the grid from removing the row from the display. Returning false when 
26997>>>>>>>>>    // pbDataAware is set to true will also cancel the delete from being sent to the DDO.
26997>>>>>>>>>    Function OnDeleteRow String sCurrentRowID Returns Boolean
26999>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
27000>>>>>>>>>    End_Function        
27001>>>>>>>>>
27001>>>>>>>>>    
27001>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestDeleteExec
27003>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27003>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
27003>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iMainFile
27003>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering
27003>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataAware bContinue
27003>>>>>>>>>
27003>>>>>>>>>        WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
27004>>>>>>>>>        Get OnDeleteRow sCurrentRowID to bContinue
27005>>>>>>>>>        
27005>>>>>>>>>        // db-aware
27005>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
27006>>>>>>>>>        
27006>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
27008>>>>>>>>>            If (bContinue) Begin
27010>>>>>>>>>                // Perform the db-aware delete
27010>>>>>>>>>                Get Server to hoDD
27011>>>>>>>>>                Send Request_Delete to hoDD       // Perform the delete
27012>>>>>>>>>                            
27012>>>>>>>>>                If (Err) Begin
27014>>>>>>>>>                    Procedure_Return
27015>>>>>>>>>                End
27015>>>>>>>>>>
27015>>>>>>>>>                
27015>>>>>>>>>                Send RemoveRow sCurrentRowID      // Tell the client to remove the deleted row.
27016>>>>>>>>>                
27016>>>>>>>>>                // Select the next logical row
27016>>>>>>>>>                Get IndexOrder to iOrdering
27017>>>>>>>>>                WebGet pbReverseOrdering to bReverseOrdering
27018>>>>>>>>>                Get Main_File of hoDD to iMainFile
27019>>>>>>>>>        
27019>>>>>>>>>                If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
27021>>>>>>>>>                    Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoDD LT iMainFile iOrdering 
27022>>>>>>>>>                End
27022>>>>>>>>>>
27022>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
27023>>>>>>>>>                    Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoDD GT iMainFile iOrdering 
27024>>>>>>>>>                End
27024>>>>>>>>>>
27024>>>>>>>>>                
27024>>>>>>>>>                Send Locate_Next of hoDD    // Try to find the row below the deleted row.
27025>>>>>>>>>                
27025>>>>>>>>>                If (not(Found)) Begin
27027>>>>>>>>>                    // If the row below the deleted row was not found then it means we deleted the
27027>>>>>>>>>                    // last row. Now we will try to load the new last row. If there are no remaining
27027>>>>>>>>>                    // rows in the dataset then the buffer will be automatically cleared (which is 
27027>>>>>>>>>                    // what we want)
27027>>>>>>>>>                    If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
27029>>>>>>>>>                        Send Request_Read of hoDD FIRST_RECORD iMainFile iOrdering
27030>>>>>>>>>                    End
27030>>>>>>>>>>
27030>>>>>>>>>                    Else Begin
27031>>>>>>>>>                        Send Request_Read of hoDD LAST_RECORD iMainFile iOrdering
27032>>>>>>>>>                    End
27032>>>>>>>>>>
27032>>>>>>>>>                End
27032>>>>>>>>>>
27032>>>>>>>>>                
27032>>>>>>>>>                If (Found) Begin
27034>>>>>>>>>                    Send Request_Assign of hoDD iMainFile
27035>>>>>>>>>                End
27035>>>>>>>>>>
27035>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
27036>>>>>>>>>                    Send ClearGrid
27037>>>>>>>>>                End
27037>>>>>>>>>>
27037>>>>>>>>>                
27037>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
27038>>>>>>>>>            End
27038>>>>>>>>>>
27038>>>>>>>>>        End 
27038>>>>>>>>>>
27038>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27039>>>>>>>>>            //  Non DB-Aware handling
27039>>>>>>>>>             If (bContinue) Begin
27041>>>>>>>>>                Send RemoveRow sCurrentRowID      // Tell the client to remove the deleted row.
27042>>>>>>>>>            End
27042>>>>>>>>>>
27042>>>>>>>>>        End
27042>>>>>>>>>>
27042>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27043>>>>>>>>>    
27043>>>>>>>>>    // Client action to remove the passed row from the cache. 
27043>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RemoveRow String sRowID
27045>>>>>>>>>        String[] aParams
27046>>>>>>>>>        
27046>>>>>>>>>        Move sRowID to aParams[0]
27047>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientAction "removeRow" aParams    
27048>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27049>>>>>>>>>
27049>>>>>>>>>    // Returns true if you can move off of the selected row.
27049>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. cWebList is read only. See AllowChangeSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
27049>>>>>>>>>    Function AllowChangeSelectedRow String sGotoRow String sToRowID Returns Boolean
27051>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
27052>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27053>>>>>>>>>
27053>>>>>>>>>    // these don't do anything with lists
27053>>>>>>>>>    Procedure AppendNewRow    
27055>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27056>>>>>>>>>
27056>>>>>>>>>    // these don't do anything with lists
27056>>>>>>>>>    Procedure InsertNewRow    
27058>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27059>>>>>>>>>    
27059>>>>>>>>>    Function IndexOrder Returns Integer
27061>>>>>>>>>        // returns the sort order for subsequent DDO Request_Read calls.
27061>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iColumnOrdering eDbGridType iConstrainFile
27061>>>>>>>>>        String iSortColumn
27061>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoColumn hoDD
27061>>>>>>>>>        
27061>>>>>>>>>        
27061>>>>>>>>>        
27061>>>>>>>>>        // if DD has an ordering we must use this
27061>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27062>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD > 0) Begin
27064>>>>>>>>>            Get Ordering of hoDD to iOrdering    // get the sort index from the DDO (if this has been set)
27065>>>>>>>>>            If (iOrdering<>-1) Begin
27067>>>>>>>>>                Function_Return iOrdering
27068>>>>>>>>>            End
27068>>>>>>>>>>
27068>>>>>>>>>        End
27068>>>>>>>>>>
27068>>>>>>>>>            
27068>>>>>>>>>        Get piOrdering to iOrdering
27069>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD > 0) Begin
27071>>>>>>>>>            // this is the ordering as defined by the grid
27071>>>>>>>>>            Get Constrain_File of hoDD to iConstrainFile
27072>>>>>>>>>            // if ordering is not specified and we have a constraining parent
27072>>>>>>>>>            // we want to limit the constraint to the best choice for a constrained find
27072>>>>>>>>>            If (iOrdering=-1 and iConstrainFile) Begin
27074>>>>>>>>>                Get ConstrainedIndexOrder iConstrainFile to iOrdering
27075>>>>>>>>>            End
27075>>>>>>>>>>
27075>>>>>>>>>        End
27075>>>>>>>>>>
27075>>>>>>>>>        // if a static grid, use the grid's ordering, if dynamic we use
27075>>>>>>>>>        // the column ordering if we are sorting by a grid column, else use grid ordering
27075>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDbGridType
27076>>>>>>>>>        If (eDbGridType=gtAutomatic) Begin
27078>>>>>>>>>            // If we are sorting by a grid column then use that
27078>>>>>>>>>            WebGet piSortColumn to iSortColumn
27079>>>>>>>>>            
27079>>>>>>>>>            If (iSortColumn <> -1) Begin
27081>>>>>>>>>                Get GetColumnObject iSortColumn to hoColumn
27082>>>>>>>>>                If (hoColumn) Begin
27084>>>>>>>>>                    Get ColumnIndexOrder of hoColumn to iColumnOrdering      // returns -1 if there is no default index
27085>>>>>>>>>                    If (iColumnOrdering<>-1) Begin
27087>>>>>>>>>                        Move iColumnOrdering to iOrdering
27088>>>>>>>>>                    End
27088>>>>>>>>>>
27088>>>>>>>>>                End
27088>>>>>>>>>>
27088>>>>>>>>>            End
27088>>>>>>>>>>
27088>>>>>>>>>        End
27088>>>>>>>>>>
27088>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iOrdering
27089>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27090>>>>>>>>>    
27090>>>>>>>>>    
27090>>>>>>>>>    // return best index for constrained find. Return -1 which asks the runtime
27090>>>>>>>>>    // to make this choice as normally there is only one choice. 
27090>>>>>>>>>    // This is suitable for augmentation.
27090>>>>>>>>>    Function ConstrainedIndexOrder Integer iConstrainFile Returns Integer
27092>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return -1 // the runtime knows best
27093>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27094>>>>>>>>>    
27094>>>>>>>>>    
27094>>>>>>>>>    Procedure UpdateCurrentRowID
27096>>>>>>>>>        // Sets the web property psCurrentRowId for pbDataAware=True grid.
27096>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27096>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRowID
27096>>>>>>>>>        
27096>>>>>>>>>        // assert pbDataAware=True
27096>>>>>>>>>        If (not(pbDataAware(Self))) Begin
27098>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Assert: UpdateCurrentRowID called for non-data aware grid"
27099>>>>>>>>>>
27099>>>>>>>>>        End
27099>>>>>>>>>>
27099>>>>>>>>>        
27099>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27100>>>>>>>>>        
27100>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD = 0) Begin
27102>>>>>>>>>            // This will probably never happen
27102>>>>>>>>>            Move (NullRowID()) to riRowID
27103>>>>>>>>>        End
27103>>>>>>>>>>
27103>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27104>>>>>>>>>            Get CurrentRowId of hoDD to riRowID
27105>>>>>>>>>        End
27105>>>>>>>>>>
27105>>>>>>>>>        
27105>>>>>>>>>        WebSet psCurrentRowId to (SerializeRowID(riRowID))
27106>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27107>>>>>>>>>
27107>>>>>>>>>
27107>>>>>>>>>    // in sub-classes that support auto-server, which uses the
27107>>>>>>>>>    // invoking server, the server used for reading the grid may
27107>>>>>>>>>    // be different than the server defined in this view.
27107>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadingServer Returns Handle
27109>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27109>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27110>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoDD
27111>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27112>>>>>>>>>
27112>>>>>>>>>    // This handles translation of find modes to make reverse ordering
27112>>>>>>>>>    // work. Pass the mode and return the mode, translated if reverse ordering is needed
27112>>>>>>>>>    Function FindMode Integer eFindMode Boolean bReverseOrdering Returns Integer
27114>>>>>>>>>        If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
27116>>>>>>>>>            Case Begin
27116>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=GE) ;                    Move (LE) to eFindMode
27119>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=GT) ;                    Move (LT) to eFindMode
27123>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LT) ;                    Move (GT) to eFindMode
27127>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LE) ;                    Move (GE) to eFindMode
27131>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=FIRST_RECORD) ;                    Move (LAST_RECORD) to eFindMode
27135>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LAST_RECORD) ;                    Move (FIRST_RECORD) to eFindMode
27139>>>>>>>>>            Case End
27139>>>>>>>>>        End
27139>>>>>>>>>>
27139>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return eFindMode
27140>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27141>>>>>>>>>
27141>>>>>>>>>    Procedure EstablishDDFindMode Integer eFindMode Handle hoServer Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering
27143>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
27143>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode eFindMode bReverseOrdering to eFindMode  // mode might change if reverse ordering
27144>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoServer to iFile
27145>>>>>>>>>        Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoServer eFindMode iFile iOrdering
27146>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27147>>>>>>>>>
27147>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDFirstRecord Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering  Returns RowID
27149>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile eFindMode
27149>>>>>>>>>        // because this uses request_read it cannot be used inside of refresh
27149>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE<>0) Begin
27151>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM ("assertion failed: ReadDDFirstRecord is called when DD is busy")
27152>>>>>>>>>>
27152>>>>>>>>>        End
27152>>>>>>>>>>
27152>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27153>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode FIRST_RECORD bReverseOrdering to eFindMode
27154>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Read of hoDD eFindMode iFile  iOrdering
27155>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (GetRowID(iFile))
27156>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27157>>>>>>>>>    
27157>>>>>>>>>    
27157>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDLastRecord Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering  Returns RowID
27159>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile eFindMode
27159>>>>>>>>>        // because this uses request_read it cannot be used inside of refresh
27159>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE<>0) Begin
27161>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM ("assertion failed: ReadDDFirstRecord is called when DD is busy")
27162>>>>>>>>>>
27162>>>>>>>>>        End
27162>>>>>>>>>>
27162>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27163>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode LAST_RECORD bReverseOrdering to eFindMode
27164>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Read of hoDD eFindMode iFile iOrdering
27165>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (GetRowID(iFile))
27166>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27167>>>>>>>>>    
27167>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDRecordInBuffer Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering Returns Boolean
27169>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bFound
27169>>>>>>>>>        RowID riId
27169>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
27169>>>>>>>>>        
27169>>>>>>>>>        Send EstablishDDFindMode Ge  hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering
27170>>>>>>>>>        Send Locate_Next of hoDD
27171>>>>>>>>>        Move (Found) to bFound
27172>>>>>>>>>        If not bFound Begin
27174>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadDDLastRecord hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to riId
27175>>>>>>>>>        End
27175>>>>>>>>>>
27175>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27176>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27177>>>>>>>>>            Move (GetRowID(iFile)) to riId
27178>>>>>>>>>        End
27178>>>>>>>>>>
27178>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (not(IsNullRowID(riId)))
27179>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27180>>>>>>>>>
27180>>>>>>>>>    // finds the record in the buffer and rebuilds the list. If the
27180>>>>>>>>>    // buffer record is not found, most likely due to a failed constraint), it
27180>>>>>>>>>    // search for the next record (where next is determined by reverse ordering).
27180>>>>>>>>>    // If there is no record, it will attemot to find the prior record. 
27180>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FindDDRecordInBuffer 
27182>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering bFound
27182>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering
27182>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27182>>>>>>>>>
27182>>>>>>>>>        Get ReadingServer to hoDD
27183>>>>>>>>>        Get IndexOrder to iOrdering
27184>>>>>>>>>        WebGet pbReverseOrdering to bReverseOrdering
27185>>>>>>>>>        
27185>>>>>>>>>        Get ReadDDRecordInBuffer hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to bFound
27186>>>>>>>>>        
27186>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27187>>>>>>>>>        If bFound Begin
27189>>>>>>>>>            Send Request_Assign of hoDD
27190>>>>>>>>>        End
27190>>>>>>>>>>
27190>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27191>>>>>>>>>            Send ClearGrid
27192>>>>>>>>>        End
27192>>>>>>>>>>
27192>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27193>>>>>>>>>    
27193>>>>>>>>>    
27193>>>>>>>>>    // Clears the DD and creates an empty grid.
27193>>>>>>>>>    // The Clear DD behavior can work different ways with grids. Most of the time, a clear to a DD should
27193>>>>>>>>>    // just open up a new row for editing. This is consistent with what clear does everyhwere else. However, there are
27193>>>>>>>>>    // times when you need to create an empty grid. This will mostly happen when there are no valid records to display so you
27193>>>>>>>>>    // need to create an empty grid. That's what this message is for.
27193>>>>>>>>>    // For now this is public, but it needs to be used carefully. If you are clearing grids when there are records that could be
27193>>>>>>>>>    // displayed, you are fighting a normal grid behavior.
27193>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ClearGrid
27195>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bInClearGrid bDataAware
27195>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27195>>>>>>>>>        
27195>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
27196>>>>>>>>>        
27196>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
27198>>>>>>>>>            Get pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
27199>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInClearGrid to True
27200>>>>>>>>>            Get Server to hoDD
27201>>>>>>>>>            Send Clear of hoDD
27202>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
27203>>>>>>>>>        End
27203>>>>>>>>>>
27203>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27204>>>>>>>>>            Send EmptyGridRefresh
27205>>>>>>>>>        End
27205>>>>>>>>>>
27205>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27206>>>>>>>>>    
27206>>>>>>>>>    
27206>>>>>>>>>    // Appends a row to the end of the list. It will update the user interface if needed. Should
27206>>>>>>>>>    // only be used on a manually loaded list (pbDataAware = false or peDbGridType = gtManual). 
27206>>>>>>>>>    // Implemented as a client-action meaning that it works asynchronously.
27206>>>>>>>>>    //
27206>>>>>>>>>    // Params:
27206>>>>>>>>>    //  tRow    Filled tWebRow struct with the new row data.
27206>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DataSetAppendRow tWebRow tRow
27208>>>>>>>>>        String[] aParams
27209>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aRows
27209>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aRows
27210>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoJson
27210>>>>>>>>>        
27210>>>>>>>>>        Move tRow to aRows[0]
27211>>>>>>>>>        
27211>>>>>>>>>        //  Convert data to JSON
27211>>>>>>>>>        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJson
27212>>>>>>>>>        Send DataTypeToJson of hoJson aRows
27213>>>>>>>>>        
27213>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientActionEx "dataSetAppendRow" aParams hoJson
27214>>>>>>>>>        Send Destroy of hoJson
27215>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
