31466>>>>>>>>>    // This is the Error_Report for non AJAX style applications. This could be 
31466>>>>>>>>>    // Web Service, HTTP Handler, ASP or old style webapps. We've copied it here
31466>>>>>>>>>    // rather than trying to integrate it directly into Error_Report. It gets called by
31466>>>>>>>>>    // Error_Report as needed.
31466>>>>>>>>>    Procedure BasicErrorReport Integer iError Integer iLine String ErrMsg
31468>>>>>>>>>        String sSystemErr sMess sLabel sFile sDtl sFullError
31468>>>>>>>>>        String sStack sSystemAndStack
31468>>>>>>>>>        Integer iErrFile iErrField
31468>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bCritical bQueueErrors bLogAllErrors bLocal bHtmlErrors
31468>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoInetSession
31468>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bUnhandledSupport
31468>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDebugging bTrapped
31468>>>>>>>>>        Integer iSrc iTxtlen
31468>>>>>>>>>        String sCaption
31468>>>>>>>>>
31468>>>>>>>>>        
31468>>>>>>>>>        Get phoInetSession to hoInetSession // this may or may not be set yet.
31469>>>>>>>>>        
31469>>>>>>>>>        Get IsCritical iError to bCritical
31470>>>>>>>>>        Get pbUnhandledErrorSupport to bUnhandledSupport
31471>>>>>>>>>        Move (IsDebuggerPresent()) to bDebugging
31472>>>>>>>>>        
31472>>>>>>>>>        // if an operator error this may be a Procedure UserError situation where the
31472>>>>>>>>>        // caption is passed in the error text. This handler does not support setting the caption so we just remove it.
31472>>>>>>>>>        // The ajax superclass handler will support this
31472>>>>>>>>>        If (iError=DFERR_OPERATOR) Begin
31474>>>>>>>>>            Move (pos(C_ErrorCaption,ErrMsg)) to iSrc
31475>>>>>>>>>            If iSrc Begin
31477>>>>>>>>>                Move (length(C_ErrorCaption)) to  iTxtLen
31478>>>>>>>>>                Move (remove(ErrMsg, 1, iSrc-1 + iTxtLen )) to sCaption // will not get used here
31479>>>>>>>>>                Move (Left(ErrMsg,iSrc-1)) to ErrMsg
31480>>>>>>>>>            End
31480>>>>>>>>>>
31480>>>>>>>>>        End
31480>>>>>>>>>>
31480>>>>>>>>>        
31480>>>>>>>>>        Get Error_Description iError ErrMsg  to sSystemErr
31481>>>>>>>>>        
31481>>>>>>>>>        // if the error source is identified we can get extended error
31481>>>>>>>>>        // text for our error message. This capability is a standard part
31481>>>>>>>>>        // of VDF5
31481>>>>>>>>>        If ghoErrorSource Begin
31483>>>>>>>>>            // These messages were just added to the DD.
31483>>>>>>>>>            Get Extended_Error_file   of ghoErrorSource to iErrFile
31484>>>>>>>>>            Get Extended_Error_Field  of ghoErrorSource to iErrField
31485>>>>>>>>>            // we are making the assumption that ghoErrorSource is a DD object
31485>>>>>>>>>            // If it is not, we will have problems.....but it will be!
31485>>>>>>>>>            If (iErrFile>0) Begin
31487>>>>>>>>>                Get_Attribute DF_FILE_DISPLAY_NAME of iErrFile to sFile
31490>>>>>>>>>                If (iErrField>0) Begin
31492>>>>>>>>>                    Get File_Field_Label of ghoErrorSource iErrFile iErrField DD_LABEL_LONG to sLabel
31493>>>>>>>>>                    Move (SFormat(C_$FieldInDataFile,sLabel, sFile)) to sMess
31494>>>>>>>>>                End
31494>>>>>>>>>>
31494>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
31495>>>>>>>>>                    Move (SFormat(C_$InDataFile,sFile)) to sMess
31496>>>>>>>>>                End
31496>>>>>>>>>>
31496>>>>>>>>>                Append sSystemErr "\n" sMess
31498>>>>>>>>>            End
31498>>>>>>>>>>
31498>>>>>>>>>        End
31498>>>>>>>>>>
31498>>>>>>>>>        
31498>>>>>>>>>        Move (SFormat(C_$VDFErrorInLine, iError, iLine)) to sDtl
31499>>>>>>>>>        If (iErrFile  > 0) ;            Move (sDtl * DD_FILE_TEXT  * String(iErrFile))  to sDtl
31502>>>>>>>>>        If (iErrField > 0) ;            Move (sDtl * DD_FIELD_TEXT * String(iErrField)) to sDtl
31505>>>>>>>>>        // full error is systemError + Error and line numbers
31505>>>>>>>>>        Move (sSystemErr + "\n" + sDtl) to sFullError
31506>>>>>>>>>        
31506>>>>>>>>>        // If 0, the COM object is not yet ready to be used. If an error occurs in this
31506>>>>>>>>>        // condition, we consider this error to always be fatal and will notify WebApp
31506>>>>>>>>>        // Server of this error via WebAppFatalError command
31506>>>>>>>>>        If (hoInetSession=0) Begin
31508>>>>>>>>>            
31508>>>>>>>>>            If bDebugging Begin
31510>>>>>>>>>                Send UnhandledErrorDisplay iLine sFullError
31511>>>>>>>>>            End
31511>>>>>>>>>>
31511>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
31512>>>>>>>>>                CallStackDump sStack
31513>>>>>>>>>                WebAppFatalError (Replaces("\n", (sFullError + "\n\n" + sStack) , character(13)+character(10)))
31514>>>>>>>>>                // we only arrive here if WebApp cannot handle the error. All we can
31514>>>>>>>>>                // do is abort.
31514>>>>>>>>>                //Send MessageBoxError sFullError 1 // might be useful for VDF debugging, but cannot be used on server
31514>>>>>>>>>            End
31514>>>>>>>>>>
31514>>>>>>>>>            Abort
31515>>>>>>>>>>
31515>>>>>>>>>        End
31515>>>>>>>>>>
31515>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
31516>>>>>>>>>            
31516>>>>>>>>>            Get pbAllErrorstoLocal    of hoInetSession to bLocal
31517>>>>>>>>>            Get pbQueueErrors         of hoInetSession to bQueueErrors
31518>>>>>>>>>            Get pbAllErrorstoEventLog of hoInetSession to bLogAllErrors
31519>>>>>>>>>            Get pbAllErrorsToHtml     of hoInetSession to bHtmlErrors
31520>>>>>>>>>            
31520>>>>>>>>>            // If error is critical, we cannot go on.
31520>>>>>>>>>            If bCritical Begin
31522>>>>>>>>>                CallStackDump sStack
31523>>>>>>>>>                Move (Replaces(Character(13)+Character(10),sStack, "\n")) to sStack
31524>>>>>>>>>                Move (sSystemErr + "\n\n" + sStack) to sSystemAndStack
31525>>>>>>>>>                Send ReportCriticalError to hoInetSession iError (If(bUnhandledSupport, sSystemAndStack, sSystemErr)) iLine iErrFile iErrField
31526>>>>>>>>>                
31526>>>>>>>>>                // also attempt to send message to client (html browser)
31526>>>>>>>>>                If bHtmlErrors Begin
31528>>>>>>>>>                    // The option to disable stack dumps only makes sense if the developer is using html errors to report unhandled problems
31528>>>>>>>>>                    // and for some reason the stack dump will mess up existing applications. This seems very unlikely but we are providing
31528>>>>>>>>>                    // a way to disable this if needed via pbUnhandledSupport.
31528>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReportError to hoInetSession iError (If(bUnhandledSupport, sSystemAndStack, sSystemErr)) iLine iErrFile iErrField
31529>>>>>>>>>                End
31529>>>>>>>>>>
31529>>>>>>>>>                
31529>>>>>>>>>                // if we are passing errors to VDF console, report the error
31529>>>>>>>>>                // if we we debugging, thereis no point in doing this
31529>>>>>>>>>                If (not(bDebugging) and bLocal) Begin
31531>>>>>>>>>                    Send MessageBoxError (sFullError + "\n\n" + sStack) // 1 means critical
31532>>>>>>>>>                End
31532>>>>>>>>>>
31532>>>>>>>>>                
31532>>>>>>>>>                // log the critical error to the event log
31532>>>>>>>>>                // if debugging, this can be an unhandled error
31532>>>>>>>>>                If bDebugging Begin
31534>>>>>>>>>                    Send UnhandledErrorDisplay iLine sFullError
31535>>>>>>>>>                End
31535>>>>>>>>>>
31535>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
31536>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReportErrorEvent to hoInetSession iError sSystemAndStack  iLine iErrFile iErrField
31537>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReportErrorEvent to hoInetSession iError C_$CriticalErrorProgramHalted iLine 0 0
31538>>>>>>>>>                End
31538>>>>>>>>>>
31538>>>>>>>>>                // and end it all
31538>>>>>>>>>                Abort
31539>>>>>>>>>>
31539>>>>>>>>>            End
31539>>>>>>>>>>
31539>>>>>>>>>            
31539>>>>>>>>>            // if we are passing errors to VDF console, report the error
31539>>>>>>>>>            If bLocal Begin
31541>>>>>>>>>                Send MessageBoxError sFullError 0 // 0 means non-critical
31542>>>>>>>>>            End
31542>>>>>>>>>>
31542>>>>>>>>>            
31542>>>>>>>>>            // we make the following assumptions:
31542>>>>>>>>>            // If errors are queue
31542>>>>>>>>>            //    We assume the error is expected, and controlled
31542>>>>>>>>>            //    Write error to queue
31542>>>>>>>>>            //    Ddo not write to Event Log unless we are logging all errors.
31542>>>>>>>>>            //
31542>>>>>>>>>            // if errors are not queued
31542>>>>>>>>>            //    We assume the error is unexpected, and must be controlled
31542>>>>>>>>>            //    Display HTML error to browser unless this is disabled
31542>>>>>>>>>            //    Send to the event log (under the assumption that the error is unexpected).
31542>>>>>>>>>            CallStackDump sStack
31543>>>>>>>>>            Move (Replaces(Character(13)+Character(10),sStack, "\n")) to sStack
31544>>>>>>>>>            Move (sSystemErr + "\n\n" + sStack) to sSystemAndStack
31545>>>>>>>>>                
31545>>>>>>>>>            If bQueueErrors Begin
31547>>>>>>>>>                Send Set_Error iError sSystemErr sFullError iLine iErrFile iErrField
31548>>>>>>>>>                If bLogAllErrors Begin
31550>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReportErrorEvent to hoInetSession iError sSystemAndStack iLine iErrFile iErrField
31551>>>>>>>>>                End
31551>>>>>>>>>>
31551>>>>>>>>>            End
31551>>>>>>>>>>
31551>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
31552>>>>>>>>>                If bHtmlErrors Begin
31554>>>>>>>>>                    // The option to disable stack dumps only makes sense if the developer is using html errors to report unhandled problems
31554>>>>>>>>>                    // and for some reason the stack dump will mess up existing applications. This seems very unlikely but we are providing
31554>>>>>>>>>                    // a way to disable this if needed via pbUnhandledSupport.
31554>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReportError to hoInetSession iError (If(bUnhandledSupport, sSystemAndStack, sSystemErr)) iLine iErrFile iErrField
31555>>>>>>>>>                End
31555>>>>>>>>>>
31555>>>>>>>>>                If bDebugging  Begin
31557>>>>>>>>>                    Send UnhandledErrorDisplay iLine sFullError
31558>>>>>>>>>                End
31558>>>>>>>>>>
31558>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
31559>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReportErrorEvent to hoInetSession iError sSystemAndStack iLine iErrFile iErrField
31560>>>>>>>>>                End
31560>>>>>>>>>>
31560>>>>>>>>>            End
31560>>>>>>>>>>
31560>>>>>>>>>        End
31560>>>>>>>>>>
31560>>>>>>>>>        
31560>>>>>>>>>        
31560>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
31561>>>>>>>>>
31561>>>>>>>>>    //  Is called by df on errors. It searches additional information and
31561>>>>>>>>>    //  saves the error. The main part of this is the error handler for AJAX framework
31561>>>>>>>>>    // applications If a basic or a legacy webapp, this Error is "forwarded" to BasicErrorReport.
31561>>>>>>>>>    //
31561>>>>>>>>>    Procedure HandleError Integer iErrNum Integer iErrLine String sErrText
31563>>>>>>>>>        String sSystemErr  sCaption  sExtErr
31563>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bUserError bDisplayControl
31563>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOldAllErrorsToHtml bAllErrorstoEventLog bInRecording bTrapped
31563>>>>>>>>>        Integer iErrFile iErrField iSrc iTxtlen
31563>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoCurrentView hoTargetControl hoInetSession
31563>>>>>>>>>        
31563>>>>>>>>>                
31563>>>>>>>>>        Get phoInetSession to hoInetSession
31564>>>>>>>>>        Get pbInErrorRecording to bInRecording
31565>>>>>>>>>        
31565>>>>>>>>>        // This means is not happening during an AJAX style Request or it means that this is an
31565>>>>>>>>>        // old webapp style error. If hoInetSession is 0, it is fatal
31565>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bInRecording)) Begin
31567>>>>>>>>>            Send BasicErrorReport iErrNum iErrLine sErrText
31568>>>>>>>>>        End
31568>>>>>>>>>>
31568>>>>>>>>>        Else If (hoInetSession=0) Begin
31571>>>>>>>>>            // this should not be possible at this point.
31571>>>>>>>>>            // If it is, it's fatal and program will abort
31571>>>>>>>>>            Send BasicErrorReport iErrNum iErrLine sErrText
31572>>>>>>>>>            // will abort
31572>>>>>>>>>        End
31572>>>>>>>>>>
31572>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
31573>>>>>>>>>            
31573>>>>>>>>>            // process an error that occurs during an AJAX Server request
31573>>>>>>>>>            
31573>>>>>>>>>            Move False to bDisplayControl
31574>>>>>>>>>            
31574>>>>>>>>>            // the caption normally used for handled user errors
31574>>>>>>>>>            Get psUserErrorCaption to sCaption
31575>>>>>>>>>            // if an operator error this may be a Procedure UserError situation where the
31575>>>>>>>>>            // caption is passed in the error text. If so, get the caption
31575>>>>>>>>>            If (iErrNum=DFERR_OPERATOR) Begin
31577>>>>>>>>>                Move (pos(C_ErrorCaption,sErrText)) to iSrc
31578>>>>>>>>>                If iSrc Begin
31580>>>>>>>>>                    Move (length(C_ErrorCaption)) to  iTxtLen
31581>>>>>>>>>                    Move (remove(sErrText, 1, iSrc-1 + iTxtLen )) to sCaption
31582>>>>>>>>>                    Move (Left(sErrText,iSrc-1)) to sErrText
31583>>>>>>>>>                End
31583>>>>>>>>>>
31583>>>>>>>>>            End
31583>>>>>>>>>>
31583>>>>>>>>>            
31583>>>>>>>>>            // Get the message....
31583>>>>>>>>>            Get Error_Description iErrNum sErrText to sSystemErr
31584>>>>>>>>>            
31584>>>>>>>>>            // Get file and field (of data dictionary error) if available
31584>>>>>>>>>            // and use this to determine the target control by searching
31584>>>>>>>>>            // for the first control with the same data binding....
31584>>>>>>>>>            If (ghoErrorSource <> 0) Begin
31586>>>>>>>>>                Get Extended_Error_file  of ghoErrorSource to iErrFile
31587>>>>>>>>>                Get Extended_Error_Field of ghoErrorSource to iErrField
31588>>>>>>>>>                
31588>>>>>>>>>                If (iErrFile > 0) Begin
31590>>>>>>>>>                    Get DetermineCurrentView to hoCurrentView
31591>>>>>>>>>                    Move False to bDisplayControl
31592>>>>>>>>>                    If (iErrField > 0 and hoCurrentView <> C_WebUnresolvedObject) Begin
31594>>>>>>>>>                        Get FirstControlWithDataBinding of hoCurrentView iErrFile iErrField to hoTargetControl
31595>>>>>>>>>                        
31595>>>>>>>>>                        If (hoTargetControl <> C_WebUnresolvedObject) Begin
31597>>>>>>>>>                            //  Try to display local error balloon
31597>>>>>>>>>                            Get ShowControlError of hoTargetControl iErrNum sSystemErr to bDisplayControl
31598>>>>>>>>>                        End
31598>>>>>>>>>>
31598>>>>>>>>>                    End
31598>>>>>>>>>>
31598>>>>>>>>>                    //  If no control found (or capable of showing errors) then we extend the error message with file and field name
31598>>>>>>>>>                    If (not(bDisplayControl)) Begin
31600>>>>>>>>>                        Get Extended_Error_Message of ghoErrorSource to sExtErr
31601>>>>>>>>>                        Move (sErrText + "\n" + sExtErr) to sErrText
31602>>>>>>>>>                        Move (sSystemErr + "\n" + sExtErr) to sSystemErr
31603>>>>>>>>>                        Move (Replaces("\n",sSystemErr,"\n\r")) to sSystemErr
31604>>>>>>>>>                    End
31604>>>>>>>>>>
31604>>>>>>>>>                End
31604>>>>>>>>>>
31604>>>>>>>>>            End
31604>>>>>>>>>>
31604>>>>>>>>>            
31604>>>>>>>>>            // Test if this is a user error or an unhandled error (i.e. "find past end of file")....
31604>>>>>>>>>            Get IsUserError iErrNum to bUserError
31605>>>>>>>>>            If not bUserError Begin
31607>>>>>>>>>                Get psUnhandledErrorCaption to sCaption
31608>>>>>>>>>            End
31608>>>>>>>>>>
31608>>>>>>>>>            
31608>>>>>>>>>            //  Forward the error to the webapp object (if not already handled by the contorl)
31608>>>>>>>>>            If (phoWebHost(Self) > 0) Begin
31610>>>>>>>>>                If (not(bDisplayControl)) Begin
31612>>>>>>>>>                    Send ShowError of (phoWebHost(Self)) iErrNum iErrLine sSystemErr sCaption bUserError
31613>>>>>>>>>                End
31613>>>>>>>>>>
31613>>>>>>>>>            End
31613>>>>>>>>>>
31613>>>>>>>>>            Get pbAllErrorstoEventLog of hoInetSession to bAllErrorstoEventLog
31614>>>>>>>>>            If (not(bUserError) or bAllErrorstoEventLog) Begin
31616>>>>>>>>>                Send BasicErrorReport iErrNum iErrLine sErrText
31617>>>>>>>>>            End
31617>>>>>>>>>>
31617>>>>>>>>>        End
31617>>>>>>>>>>
31617>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
31618>>>>>>>>>    
31618>>>>>>>>>    // FinishRecording:
31618>>>>>>>>>    
31618>>>>>>>>>    // Stops fetching the error by resetting the origional error handler.
31618>>>>>>>>>    //
31618>>>>>>>>>    // Returns - Array with error structs of occurred errors
31618>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FinishRecording
31620>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bInErrorRecording
31620>>>>>>>>>        Get pbInErrorRecording to bInErrorRecording
31621>>>>>>>>>        If bInErrorRecording Begin
31623>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInErrorRecording to False
31624>>>>>>>>>        End
31624>>>>>>>>>>
31624>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
31625>>>>>>>>>    
31625>>>>>>>>>    
31625>>>>>>>>>    // Starts fetching the errors by setting this object as the error handler
31625>>>>>>>>>    // and clearing the error array.
31625>>>>>>>>>    Procedure StartRecording Handle hoHost
31627>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bInErrorRecording
31627>>>>>>>>>        
31627>>>>>>>>>        Get pbInErrorRecording to bInErrorRecording
31628>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bInErrorRecording)) Begin
31630>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInErrorRecording to True
31631>>>>>>>>>        End
31631>>>>>>>>>>
31631>>>>>>>>>        
31631>>>>>>>>>        Set phoWebHost to hoHost
31632>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
